<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=2 -->
I. Background on the Indiana Program
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=2 -->
On July 29, 1982, the Secretary of the Interior conditionally approved the Indiana program. Background information
on the Indiana program, including the Secretary's findings, the disposition of comments, and the conditions of approval
can be found in the July 26, 1982, 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (47 FR 32071). Subsequent actions concerning the conditions of approval and program amendments can be found at 30
CFR 914.10, 914.15, and 914.16.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
II. Discussion of the Proposed Amendment
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
By letter dated October 1, 1993, (Administrative Record No. IND&hyph;1325) Indiana submitted a proposed amendment
to its program pursuant to SMCRA. The amendment consists of statute changes made by the Indiana General Assembly and
contained in the 1993 SEA 179. SEA 179 contains numerous amendments to Indiana statutes, but only those which pertain
to the Indiana program are discussed below.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=83 g=1 f=1 -->
IC 13&hyph;4.1&hyph;4&blank;Permit Approval or Denial
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Indiana has amended subsection IC 13&hyph;4.1&hyph;4&hyph;3(a) concerning the findings required to be made by
the director of the Indiana Department of Natural Resources (IDNR) prior to issuing a permit. New subdivision 3(a)(10)
is added to provide as follows:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
(10) if any part of the operation would take place in a floodway (as defined in IC 13&hyph;2&hyph;22&hyph;3), the operation
will not:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) result in unreasonably detrimental effects upon the fish, wildlife, or botanical resources;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) adversely affect the efficiency; or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) unduly restrict the capacity of the floodway.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In its submittal of this amendment, Indiana explained that the proposed language quoted above is being added to the
Indiana program as a consequence of an amendment to IC 13&hyph;2&hyph;22&hyph;13. New subdivision 13(c)(3) is added
to IC 13&hyph;2&hyph;22&hyph;13 to provide that operations conducted under IC 13&hyph;4.1 (Indiana SMCRA) are
exempted from the need for a ``construction in a floodway'' permit issued by the IDNR, Division of Water. Instead,
any activity in a floodway which is to be conducted as part of an operation regulated under IC 13&hyph;4.1 must be identified
in the permit application to the Division of Reclamation. A determination must then be made by the Division of Reclamation
that the environmental standards identified in the proposed language are met. This determination will then become
part of the ``Findings Document'' which accompanies each of the Division's final permit recommendation.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->
</SUPPLEM>
<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
