<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00053 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
b.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
 Description of plan.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
On November 12, 1993, the SCAQMD adopted its Rate-of-Progress 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Plan, following reasonable notice and public hearing. CARB 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submitted the Rate-of-Progress plan as a proposed SIP revision on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
November 15, 1993. The submitted plan shows a 1990 base year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions inventory of 1683 tons per day of reactive organic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compounds (ROC), an adjusted 1990 inventory of 1450 tons per day 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(after subtracting FMVCP and RVP reductions of 233), resulting in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a 1996 target emissions reductions of 217.5 tons per day. After 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
credit for fully adopted State and local measures and taking into 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
account growth in emissions through 1996, the plan achieves almost 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all of the reductions needed to meet the target. The plan 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
addresses the small remaining shortfall by commitments to adopt 9 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
SCAQMD measures in 1994, one SCAQMD measure in 1995, and one CARB 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measure: the enhanced I/M program. Even after applying an 80 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
percent rule effectiveness discount (in accordance with EPA's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
policy), the proposed SCAMQD measures alone would eliminate the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shortfall, without the need to count credits assigned to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
enhanced I/M program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Under section 110(k)(4) of the Act, EPA has the authority to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditionally approve the South Coast plan based upon the State's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
commitment to adopt these measures. However, EPA's current policy 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
does not allow approval of rate-of-progress plans if they depend 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upon commitments to adopt measures in order to meet the 15 percent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction requirement. See Memorandum from Michael H. Shapiro, EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Acting Assistant Administrator for Air and Radiation, ``Guidance on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Issues Related to 15 Percent Rate-of-Progress Plans,'' August 23, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1993. As a result, EPA intends not to take action to approve the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
South Coast Rate-of-Progress Plan at this time. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
c.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
 Conditional approval of commitments.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
As discussed above, EPA policy does not allow approval of 15 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Percent Rate-of-Progress Plans based on committal measures. In 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with this policy, EPA does not propose to assign credit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the SCAQMD committal measures and approve the progress plan 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
until all measures are submitted in fully enforceable form. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
However, commitments that strengthen the existing SIP can be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved, although without assignment of emission reduction credit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA proposes to conditionally approve the SCAQMD commitments 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to adopt the measures listed below, as strengthening the SIP. EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
has evaluated the commitments to adopt measures and finds that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
those commitments to adopt rules before 1996 are eligible for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditional approval under section 110(k)(4). EPA cannot propose 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to conditionally approve commitments to adopt measures with 1996 or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
later adoption dates because the SCAQMD's commitment may extend 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
beyond one year from the date of the final conditional approval 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
action (see pages 2&hyph;4 and 6&hyph;2 of the plan, and the SCAQMD 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Resolution of Adoption). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Commitments to adopt measures to contribute emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions in the period 1990&hyph;1996. 
