<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
However, because pesticide use is estimated to represent a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
significant component of the VOC emissions inventory in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento, South Coast and Ventura areas, EPA considers emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions from pesticides an important part of the overall FIP 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
attainment strategy.
<FOOTCITE>59</FOOTCITE>

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
59
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
As with all components of the FIP, &sect;52.2960 is proposed under authority of the Clean Air Act. Failure to comply
with any provision of &sect;52.2960 will violate the applicable implementation plan for purposes of section 113
of the Clean Air Act, and be subject to all administrative, civil, and criminal penalties described therein.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Under the proposed rule, EPA will establish a VOC limit that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all pesticides must meet to be distributed or applied in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
affected area. Specific pesticides are not regulated, and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proposed rule does not conflict with FIFRA's registration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cancellation or suspension procedures (7 U.S.C. 136d). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Nonetheless, EPA expects that many pesticides will need to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reformulated in order to meet the VOC limit and be useable in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
affected area. EPA has accounted for the costs of reformulation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in the technical support to this proposed rule. EPA specifically 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requests comment on how to minimize the costs of this regulation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in light of existing FIFRA regulations while still achieving the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
necessary emission reductions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
5. Cap Regulations 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
a. Introduction
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
_EPA is today proposing to promulgate Federal control measure rules to reduce emissions of VOC from sources located
in all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
three FIP areas, and NO
