contributors to FIP area emissions and whether there is any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reason that it should be expanded beyond the scope of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
existing I/M areas. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) Enforcement. Under this proposal, the Secretary of State of California, the California Department of Motor Vehicles,
its employees, any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any other persons representing the State of California are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prohibited from registering any subject vehicle which does not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
present a valid certificate of compliance with or a valid waiver 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from the FIP's I/M program requirements. At Federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
installations, where vehicles may not have California 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registration, the vehicles may not be issued a base sticker or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other operating permit without evidence of compliance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
enhanced I/M program requirements. EPA or the test provider(s) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will issue these certificates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
