<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The total fee thus would be $2.30 per LTO. In light of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
low dollar amount, and since EPA would plan in any case to adjust 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the fee upward to get the desired effect, the Agency requests 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comments on whether it is reasonable to depart from the $10,000 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
per ton level generally being used for all proposed fee systems 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in this NPRM, and start with a higher fee in the final rule for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
general aviation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Agency also requests comment on differentiating the fee 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to reflect the varying pollution potential of different aircraft 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e.g., single- versus twin-engined and piston versus turbine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
powered). As a further differentiation, EPA requests comment on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a variable fee structure for specific airports where other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission reduction schemes have been implemented by the airport 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proprietor beyond those required by the FIP or other regulations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
This would encourage control measures such as vapor recovery. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A takeoff fee would be assessed by selling one-time takeoff 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permits. The program would be administered and ultimately 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
enforced by EPA, presumably at each airport. Denial of takeoff 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permission is the most practical means of enforcement for most 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
general aviation applications, given the number of individual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pilots that would be involved in such a program. The Agency is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
consulting with the FAA in this regard, and requests comments on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the legal authority for and practical consequences of enlisting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FAA assistance in this program. At uncontrolled public and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
private airports, proprietors or owners may be able to refuse 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
services such as tie-down facilities or refueling to noncomplying 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aircraft. Otherwise, EPA would have to have a presence or a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
credible prospect of enforcement against noncomplying pilots in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
order to enforce the program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
In order to accurately track and help enforce the proposed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fee program, EPA will require owners or operators of civil 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
airports in the control areas with general aviation activity to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
obtain a general aviation operations certificate and submit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
seasonal aircraft activity reports during the ozone season. This 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will provide EPA with the information necessary to verify that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
general aviation emission reductions are occurring as intended. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Military air bases with general aviation activity will not be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject to these requirements, since such activity will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
included in an air base's environmental performance evaluation as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
described in section III.D.4.e.(2)(c) above. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
All civilian airports in the control areas with general 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aviation activity will be required to obtain a general aviation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation certificate no later than December 31, 2000. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Applications for these certificates will be submitted to EPA by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
March 20, 2000 and will include the following information: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Airport name 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&bull;Airport location, including latitude and longitude 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

