FIP. To obtain total tons of NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emitted, the number of hours of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation in the port area must be reported, as well as the rated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
power for each applicable engine on board. Thus, ships which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
enter and leave their berth efficiently will receive a lower fee. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A load factor of 80 percent
<FOOTCITE>94</FOOTCITE>
 of rated output is assumed, which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is a typical load for vessels that are cruising at sea. For 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
berthing and hotelling operations, a load factor of 25 percent is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
assumed for main propulsion engines. For auxiliary power 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
generators, a load factor of 50 percent is assumed. EPA is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proposing that cruise hours are determined as the hours that an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine operates when the ship is between 3 and 100 miles from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
port; and maneuvering/hotelling hours are hours that an engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operates when the ship is less than 3 miles from port. Both the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cruise time and the maneuvering/hotelling time are proposed to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reported for each main propulsion engine and auxiliary engine of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
each ship entering port. CARB has indicated that emissions from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
these distances may affect shore pollution levels. However, EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is currently evaluating, with the assistance of the State 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Department and Coast Guard, the appropriateness of applying these 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fees to foreign flag vessels in light of international maritime 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
law and international trade concerns. EPA requests comment on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the appropriateness of the distances proposed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

