at a rate of 18.6 g/kW-hr (64.3 x (500)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
^0.2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) at MCR. If this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine operated within the port area for 6 hours in cruising mode 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(0.8 load factor) and 12 hours in maneuvering and hotelling 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operations (0.25 load factor) it would be assessed a fee of about 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
$16,000 ([18.6&times;10,000&times;0.8&times;6&times;$5.00&times;1 lb/453.59 gr] + 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
[18.6&times;10,000&times;0.25&times;12&times;$5.00&times;1 lb/453.59 gr] = $16,000). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
By using technologies that achieve between 30 and 80 percent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction, this fee would be reduced to $8,000 ($16,000&times;.50). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Technologies achieving over 80 percent reduction would be charged 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
$1,600 ($16,000&times;.10). Discounts described below will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied on a percentage basis to these base fees, provided that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
no ship meeting the requirements for the 10 percent fee category, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cold ironing and avoiding the Ventura Air Basin will be charged 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any fee. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
These fees would be in addition to any fee assessed by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
port for docking or other benefits. EPA requests comments on: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the appropriateness of this fee calculation methodology, whether 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or not other methodologies are more appropriate, and how likely 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the proposed scheme encourages the use of technologies that would 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
achieve the emissions reduction objectives. Specifically, EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requests comments on the appropriate load factors for engines 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
during cruising (at sea) and maneuvering/hotelling operations, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and on the level of discount for the three fee levels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Emission Reduction Technologies. A number of technical designs/engine modifications are known 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to reduce, or are technologically feasible for reducing, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions of NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 from marine diesel engines. These technologies 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are presented in the table below and more fully discussed in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following text. Also, these technologies form the basis of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
three-tier fee level described in the previous section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
New engines can easily achieve the IMO specified reductions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and have achieved the lowest levels shown. Retrofitting some of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
these technologies, however, can be difficult. 
