<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
EPA recognizes that numerous issues must be addressed before 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
many of these technologies can be commercialized for diesel-fueled engines; such issues include durability, fuel
consumption 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
impacts, cost and availability of improved fuels, if they are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
needed. The Agency solicits input on these issues as well as the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
overall feasibility of the 1.5 g/bhp-hr NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 standard for diesels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Agency has received information that certain on-highway 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
heavy-duty diesel engines are using ``transient sensing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
algorithms'' that have the effect of retarding the timing during 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transient engine operating conditions and advancing the timing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
during certain steady state operating conditions.
<FOOTCITE>111</FOOTCITE>
 Since 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
injection timing has a very significant impact on NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rates, with advanced timing settings being associated with higher 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, the continued use of these algorithms could result in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engines that appear to be very low NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emitters for certification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes but would not be nearly so low when operated in-use. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The Agency would consider such algorithms used to meet the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1.5 g/bhp-hr standard to be defeat devices. They would not be an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
acceptable strategy. The Agency solicits comments on appropriate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
means of discouraging use of such design approaches. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
111
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

