=volume of exempt compounds in liters. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Person 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any firm, business establishment, association, partnership, corporation or individual, whether acting
as principal, agent, employee, or other capacity including any governmental entity or charitable organization.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rate per calendar year 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the amount applied between 12 a.m. January 1 and 11:59 p.m. December 31. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rate per day 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the amount applied between 12 a.m. and 11:59 p.m. on the same calendar day. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transfer efficiency 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the ratio of the weight of coating solids deposited on an object to the total weight of coating solids used in a
coating application step, expressed as a percentage. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Volatile organic compound (VOC) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any compound of carbon, excluding carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, carbonic acid, metallic carbides or carbonates,
and ammonium carbonate, which participates in atmospheric photochemical reactions other than those defined as
exempt compounds. These exempt compounds have been determined to have negligible photochemical reactivity. For
purposes of determining compliance with emission limits, VOC will be measured by test methods given in this section.
Where such a method also measures compounds with negligible photochemical reactivity, an owner or operator may exclude
these negligibly reactive compounds when determining compliance with an emission standard. However, the U.S. EPA
may require such owner or operator, as a precondition to excluding these compounds for purposes of determining compliance,
to provide monitoring methods and monitoring results demonstrating, to the satisfaction of the U.S. EPA, the amount
of negligibly reactive compounds in the source's emissions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;52.2951 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
New technology measures applicable to VOC and NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) The applicable area of control is the South Coast Air Basin Nonattainment Area for ozone, as defined in 40 CFR 81.305.
For purposes of this regulation, the definitions of &sect;52.2950 shall apply. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stationary and area source VOC cap categories to be controlled. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purpose of this paragraph, the following categories of VOC emissions sources shall constitute the control
categories. The categories are further defined in &sect;52.2954. Facilities which emit greater than or equal to
4 tons per year of VOCs from any of the following processes or combination of these processes are affected: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Industrial and commercial solvents and coatings;
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=5 f=1 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
In the alternative, rules may apply to any manufacturer, or consortium of manufacturers, of industrial solvents
or industrial/commercial coatings for sale or use within the State of California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(2) VOC emissions associated with the manufacturing of products; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Disposal of materials containing VOCs; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Commercial food preparation and/or baking; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Petroleum and natural gas extraction, processing, and storage. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
