<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Control Device Efficiency Testing and Monitoring. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Control Efficiency Test. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The control device efficiency shall be determined by simultaneously measuring the inlet and outlet gas phase VOC
concentrations and gas volumetric flow rates in accordance with the gas phase test methods specified in paragraph
(a)(4)(vi) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Continuous Monitoring. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any owner or operator that uses an afterburner or carbon adsorber to comply with any requirement of this section shall
use continuous monitoring equipment which is installed, calibrated, maintained, and operated according to vendor
specifications and which meets EPA-approved performance specifications at all times when the afterburner or carbon
adsorber is in use. The continuous monitoring equipment must automatically monitor and record the following parameters:

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Combustion chamber temperature of each afterburner. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Temperature rise across each catalytic afterburner bed or VOC concentration exhaust. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The VOC concentration of each carbon adsorption bed exhaust. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recordkeeping and Reporting. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All affected facilities must maintain a copy of all control efficiency test protocols for a period of five (5) years.
All control test results must be reported to EPA within sixty (60) days of the test date. A copy of the results must be
kept on file with the source for a period of five (5) years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All affected facilities must maintain copies of all required continuous monitoring records for a period of five
(5) years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) If any changes are made to control equipment, affected facilities must notify EPA of these changes and a new control
efficiency test may be required by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All affected facilities must notify the Administrator 30 days prior to performing any control efficiency test.
At that time, the source must notify the Administrator which test methods will be used. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Overall Efficiency. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The overall efficiency of each emission control system shall be determined as the product of the capture system
efficiency and the control device efficiency or by the liquid/liquid test protocol as specified in paragraph (a)(4)(iii)(A)(2)
of this section for each solvent recovery system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The overall efficiency of the capture system and control device used to control VOC emissions from a paper, fabric,
film, can, coil, or miscellaneous metal parts and products coating line, as determined by the test methods and procedures
specified in paragraphs (a)(4)(iii), (a)(4)(iv), and (a)(4)(v)(A) of this section, shall be no less than the equivalent
overall efficiency which shall be calculated by the following equation:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=3 -->
E = ([VOC
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
a
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
&hyph;VOC
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
]/VOC
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
a
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
) x 100
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
where: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
E = Equivalent overall efficiency of the capture system and control device as a percentage, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VOC
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
a
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
 = Actual VOC content of a coating, or the daily-weighted average VOC content of two or more coatings (if more than one
coating is used), as applied to the subject coating line as determined by the applicable test methods and procedures
specified in paragraph (a)(4)(i) of this section in units of kg VOC/l (lb VOC/gal) of coating solids as applied, and

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VOC
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
 = The VOC emission limit specified in units of kg VOC/liter (lb VOC/gal) of coating solids as applied. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(vi) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Volatile Organic Compound Gas Phase Source Test Methods. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The methods in 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, delineated below shall be used to determine control device efficiencies.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Methods 18, 25, 25A, or 25B, as appropriate to the conditions at the site, shall be used
to determine VOC concentration. Method selection shall be based on consideration of the diversity of organic species
present and their total concentration and on consideration of the potential presence of interfering gases. Except
as indicated in paragraphs (a)(4)(vi)(A) (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section, the test shall consist of three separate runs, each lasting a minimum of 60 min., unless the Administrator
determines that process variables dictate shorter sampling times. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) When the method is to be used to determine the efficiency of a fixed-bed carbon adsorption system with a common exhaust
stack for all the individual adsorber vessels, the test shall consist of three separate runs, each coinciding with
one or more complete sequences through the adsorption cycles of all the individual adsorber vessels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) When the method is to be used to determine the efficiency of a carbon adsorption system with individual exhaust stacks
for each adsorber vessel, each adsorber vessel shall be tested individually. The test for each adsorber vessel shall
consist of three separate runs. Each run shall coincide with one or more complete adsorption cycles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 1 or 1A shall be used for sample and velocity traverses. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 2, 2A, 2C, or 2D shall be used for velocity and volumetric flow rates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 3, 3A or 3B shall be used for gas analysis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 4 shall be used for stack gas moisture. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Methods 2, 2A, 2C, or 2D; 3, 3A, or 3B; and 4 shall be performed, as applicable, at least
twice during each test run. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
