<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(G) Use of an adaptation to any of the test methods specified in paragraphs (a)(4)(vi) (A), (B), (C), (D), (E), and (F)
of this section may be approved by the Administrator on a case-by-case basis. An owner or operator must submit sufficient
documentation for the Administrator to find that the test methods specified in paragraphs (a)(4)(vi) (A), (B), (C),
(D), (E), and (F) of this section will yield inaccurate results and that the proposed adaptation is appropriate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak Detection Methods for Volatile Organic Compounds
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Owners or operators required by the various subparts of this regulation to carry out a leak detection monitoring
program shall comply with the following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Leak Detection Monitoring. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Monitoring shall comply with 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 21. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The detection instrument shall meet the performance criteria of 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 21. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The instrument shall be calibrated before use on each day of its use by the methods specified in 40 CFR part 60, appendix
A, Method 21. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Calibration gases shall be: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Zero air (less than 10 ppm of hydrocarbon in air), and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A mixture of methane or n-hexane and air at a concentration of approximately, but no less than, 10,000 ppm methane or
n-hexane. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The instrument probe shall be traversed around all potential leak interfaces as close to the interface as possible
as described in 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 21. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) When equipment is tested for compliance with no detectable emissions as required, the test shall comply with the
following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of paragraphs (a)(4)(vii)(A)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
through (vii)(A)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
of this section shall apply. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The background level shall be determined as set forth in 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 21. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Leak detection tests shall be performed consistent with: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
``APTI Course SI 417 Controlling Volatile Organic Compound Emissions from Leaking Process Equipment'' EPA&hyph;450/2&hyph;82&hyph;015
(which is available from the National Technical Information Services, 5285 Port Royal Road, Springfield, Virginia,
22161) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
``Portable Instrument User's Manual for Monitoring VOC Sources'' EPA&hyph;340/1&hyph;86&hyph;015 (which is
available from the National Technical Information Services, 5285 Port Royal Road, Springfield, Virginia, 22161)

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

