<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 ``Petroleum Refinery Enforcement Manual'' EPA&hyph;340/1&hyph;80&hyph;008 (which is available from the National
Technical Information Services, 5285 Port Royal Road, Springfield, Virginia 22161) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Bulk Gasoline Delivery System Test Protocol. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The method for determining the emissions of gasoline from a vapor recovery system are delineated in 40 CFR part
60, subpart XX, &sect;60.503. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Other tests shall be performed consistent with: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 ``Inspection Manual for Control of Volatile Organic Emissions from Gasoline Marketing Operations: appendix D''
EPA&hyph;340/1&hyph;80&hyph;012 (which is available from the National Technical Information Services, 5285
Port Royal Road, Springfield, Virginia 22161). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 ``Control of Hydrocarbons from Tank Truck Gasoline Loading Terminals: appendix A'', EPA&hyph;450/2&hyph;77&hyph;026
(which is available from the National Technical Information Services, 5285 Port Royal Road, Springfield, Virginia
22161).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ix) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vapor Pressure of Volatile Organic Liquids. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) If the VOL consists of only a single compound, the vapor pressure shall be determined by ASTM Method D2879&hyph;86
(incorporated by reference as specified in paragraph (c) of this section or the vapor pressure may be obtained from
a published source such as: Boublik, T., V. Fried and E. Hala, ``The Vapor Pressure of Pure Substances,'' Elsevier
Scientific Publishing Co., New York (1973), Perry's Chemical Engineer's Handbook, McGraw-Hill Book Company (1984),
CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, Chemical Rubber Publishing Company (1986&hyph;87), and Lange's Handbook
of Chemistry, John A. Dean, editor, McGraw-Hill Book Company (1985). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) If the VOL is a mixture, the vapor pressure shall be determined by ASTM Method D2879&hyph;86 (incorporated by reference
as specified in paragraph (c) of this section) or by the following equation: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->

<!-- PJG STAG 4725 -->

<IMPORT>

<!-- PJG importformat s,w58,d29 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=92 g=1 f=3 -->
E:GraphicsEP05MY94.004
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</IMPORT>

<!-- PJG /STAG -->

<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=3 -->
where: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
P
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
vol
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

