<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Lithographic printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which the image and nonimage areas are on the same plane of the roll printer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Magnet wire coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more magnet coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Magnet wire coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which electrically insulating varnish or enamel is applied onto the surface of wire to be used
in electrical machinery. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Marine vessel 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a ship or boat used to travel on, or a submarine used to travel through, the sea. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Marine vessel coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more marine vessel coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Marine vessel coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied on the fabricated part,
assembly of parts, or completed unit of any marine vessel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metal furniture 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any furniture piece made of metal or any metal part which is or will be assembled with other metal, wood, fabric,
plastic, or glass parts to form a furniture piece including, but not limited to, tables, chairs, waste baskets, beds,
desks, lockers, benches, shelving, file cabinets, lamps, and room dividers. This definition shall not apply to any
coating unit coating miscellaneous metal parts or products. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metal furniture coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more metal furniture coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metal furniture coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
unit means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of
metal furniture. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Miscellaneous metal part or product 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any metal part or metal product, even if attached to or combined with a nonmetal part or product. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Miscellaneous metal parts or products coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more miscellaneous metal parts or products coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Miscellaneous metal parts or products coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of miscellaneous
metal parts or products. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Mobile equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means self-propelled equipment which is physically capable of being driven on a highway. Mobile equipment includes:
Automobiles, motorcycles, trucks, vans, construction equipment (e.g., mobile cranes, bulldozers, concrete mixers),
farming equipment (e.g., wheel tractors, pesticide sprayers), and miscellaneous equipment (e.g., street cleaners,
golf carts, and hauling equipment used inside and around airports, docks, depots, and industrial and commercial
plants).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a vehicle which is self-propelled and physically capable of being driven on a highway. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle or mobile equipment assembly line coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility where parts are manufactured or finished for eventual inclusion into finished motor vehicles or
mobile equipment ready for sale to motor vehicle or mobile equipment dealers. This definition does not include customizers,
body shops, and/or other auto refinishing facilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle or mobile equipment refinishing facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility where all or any part of used motor vehicles or mobile equipment is refinished, or customized, by the
application of paint. This definition includes motor vehicles or mobile equipment dealerships who purchase new
motor vehicle or mobile equipment from Original Equipment Manufacturers. This definition does not include motor
vehicle or mobile equipment assembly line coating facilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motorcycle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any motor vehicle other than a tractor having a seat or saddle for the use of the rider and designed to travel on
not more than three wheels in contact with the ground and weighing less than 1,500 lbs, except that four wheels may be
in contact with the ground when two of the wheels are a functional part of a sidecar. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Offset 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a blanket cylinder that is used to transfer ink from a plate cylinder to the substance to be printed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Open-top vapor degreasing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the batch process of cleaning and removing soils from surfaces by condensing hot solvent vapor on the colder
metal parts. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Oven 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a chamber within which heat is used for one or more of the following purposes: To dry, bake, cure, or polymerize
a coating or ink. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00259 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Packaging rotogravure printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means rotogravure printing upon paper, paper board, metal foil, plastic film, and other substrates which are, in
subsequent operations, formed into packaging products or labels for articles to be sold. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Packaging rotogravure printing press 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a rotogravure printing press in which surface coatings are applied to paper, paperboard, metal foil, plastic
film, or other substrates which are to be used to produce containers, packaging products, or labels for articles.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Paper coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more paper coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Paper coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a web coating unit where coating is applied to paper. Printing presses are not considered paper coating units.
Products produced on a paper coating unit include, but are not limited to, adhesive tapes and labels, book covers,
post cards, office copier paper, drafting paper, and pressure sensitive tapes. Paper coating units include, but
are not limited to, application by impregnation or saturation or by the use of roll, knife, or rotogravure coating.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an operation consisting of a series of one or more roll printers and any associated roll coaters, drying areas,
and/or ovens wherein one or more surface coatings are applied, dried, and/or cured. It is not necessary for an operation
to have an oven, or flashoff area, or drying area to be included in this definition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Publication rotogravure printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a rotogravure printing unit in which surface coatings are applied to paper which is subsequently formed into
books, magazines, catalogues, brochures, directories, newspaper supplements, or other types of printed material.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Refinish 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means to restore or replace coatings on Group I vehicles (large-sized trucks, buses, and mobile equipment) and Group
II vehicles (passenger cars, small-sized trucks and vans, medium-sized trucks and vans, and motorcycles) and equipment,
or their parts and components, except Original Equipment Manufacturer coatings applied at motor vehicle or mobile
equipment assembly line coating facilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Roll coater 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an apparatus in which a uniform layer of coating material is applied by means of a roll or rolls across the entire
width of a moving substrate which is fed from an unwinding roll. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Roll printer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an apparatus in which a surface coating is applied by means of a roll or rolls with only partial coverage across
the width of a moving substrate which is fed from an unwinding roll. The partial coverage results in the formation of
words, designs, or pictures on the substrate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rotogravure printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the application of words, designs, and pictures to a substrate using a gravure cylinder by means of a roll printing
technique in which the pattern to be applied is recessed relative to the nonimage area. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rotogravure printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which each roll printer uses a roll with recessed areas for applying an image to a substrate.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Screen printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which the printing ink passes through a web or a fabric to which a refined form of stencil has
been applied. The stencil openings determine the form and dimensions of the imprint. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a substance that is liquid at standard conditions that is used to dissolve or dilute another substance; this
term includes, but is not limited to, organic materials used as dissolvers, viscosity reducers, degreasing agents,
or cleaning agents. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent cleaning 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the process of cleaning soils from surfaces by cold cleaning, open-top vapor degreasing, or conveyorized degreasing.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Space vehicle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any vehicle designed to travel beyond the earth's atmosphere. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Street 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a public road in a town or city. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Substrate 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the surface to which a coating is applied on, saturated into, or impregnated into. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vinyl coating facility
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a facility that includes one or more vinyl coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vinyl coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a web coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating or printing ink is applied onto
a continuous web of vinyl-coated fabric or vinyl sheets. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00260 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Web 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an automatic system which supplies substrate from a continuous roll or an extrusion process. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood furniture 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means room furnishings including cabinets (kitchen, bath, and vanity), tables, chairs, beds, sofas, shutters,
art objects, wood paneling, wood flooring, and any other coated furnishings made of wood, wood composition, or fabricated
wood materials. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood furniture coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more wood furniture coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood furniture coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto wood furniture. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicability. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The requirements of paragraphs (b)(1 (iii)(A) and (B), (iv)(A), (v)(A), and (vi)(A) of this section shall apply
to any owner or operator of any degreasing facility or any motor vehicle or mobile equipment refinishing facility
located in the control area as defined in paragraph (a)(1) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The requirements of paragraphs (b)(1) (iii)(A) and (B), (iv)(A), (v)(A), and (vi)(A) of this section shall apply
to any owner or operator of an industrial or commercial solvent use facility located in the applicable area specified
in paragraph (b)(1)(ii)(A) of this section at which actual emissions of VOC are greater than or equal to 6.8 kg (15 lbs)
during any one day. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The requirements of paragraphs (b)(1) (iv)(B), (v)(B), and (vi)(B) of this section shall apply to any owner or
operator of an industrial or commercial solvent use facility located in the applicable area specified in paragraph
(b)(1)(ii)(A) of this section at which actual emissions of VOC from all emissions sources are always less than 6.8
kg (15 lbs) during any one day. If actual emissions of VOC from a facility which is exempt from the limitations of paragraph
(b)(1)(iii)(B) of this section ever exceed 6.8 kg (15 lbs) during any one day on or after January 1, 2000, the facility
will lose its exempt status, and the owner or operator shall comply with the requirements of paragraphs (b)(1)(iii)(B)
(1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 through 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(5),
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (b)(1)(iv)(A), (b)(1)(v)(A), and (b)(1)(vi)(A) of this section beginning January 1 of the calendar year following
the date of the exceedance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Specific Provisions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Each owner or operator of a source subject to the FIP VOC emissions cap program as defined in paragraph (b)(1)(ii)
of this section shall submit a VOC emissions reduction compliance plan to the Administrator by January 1, 1999. The
plan shall be prepared for the years 2001 through 2005 and shall include all of the information specified in paragraphs
(b)(1)(iii)(A) (1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) through (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section. Each owner or operator shall submit a revised plan to the Administrator within 30 calendar days of
receipt of comments from the Administrator. Each owner or operator shall comply at all times with the provisions of
the most recent plan approved by the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The name, title, address, and telephone number of the owner or operator of the facility, and of each person responsible
for preparing the information required under paragraph (b)(1)(iii)(A)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
