<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Monitor 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means to measure and record. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Organic compound 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a chemical compound of carbon, excluding carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, carbonic acid, metallic carbides,
carbonates, and ammonium carbonate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Organic vapor 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the gaseous phase of an organic compound or a mixture of organic compounds present in the atmosphere. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Owner or operator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any person who owns, operates, leases, controls, or supervises an emissions source or air pollution control
equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Person 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any individual, corporation, copartnership, firm, company, partnership, joint stock company, trust, association,
State, municipality, political subdivision, or any other legal entity, or their legal representative, agent, or
assigns. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Process 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any stationary emission source other than a fuel combustion emission source or an incinerator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Source 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means emission source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standard conditions 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a temperature of 20
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F) and a pressure of 760 mm Hg (29.92 in. Hg).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stationary emission source 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
and 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stationary source
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 mean an emission source which is not self-propelled. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods and Procedures
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coatings, Inks, and Fountain Solutions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The following test methods and procedures shall be used to determine the VOC content of as applied coatings, inks,
and fountain solutions to determine compliance with the limitations set forth in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Sampling
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Samples collected for analyses shall be one-liter taken into a one-liter container at a location and time such that
the sample will be representative of the coating as applied (i.e., the sample shall include any dilution solvent or
other VOC added during the manufacturing process). The container must be tightly sealed immediately after the sample
is taken. Any solvent or other VOC added after the sample is taken must be measured and accounted for in the calculations
in paragraph (a)(4)(i)(C) of this section. For multiple package coatings, separate samples of each component shall
be obtained. A mixed sample shall not be obtained as it will cure in the container. Sampling procedures shall follow
the guidelines presented in: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D3925&hyph;81 (1985) Standard Practice for Sampling Liquid Paints and Related Pigment Coating. This practice
is incorporated by reference in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM E300 Standard Practice for Sampling Industrial Chemicals. This practice is incorporated by reference in paragraph
(c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Analyses. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The applicable analytical methods specified below shall be used to determine the composition of coatings, inks,
or fountain solutions as applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Method 24 of 40 CFR part 60, appendix A shall be used to determine the VOC content and density of coatings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Method 24A of 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, shall be used to determine the VOC content and density of publication rotogravure
printing inks and related coatings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The following ASTM methods and practices are the analytical procedures for determining VOC: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D1475&hyph;85: Standard Test Method for Density of Paint, Varnish, Lacquer and Related Products. This test
method is incorporated by reference in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D2369&hyph;87: Standard Test Method for Volatile Content of a Coating. This test method is incorporated by reference
in paragraph (c) of this section. The following minor modifications should be used for multicomponent coatings.
All components of the coating are to be weighed in the proper proportion into the analysis container and mixed together
just prior to analysis and the mixture is allowed to stand for at least one hour but no more than 24 hours prior to being
oven dried at 110 degrees celsius for one hour. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D3792&hyph;86: Standard Test Method for Water Content of Water-Reducible Paints by Direct Injection into a
Gas Chromatograph. This test method is incorporated by reference in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D4017&hyph;81 (1987): Standard Test Method for Water Content in Paints and Paint Materials by the Karl Fischer
Method. This test method is incorporated by reference in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D4457&hyph;85: Standard Test Method for Determination of Dichloromethane and 1,1,1-Trichloroethane in Paints
and Coatings by Direct Injection into a Gas Chromatograph. (The procedure delineated above can be used to develop
protocols for any compounds specifically exempted from the definition of VOC.) This test method is incorporated
by reference in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(vi) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D2697&hyph;86: Standard Test Method for Volume Non-volatile Matter in Clear or Pigmented Coatings. This test
method is incorporated by reference in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(vii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM E180&hyph;85: Standard Practice for Determining the Precision Data of ASTM Methods for Analysis and Testing
of Industrial Chemicals. This practice is incorporated by reference in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
