<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(C) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recordkeeping and Reporting
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All affected facilities must maintain a copy of the capture efficiency protocol submitted to EPA on file. All results
of the appropriate test methods and capture efficiency protocols must be reported to EPA within sixty (60) days of
the test date. A copy of the results must be kept on file with the source for a period of five (5) years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 If any changes are made to capture equipment, then affected facilities must notify EPA of these changes and a new test
may be required by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(3)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All affected facilities must notify the Administrator 30 days prior to performing any capture efficiency test. At
that time, the source must notify the Administrator which capture efficiency protocol will be used. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(4)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All affected facilities utilizing a PTE must demonstrate that this enclosure meets the requirement given in Procedure
T in appendix B of 40 CFR 52.741 at all times. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(5)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All affected facilities utilizing a TTE must demonstrate that their TTE meets the requirements given in Procedure
T in appendix B of 40 CFR 52.741 for a TTE during testing of their control device. The source must also provide documentation
that the quality assurance criteria for a TTE have been achieved. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Control Device Efficiency Testing and Monitoring. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Control Efficiency Test.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The control device efficiency shall be determined by simultaneously measuring the inlet and outlet gas phase VOC
concentrations and gas volumetric flow rates in accordance with the gas phase test methods specified in paragraph
(a)(4)(vi) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Continuous Monitoring.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Any owner or operator that uses an afterburner or carbon adsorber to comply with any requirement of this section shall
use continuous monitoring equipment which is installed, calibrated, maintained, and operated according to vendor
specifications and which meets EPA-approved performance specifications at all times when the afterburner or carbon
adsorber is in use. The continuous monitoring equipment must automatically monitor and record the following parameters:

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Combustion chamber temperature of each afterburner. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Temperature rise across each catalytic afterburner bed or VOC concentration exhaust. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(3)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The VOC concentration of each carbon adsorption bed exhaust. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recordkeeping and Reporting. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All affected facilities must maintain a copy of all control efficiency test protocols for a period of five (5) years.
All control test results must be reported to EPA within sixty (60) days of the test date. A copy of the results must be
kept on file with the source for a period of five (5) years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All affected facilities must maintain copies of all required continuous monitoring records for a period of five (5)
years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(3)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 If any changes are made to control equipment, affected facilities must notify EPA of these changes and a new control
efficiency test may be required by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(4)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All affected facilities must notify the Administrator 30 days prior to performing any control efficiency test. At
that time, the source must notify the Administrator which test methods will be used. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Overall Efficiency.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The overall efficiency of each emission control system shall be determined as the product of the capture system
efficiency and the control device efficiency or by the liquid/liquid test protocol as specified in paragraph (a)(4)(iii)(A)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 of this section for each solvent recovery system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The overall efficiency of the capture system and control device used to control VOC emissions from a paper, fabric,
film, can, coil, or miscellaneous metal parts and products coating line, as determined by the test methods and procedures
specified in paragraphs (a)(4)(iii), (a)(4)(iv), and (a)(4)(v)(A) of this section, shall be no less than the equivalent
overall efficiency which shall be calculated by the following equation:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

