<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(vi) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Volatile Organic Compound Gas Phase Source Test Methods.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The methods in 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, delineated below shall be used to determine control device efficiencies.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Methods 18, 25, 25A, or 25B, as appropriate to the conditions at the site, shall be used
to determine VOC concentration. Method selection shall be based on consideration of the diversity of organic species
present and their total concentration and on consideration of the potential presence of interfering gases. Except
as indicated in paragraphs (a)(4)(vi)(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 of this section, the test shall consist of three separate runs, each lasting a minimum of 60 min., unless the Administrator
determines that process variables dictate shorter sampling times. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 When the method is to be used to determine the efficiency of a fixed-bed carbon adsorption system with a common exhaust
stack for all the individual adsorber vessels, the test shall consist of three separate runs, each coinciding with
one or more complete sequences through the adsorption cycles of all the individual adsorber vessels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 When the method is to be used to determine the efficiency of a carbon adsorption system with individual exhaust stacks
for each adsorber vessel, each adsorber vessel shall be tested individually. The test for each adsorber vessel shall
consist of three separate runs. Each run shall coincide with one or more complete adsorption cycles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 1 or 1A shall be used for sample and velocity traverses. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 2, 2A, 2C, or 2D shall be used for velocity and volumetric flow rates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 3, 3A or 3B shall be used for gas analysis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 4 shall be used for stack gas moisture. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
