<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(B) The reduced daily baseline emissions shall be annualized by multiplying the daily value by 365. This value shall
be defined as the reduced annual baseline emissions and is denoted in pounds of VOC/year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The reduced annual baseline emissions shall be converted into a monthly value by dividing by 12. This value shall
be defined as the implementation year monthly baseline. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Enforcement. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) All sources and facilities subject to provisions of &sect;52.2952 shall be subject to unannounced inspections
by representatives of the USEPA pursuant to section 114 of the Clean Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Documentation maintained by all sources, facilities, and persons subject to this section must be sufficient
to demonstrate compliance with all requirements of this section and must be provided to representatives of USEPA
upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Failure to comply with any provision of this section is a violation of the applicable implementation plan for
purposes of section 113 of the Clean Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Each 50 pounds of emissions in excess of a facility's monthly cap shall be a separate violation for federal enforcement
purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) Stationary and Area Source Control Measures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Industrial and Commercial Solvents/Coatings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Definitions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) For the purpose of paragraph (b)(1) of this section, the general definitions in paragraph (a)(3) of this section
apply. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) For the purpose of paragraph (b)(1) of this section, the following definitions also apply: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Adhesives 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any substance or mixture of substances intended to serve as a joining compound. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aerospace component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the fabricated part, assembly of parts, or completed unit of any aircraft or space vehicle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aerospace component coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more aerospace component coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aerospace component coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating or reinforcing material is applied
on or impregnated into an aerospace component. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aircraft 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any machine designed to travel through the air above ground without leaving the earth's atmosphere, whether
heavier or lighter than air, including airplanes, balloons, dirigibles, helicopters, and missiles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Automobile 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a motor vehicle capable of carrying no more than 12 passengers. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Can 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any cylindrical, single walled container that is manufactured from metal sheets thinner than 29 gauge (0.0141
in.); with or without a top, cover, spout, or handles; into which solid or liquid materials are packaged. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Can coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more can coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Can coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of cans
or can components. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a material applied onto or impregnated into a substrate for protective, decorative, or functional purposes.
Such materials include, but are not limited to, paints, varnishes, sealants, adhesives, thinners, diluents, inks,
maskants, and/or temporary protective coatings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coating applicator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any equipment or device, including but not limited to cloth, rollers, brushes, spray guns, and dip tanks, used
to apply a coating onto or into a substrate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a series of one or more coating applicators and any associated drying areas and/or oven wherein a coating is applied,
dried, and/or cured. A coating unit ends at the point where the coating is dried or cured, or prior to any subsequent
application of a different coating. It is not necessary to have an oven or a flashoff area in order to be included in this
definition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coil 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any continuous metal sheet or strip with thickness of 0.15 mm (0.006 in.) or more that is packaged in a roll or coil.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coil coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more coil coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00307 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coil coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of flat
metal sheets, strips, rolls, or coils for industrial or commercial use. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cold cleaning 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the batch process of cleaning and removing soils from surfaces by spraying, brushing, flushing, or immersion
while maintaining the organic solvent below its boiling point. Wipe cleaning is not included in this definition.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Conveyorized degreasing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the continuous process of cleaning and removing soils from surfaces using either cold or vaporized solvents.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Degreaser 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any equipment or system used in solvent cleaning. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Degreasing facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more cold cleaning, open-top vapor degreasing, and/or conveyorized degreasing
processes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Dry cleaning facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility engaged in the cleaning of fabrics using an essentially nonaqueous solvent by means of one or more
solvent washes, extraction of excess solvent by spinning, and drying by tumbling in an airstream. The facility includes,
but is not limited to, washers, dryers, filter and purification systems, waste disposal systems, holding tanks,
pumps, and attendant piping and valves. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fabric coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more fabric coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fabric coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a web coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating or reinforcing material is applied
on, saturated into, or impregnated into a textile fabric. A fabric printing unit is not considered a fabric coating
unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Film coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more film coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Film coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied on, saturated into, or
impregnated into any film substrate; other than paper, fabric, or vinyl; including but not limited to typewriter
ribbons, photographic film, plastic film, magnetic tape, and metal foil. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Flatwood product 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means panels made of wood materials including; but not limited to; plywood, particle board, and hardboard. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Flatwood product coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more flatwood product coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Flatwood product coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied on or impregnated into
a flatwood product. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Flexographic printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the application of words, designs, and pictures to a substrate by means of a roll printing technique in which
the pattern to be applied is raised above the printing roll and the image carrier is made of elastomeric materials.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Flexographic printing press 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing press in which each roll printer uses a roll with raised areas for applying an image such as words, designs,
or pictures to a substrate. The image carrier on the roll is made of rubber or other elastomeric material. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fountain solution 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the solution which is applied to the lithographic printing plate to maintain hydrophilic properties of the
nonimage areas. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Graphic arts coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more graphic arts coating units. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Graphic arts coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any packaging rotogravure printing, publication rotogravure printing, flexographic printing, lithographic
printing, letterpress printing, laminating, or screen printing unit or any paper, fabric, or film coating unit operated
in conjunction with a printing unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Group I vehicles and equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means large-sized trucks, buses, and mobile equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Group II vehicles 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means passenger cars, small-sized trucks and vans, medium-sized trucks and vans, and motorcycles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heatset 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a class of web-offset lithography which requires a heated dryer to solidify the printing inks. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heatset-web-offset lithographic printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a lithographic printing unit in which a blanket cylinder is used to transfer ink from a plate cylinder to a substrate
continuously fed from a roll or an extension process and an oven is used to solidify the printing inks. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00308 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heavy off-highway vehicle products 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means heavy construction, mining, farming, or material handling equipment; heavy industrial engines; diesel-electric
locomotives and associated power generation equipment; and the components of such equipment or engines. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heavy off-highway vehicle products coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more heavy off-highway vehicle products coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heavy off-highway vehicle products coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of heavy
off-highway vehicle products. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Highway 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a way or place of whatever nature, publicly maintained and open to the public for purposes of vehicular travel.
Highway includes street. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Industrial or commercial solvent use facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any industrial or commercial facility that uses solvents which contain VOCs or substances that contain solvents
which contain VOCs. Industrial and commercial solvent use facilities include, but are not limited to, perchloroethylene
dry cleaning, petroleum dry cleaning, metal cleaning, degreasing, aerospace component coating, motor vehicle
and mobile equipment assembly line coating, motor vehicle and mobile equipment refinishing, can coating, coil coating,
fabric coating, film coating, flatwood product coating, graphic arts coating, large appliance coating, magnet
wire coating, marine vessel coating, metal and wood furniture coating, miscellaneous metal parts and products coating,
paper coating, and plastic parts coating facilities. Substances that contain solvents include, but are not limited
to, coatings, inks, fountain solutions, adhesives, thinners, and clean-up solvents. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Ink 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating used in printing, impressing, or transferring an image onto a substrate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Laminating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which an adhesive is used to form two or more layers of material into a single, multiple-layer
sheet. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Large appliance 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the component metal parts (including, but not limited to, doors, cases, lids, panels, and interior support
parts) of residential and commercial washers, dryers, ranges, refrigerators, freezers, water heaters, dish washers,
trash compactors, air conditioners, and other similar products under SIC Code 363. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Large appliance coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more large appliance coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Large appliance coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of component
metal parts of large appliances. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Letterpress printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which the image area is raised relative to the nonimage area on the roll printer and the ink is
transferred to the paper directly from the image surface. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Light-duty truck 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any motor vehicle rated at 3864 kg (8500 lb) gross vehicle weight or less, designed mainly to transport property.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Lithographic printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which the image and nonimage areas are on the same plane of the roll printer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Magnet wire coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more magnet coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Magnet wire coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which electrically insulating varnish or enamel is applied onto the surface of wire to be used
in electrical machinery. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Marine vessel 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a ship or boat used to travel on, or a submarine used to travel through, the sea. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Marine vessel coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more marine vessel coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Marine vessel coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied on the fabricated part,
assembly of parts, or completed unit of any marine vessel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metal furniture 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any furniture piece made of metal or any metal part which is or will be assembled with other metal, wood, fabric,
plastic, or glass parts to form a furniture piece including, but not limited to, tables, chairs, waste baskets, beds,
desks, lockers, benches, shelving, file cabinets, lamps, and room dividers. This definition shall not apply to any
coating unit coating miscellaneous metal parts or products. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metal furniture coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more metal furniture coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metal furniture coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of metal
furniture. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Miscellaneous metal part or product 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any metal part or metal product, even if attached to or combined with a nonmetal part or product. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Miscellaneous metal parts or products coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more miscellaneous metal parts or products coating unit(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Miscellaneous metal parts or products coating unit means 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto the surface of miscellaneous
metal parts or products. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Mobile equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means self-propelled equipment which is physically capable of being driven on a highway. Mobile equipment includes:
automobiles, motorcycles, trucks, vans, construction equipment (e.g., mobile cranes, bulldozers, concrete mixers),
farming equipment (e.g., wheel tractors, pesticide sprayers), and miscellaneous equipment (e.g., street cleaners,
golf carts, and hauling equipment used inside and around airports, docks, depots, and industrial and commercial
plants). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a vehicle which is self-propelled and physically capable of being driven on a highway. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00309 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle or mobile equipment assembly line coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility where parts are manufactured or finished for eventual inclusion into finished motor vehicles or
mobile equipment ready for sale to motor vehicle or mobile equipment dealers. This definition does not include customizers,
body shops, and/or other auto refinishing facilities.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle or mobile equipment refinishing facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility where all or any part of used motor vehicles or mobile equipment is refinished, or customized, by the
application of paint. This definition includes motor vehicles or mobile equipment dealerships who purchase new
motor vehicle or mobile equipment from Original Equipment Manufacturers. This definition does not include motor
vehicle or mobile equipment assembly line coating facilities.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motorcycle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any motor vehicle other than a tractor having a seat or saddle for the use of the rider and designed to travel on
not more than three wheels in contact with the ground and weighing less than 1,500 lbs, except that four wheels may be
in contact with the ground when two of the wheels are a functional part of a sidecar.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Offset 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a blanket cylinder that is used to transfer ink from a plate cylinder to the substance to be printed.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Open-top vapor degreasing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the batch process of cleaning and removing soils from surfaces by condensing hot solvent vapor on the colder
metal parts.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Oven 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a chamber within which heat is used for one or more of the following purposes: To dry, bake, cure, or polymerize
a coating or ink.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Packaging rotogravure printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means rotogravure printing upon paper, paper board, metal foil, plastic film, and other substrates which are, in
subsequent operations, formed into packaging products or labels for articles to be sold.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Packaging rotogravure printing press 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a rotogravure printing press in which surface coatings are applied to paper, paperboard, metal foil, plastic
film, or other substrates which are to be used to produce containers, packaging products, or labels for articles.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Paper coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more paper coating unit(s).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Paper coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a web coating unit where coating is applied to paper. Printing presses are not considered paper coating units.
Products produced on a paper coating unit include, but are not limited to, adhesive tapes and labels, book covers,
post cards, office copier paper, drafting paper, and pressure sensitive tapes. Paper coating units include, but
are not limited to, application by impregnation or saturation or by the use of roll, knife, or rotogravure coating.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an operation consisting of a series of one or more roll printers and any associated roll coaters, drying areas,
and/or ovens wherein one or more surface coatings are applied, dried, and/or cured. It is not necessary for an operation
to have an oven, or flashoff area, or drying area to be included in this definition.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Publication rotogravure printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a rotogravure printing unit in which surface coatings are applied to paper which is subsequently formed into
books, magazines, catalogues, brochures, directories, newspaper supplements, or other types of printed material.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Refinish 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means to restore or replace coatings on Group I vehicles (large-sized trucks, buses, and mobile equipment) and Group
II vehicles (passenger cars, small-sized trucks and vans, medium-sized trucks and vans, and motorcycles) and equipment,
or their parts and components, except Original Equipment Manufacturer coatings applied at motor vehicle or mobile
equipment assembly line coating facilities.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Roll coater 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an apparatus in which a uniform layer of coating material is applied by means of a roll or rolls across the entire
width of a moving substrate which is fed from an unwinding roll.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Roll printer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an apparatus in which a surface coating is applied by means of a roll or rolls with only partial coverage across
the width of a moving substrate which is fed from an unwinding roll. The partial coverage results in the formation of
words, designs, or pictures on the substrate.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rotogravure printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the application of words, designs, and pictures to a substrate using a gravure cylinder by means of a roll printing
technique in which the pattern to be applied is recessed relative to the nonimage area.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rotogravure printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which each roll printer uses a roll with recessed areas for applying an image to a substrate.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Screen printing unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing unit in which the printing ink passes through a web or a fabric to which a refined form of stencil has
been applied. The stencil openings determine the form and dimensions of the imprint.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a substance that is liquid at standard conditions that is used to dissolve or dilute another substance; this
term includes, but is not limited to, organic materials used as dissolvers, viscosity reducers, degreasing agents,
or cleaning agents.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent cleaning 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the process of cleaning soils from surfaces by cold cleaning, open-top vapor degreasing, or conveyorized degreasing.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Space vehicle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any vehicle designed to travel beyond the earth's atmosphere.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Street 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a public road in a town or city.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Substrate 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the surface to which a coating is applied on, saturated into, or impregnated into.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vinyl coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more vinyl coating unit(s).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vinyl coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a web coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating or printing ink is applied onto
a continuous web of vinyl-coated fabric or vinyl sheets.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Web 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an automatic system which supplies substrate from a continuous roll or an extrusion process.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood furniture 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means room furnishings including cabinets (kitchen, bath, and vanity), tables, chairs, beds, sofas, shutters,
art objects, wood paneling, wood flooring, and any other coated furnishings made of wood, wood composition, or fabricated
wood materials.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood furniture coating facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that includes one or more wood furniture coating unit(s).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood furniture coating unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating unit in which any protective, decorative, or functional coating is applied onto wood furniture.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicability.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The requirements of paragraphs (b)(1)(iii) (A) and (B), (iv)(A), (v)(A), and (vi)(A) of this section shall apply
to any owner or operator of any degreasing facility or any motor vehicle or mobile equipment refinishing facility
located in the control area as defined in paragraph (a)(1) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The requirements of paragraphs (b)(1)(iii) (A) and (B), (iv)(A), (v)(A), and (vi)(A) of this section shall apply
to any owner or operator of an industrial or commercial solvent use facility located in the applicable area specified
in paragraph (b)(1)(ii)(A) of this section at which actual emissions of VOC are greater than or equal to 6.8 kg (15 lbs)
during any one day.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

