<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Baseline emissions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the emissions calculated using 1990 emission inventory data in the affected FIP areas and adjusted for emission
reductions projected to occur by the implementation year of the FIP cap program in the affected FIP area. The baseline
shall be denominated in pounds per year of FIP cap pollutant (e.g., pounds of NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 per year) and monthly caps shall be prorated based on this data. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cement kiln
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is a device for the calcining and clinkering of limestone, clay and other raw materials, and recycle dust in the dry-process
manufacture of cement. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Clinker
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is a mass of fused material produced in a cement kiln from which the finished cement is manufactured by milling and grinding.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Combustion equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is any equipment that burns fuel, including but not limited to natural gas or fuel oil in order to operate. Combustion
equipment includes, but is not limited to, boilers, turbines, heaters, engines, kilns, furnaces, ovens, dryers,
flares, and afterburners. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Continuous emissions monitoring system (CEMS) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any system of equipment that continuously measures all parameters necessary to directly determine mass emissions
of a pollutant, and which meets all performance standards for CEMS set forth in this regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Continuously measure 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means to measure at least once every 15 minutes except during periods of routine maintenance and calibration, or as
otherwise specified in this regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Daily 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means occurring once between 12 midnight and 24 hours later at midnight. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Day
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a period of consecutive 24 hours beginning at 12:00 a.m. (midnight) local time, or beginning at a time consistent
with a facility's operating schedule. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Direct monitoring device
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is a device that measures the emissions of NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and all other variables as specified in this regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Electric utility
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is all facilities which generate power and are owned or operated by any one of the following: Southern California Edison
or any of its successors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission rate
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the total mass of NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 released or discharged from an emissions source into the atmosphere per unit of production, throughput, or heat input
(e.g., pounds NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
/mmBtu). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission source
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
source
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any building, structure, facility, property, equipment, device, container, or any combination thereof,
at, from, or by reason which NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is emitted or discharged into the atmosphere. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Facility
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means all of the pollutant-emitting activities which belong to the same industrial grouping, are located on one or
more contiguous or adjacent properties, and are under the control of the same person (or persons under common control),
except the activities of any marine vessel. Pollutant-emitting activities shall be considered as part of the same
industrial grouping if they belong to the same ``Major Group'' (i.e., which have the same two-digit code) as described
in the ``Standard Industrial Classification Manual, 1987'' (incorporated by reference as specified in paragraph
(b) of this section). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Federally enforceable
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means all limitations and conditions that are enforceable by the Administrator including those requirements contained
in permits issued pursuant to 40 CFR parts 70 and 71, except those terms or conditions designated as not federally enforceable;
those requirements developed pursuant to 40 CFR parts 60 and 61; requirements within any applicable implementation
plan; and any permit requirements established pursuant to &sect;52.21 or under regulations approved pursuant to
40 CFR part 51, subpart I, and 40 CFR 51.166. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gaseous fuels
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 include, but are not limited to, any natural, process, synthetic, landfill, sewage digester or waste gases with a
gross heating value of 300 Btu per cubic foot or higher, at standard conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Incinerator
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a combustion apparatus in which solid, semi-solid, liquid, or gaseous combustible wastes are ignited and burned
and from which the solid and gaseous residues contain little or no combustible material. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Monitor
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means to measure and record. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Natural gas
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is a mixture of gaseous hydrocarbons, with at least 80 percent methane (by volume), and of pipeline quality, such as
the gas sold or distributed by any utility company regulated by the California Public Utilities Commission. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emissions means the sum of nitric oxides and nitrogen dioxides emitted, calculated as nitrogen dioxide. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-cap program pollutants
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are those pollutants other than NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 and VOC. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Owner or operator
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any person who owns, operates, leases, controls, or supervises an emissions source or air pollution control
equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Person
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any individual, corporation, copartnership, firm, company, partnership, joint stock company, trust, association,
State, municipality, political subdivision, or any other legal entity, or their legal representative, agent, or
assigns. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Process
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any stationary emission source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quarter
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is a three-month period from January 1 to March 31, April 1 to June 30, July 1 to September 30, or October 1 to December
31, inclusive. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rated brake horsepower (bhp)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is the maximum rating specified by the manufacturer and listed on the nameplate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rental equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is equipment which is rented or leased for operation by someone other than the owner of the equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Research operations
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are those operations the sole purpose of which is to permit investigation of experimental research to advance the
state of knowledge or state-of-the-art technology. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Source
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means emission source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standard conditions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a temperature of 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F) and a pressure of 760 mm Hg (29.92 in. Hg). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
