<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(i) This article shall not apply to any consumer product manufactured in California for shipment and use outside of
California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The provisions of this article shall not apply to a manufacturer or distributor who sells, supplies, or offers
for sale in California a consumer product that does not comply with the VOC standards specified in paragraphs (a)(3)(i)
or (a)(3)(viii) of this section, as long as the manufacturer or distributor can demonstrate both that the consumer
product is intended for shipment and use outside of California, and that the manufacturer or distributor has taken
reasonable prudent precautions to assure that the consumer product is not distributed to California. This paragraph
does not apply to consumer products that are sold, supplied, or offered for sale by any person to retail outlets in California.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to fragrances up to a combined level
of 2 percent by weight contained in any consumer product. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to any VOC which: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Has a vapor pressure of less than 0.1 mm Hg at 20 degrees Centigrade, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Consists of more than 12 carbon atoms, if the vapor pressure is unknown. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The requirements of paragraph (a)(6)(ii) of this section shall not apply to consumer products registered under
the Federal Insecticide, Fungicide, and Rodenticide Act, (FIFRA; 7 U.S.C. 136 et seq.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to air fresheners that are comprised
entirely of fragrance, less compounds not defined as VOCs under paragraph (a)(2) of this section or exempted under
paragraph (a)(4)(iv) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to air fresheners and insecticides
containing at least 98% paradichlorobenzene. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Existing personal fragrance products or personal fragrance products in development on or before April 1, 1992,
provided that both: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The registration data specified in paragraph (a)(7) of this section is submitted for every such product by the date
specified in paragraph (a)(7)(i) of this section, or prior to July 1, 1993, whichever date occurs later, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Such product is sold in California prior to January 1, 1994. For the purposes of this subsection, a product in development
means: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A product which a fragrance materials manufacturer is designing at the request of a personal fragrance product manufacturer,
or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A product which is the subject of a written marketing profile or other documentation authorizing the creation and
marketing of the product. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Personal fragrance products in development may be registered to qualify for this exemption under hypothetical
trade names or pseudonyms, provided that the actual trade name is supplied to the Administrator within 30 days of marketing
such products, or January 1, 1994, whichever occurs first. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ix) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to adhesives sold in containers of 1 fluid
ounce or less. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(x) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to any VOC which is a fragrance in a personal
fragrance product. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(xi) The requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section shall not apply to bait station insecticides. For the
purpose of this paragraph, bait station insecticides are containers enclosing an insecticidal bait that is not more
than 0.5 ounce by weight, where the bait is designed to be ingested by insects and is composed of solid material feeding
stimulants with less than 5 percent active ingredients. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(xii) The January 1, 1999 VOC limits specified in paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section for personal fragrance products
shall not apply to such products which have been sold in California prior to January 1, 1999. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Innovative Products.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
