<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(4) The requirements of paragraph (c)(3) of this section shall not apply to any aerosol coating product containing
methylene chloride, perchloroethylene, or an ozone depleting substance as identified in paragraph (c)(3) of this
section that are present as impurities in a combined amount equal to or less than 0.01% by weight of the product. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) No person shall sell, supply, offer for sale, apply, or manufacture for sale in California: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Any multi-component kit as defined in paragraph (b) of this section, unless the total VOC emitted from the use of
that multi-component kit does not exceed the VOC which would be allowed from a single-component product in the same
product category listed in the Table of Standards; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any aerosol coating product assembled by adding bulk paint to aerosol containers of propellant and solvent,
unless such products comply with the standards specified in paragraph (c)(1) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) Any manufacturer of an aerosol coating product subject to this article shall submit the following information
by March 31, 1998 to EPA: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The information required under paragraphs (e)(3)(ii) (A) through (G) and (e)(c)(3) of this section for the 1997
calendar year; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
