<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Graphic arts coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (Sign Paints) are coatings formulated for and hand-applied by artists using brush or roller techniques to indoor
and outdoor signs (excluding structural components) and murals, including lettering enamels, poster colors, copy
blockers, and bulletin enamels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
High-temperature industrial maintenance coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are industrial maintenance coatings formulated for and applied to substrates exposed continuously or intermittently
to temperatures above 400 degrees Fahrenheit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Impact immersion coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are an industrial maintenance, vinyl chloride based multicoat system formulated and recommended for application
to submerged surfaces of locks, dams and other steel structures subjected to frequent severe abrasion. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Industrial maintenance anti-graffiti coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are two-component clear industrial maintenance coatings formulated for and applied to exterior walls and murals
to resist repeated scrubbing and exposure to harsh solvents. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Industrial maintenance coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are high performance coatings formulated for and applied to substrates in industrial, commercial, or institutional
situations that are exposed to one or more of the following extreme environmental conditions: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) immersion in water, wastewater, or chemical solutions (aqueous and non-aqueous solutions), or chronic exposure
of interior surfaces to moisture condensation; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) acute or chronic exposure to corrosive, caustic or acidic agents, or to chemicals, chemical fumes, chemical mixtures,
or solutions; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) repeated exposure to temperatures in excess of 250 degrees Fahrenheit; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) repeated heavy abrasion, including mechanical wear and repeated scrubbing with industrial solvents, cleaners,
or scouring agents; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) exterior exposure of metal structures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Industrial maintenance coatings are not for residential use or for use in areas of industrial, commercial, or institutional
facilities such as office space and meeting rooms. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Lacquers
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are clear wood finishes, including clear lacquer sanding sealers, formulated with nitrocellulose or synthetic
resins to dry by evaporation without chemical reaction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Low-solids stain
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a wood stain containing 1 pound or less of solids per gallon of material. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Magnesite cement coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings formulated for and applied to magnesite cement decking to protect the magnesite cement substrate from
erosion by water. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
