<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00354 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Mastic coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings formulated to cover holes and minor cracks and to conceal surface irregularities, and applied in a thickness
of at least 10 mils (dry, single coat). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metallic pigmented coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings containing at least 0.4 pound of elemental metallic pigment per gallon (50 grams/liter of coating as
applied) or non-bituminous coatings which are formulated with metalic pigment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Multi-colored coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings which exhibit more than one color when applied and which are packaged in a single container and applied
in a single coat. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-flat coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings which register gloss of 15 or greater on an 85
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir; meter or five or greater on a 60
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir; meter, and which are identified on the label as a gloss, semigloss, or eggshell enamel coating. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-flat high gloss coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings which register gloss of 70 or greater on a 60
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir; meter, and which are identified on the label as a high gloss enamel coating. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
NOS
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means not otherwise specified. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Nuclear power plant coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are industrial maintenance coatings formulated and certified by the US Department of Energy for application to Level
1 containment structures at nuclear power facilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Opaque stains
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are all stains that are not classified as semitransparent stains. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Opaque wood preservatives
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are all wood preservatives not classified as clear or semitransparent wood preservatives or as below-ground wood
preservatives. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pre-treatment wash primers
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings which contain a minimum of 1/2 percent acid by weight, applied directly to bare metal surfaces to provide
necessary surface etching. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Primers
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings applied to a surface to provide a firm bond between the substrate and subsequent coats. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Residential use
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is use in areas where people reside or lodge including, but not limited to single and multiple family dwellings, condominiums,
mobile homes, apartment complexes, motels, and hotels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Roof coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings formulated for application to exterior roofs and for the primary purpose of preventing penetration
of the substrate by water, or reflecting heat and reflecting ultraviolet radiation. Metallic pigmented roof coatings
which qualify as metallic pigmented coatings shall not be considered to be in this category, but shall be considered
to be in the metallic pigmented coatings category. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Sanding sealers
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are clear wood coatings formulated for and applied to bare wood for sanding and to seal the wood for subsequent application
of varnish. To be considered a sanding sealer a coating must be clearly labelled as such. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Sealers
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings applied to substrates to prevent subsequent coatings from being absorbed by the substrate, or to prevent
harm to subsequent coatings by materials in the substrate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Semitransparent stains
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings which are formulated to change the color of a surface but not conceal the surface. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Semitransparent wood preservative
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are wood preservative stains formulated to protect exposed wood from decay or insect attack by the addition of a wood
preservative registered with the USEPA, Office of Pesticide Programs, and which change the color of a surface but
do not conceal the surface, including clear wood preservatives. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Shellacs
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are clear or pigmented coatings formulated solely with the resinous secretions of the lac beetle (laccifer lacca),
thinned with alcohol, and formulated to dry by evaporation without a chemical reaction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solicit
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is to require for use or to specify, by written or oral contract. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solventborne
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a coating that contains only organic solvents. If water is present, the coating must contain less than or equal
to five percent water by weight in its volatile fraction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Specialty primers, sealers, and undercoaters
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means primers, sealers, and undercoaters used only to perform one of the following functions: repair fire, smoke
or water damage; neutralize odor; block strains; block efflorescence; condition chalky surfaces; or coat accoustical
materials without affecting their accoustical abilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00355 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Swimming pool coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings specifically formulated to coat the interior of swimming pools and to resist swimming pool chemicals.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Swimming pool repair coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are chlorinated rubber based coatings used for the repair and maintenance of swimming pools over existing chlorinated
rubber based coatings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Tint base
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is an architectural coating to which colorants are added. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Traffic coatings
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings formulated for and applied to public streets, highways, and other surfaces including, but not limited
to curbs, berms, driveways, and parking lots. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Undercoaters
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are coatings formulated and applied to substrates to provide a smooth surface for subsequent coats. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Varnishes
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are clear wood finishes formulated with various resins to dry by chemical reaction on exposure to air. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Waterborne coating
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a coating that contains more than five percent water by weight in its volatile fraction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Waterproofing sealers
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are colorless coatings which are formulated for the sole purpose of preventing penetration of porous substrates
by water and which do not alter surface appearance or texture. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirements
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Except as provided in paragraphs (c)(2), (c)(3), (c)(4) and (c)(5) of this section, no person shall manufacture,
supply, sell, offer for sale, blend, repackage, apply, or solicit the application for use within California any architectural
coating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which contains more than 250 grams of volatile organic compounds per liter of coating (excluding water and exempt
solvents, and any colorant added to tint bases). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Except as provided in paragraphs (c)(3), (c)(4) and (c)(5) of this section, no person shall manufacture, supply,
sell, offer for sale, blend, repackage, apply, or solicit the application for use within California any architectural
coating listed in the Table of Standards which contains volatile organic compounds (less water and exempt solvents,
and excluding any colorant added to tint bases) in excess of the corresponding limit and date specified in the table.

