<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Structural pesticide 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a pesticide intended for use in the protection of structures, buildings or building materials, including but
not limited to fumigants, termiticides, and wood preservatives. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Volatile organic vompound 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(VOC) means any compound of carbon excluding carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, carbonic acid, metallic carbides
or carbonates, and ammonium carbonate, which participates in atmospheric photochemical reactions other than those
defined as exempt compounds. These exempt compounds have been determined to have negligible photochemical reactivity.
For purposes of determining compliance with this section, VOC will be measured by test methods given in this section.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Specific provisions. (1) Required submission of data. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) By June 1, 1996 or 120 (one hundred and twenty) days after the effective date of this section, whichever is later,
all persons who produce agricultural and/or structural pesticides that are registered in California must submit
reports in accordance with paragraph (d) of this section that identify the VOC content of each pesticide. The VOC content
will be determined according to the methodology provided in paragraph (f) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) If EPA determines that a report does not affirmatively demonstrate compliance with the methodology in paragraph
(f) of this section, EPA may assign the pesticide a VOC content value equal to the highest VOC content reported for any
pesticide. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Establish VOC limit. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Upon compilation of the data received pursuant to paragraph (c)(1) of this section, EPA will determine a pesticide
VOC limit based on the following criteria: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) EPA will establish a base-year inventory for each registered pesticide. This inventory will be based on the amount
of each pesticide used in the affected area. These amounts will be based on data from the 1990 pesticide use report (PUR)
and the inerts database, which are both maintained by the California Department of Pesticide Regulation (DPR), unless
EPA determines that another year or years of PUR data or other information provides a more appropriate basis for the
inventory. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) EPA will rank all registered pesticides according to their VOC content as determined by the data submitted pursuant
to paragraph (c)(1) of this section. The pesticide with the largest VOC content will be ranked ``1''. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00360 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iii) EPA will multiply the VOC contents (as determined by paragraph (c)(1) of this section) by the inventory (as determined
in paragraph (c)(2)(i) of this section) to determine ``individual base-year VOC emissions'' for each individual
pesticide. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) EPA will add the individual base-year VOC emissions for all pesticides to determine the ``total base-year VOC
emissions'' from all pesticides combined. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Starting with the pesticide or pesticides ranked ``1'' according to paragraph (c)(2)(ii) of this section, EPA
will add the individual base-year VOC emissions for pesticides ranked 2, 3, 4 *&blank;*&blank;* etc, until the sum
equals forty to seventy percent (40%&hyph;70%)
<FOOTCITE>31</FOOTCITE>
 of the total base-year VOC emissions. The VOC content of the last pesticide needed to achieve 40%&hyph;70% of the total
base-year VOC emissions becomes the ``VOC limit.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
31
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
As discussed further in the preamble to the proposed regulations, the range of 40% to 70% reflects the target range
of 20%&hyph;45% reductions in emissions from pesticide application. This range was selected for consistency with
the VOC cap rules proposed as 40 CFR 52.2952 through 52.2954. Based on planned modeling and inventory analysis and
comments received during the comment period, EPA hopes to select a specific reduction target from within this range
for use in the final rule.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(vi) EPA will promulgate the VOC limit with a summary of the assumptions and results from paragraphs (c)(2) (i) through
(v) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Restrictions on pesticides. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) On and after 1 (one) year after EPA publishes the VOC limit, all persons are prohibited from distribution within
the affected area of pesticides with VOC contents in excess of the VOC limit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) On and after 2 (two) years after EPA publishes the VOC limit, all persons are prohibited from application and/or
storage within the affected area of pesticides with VOC contents in excess of the VOC limit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Revisions to the VOC limit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) EPA may, at any time, require producer(s) to reanalyze their pesticides according to the methodology described
in paragraph (f) of this section and to submit the new data according to paragraph (d) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) EPA may, at any time, revise the VOC limit consistent with the methodology described in paragraph (c)(2) of this
section and based on information submitted pursuant to paragraph (c)(4)(i) of this section or elsewhere. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) Reporting. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Producers. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Reports submitted pursuant to paragraphs (c)(1)(i) and (c)(4)(i) of this section must include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Name, address, name of contact person, and telephone number of producer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Name and description of pesticide product, including a copy of the pesticide product label. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Name, address and telephone number of the laboratory performing analysis; name of analyst; and date and time
of analysis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) All raw data collected during analysis performed pursuant to paragraph (f) of this section. If, for example,
TGA analysis is performed as described in paragraph (f)(1)(i) of this section, all thermograms produced must be submitted,
as well as justification for rejecting any unacceptable thermogram. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Summary and results of analysis performed pursuant to paragraph (f) of this section. If, for example, TGA analysis
is performed, the summary of analysis shall include uncorrected weight percent VOC content (i.e., kg VOC per kg pesticide),
weight percent water content, weight percent exempt solvents content, and weight percent VOC content corrected
for water and exempt solvents, as applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Certification signed and dated by a responsible official of the producer stating the following:
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=21 g=1 f=1 -->
I certify under penalty of law that this document and all attachments were prepared under my direction or supervision
in accordance with a system designed to assure that qualified personnel properly gather and evaluate the information
submitted. Based on my inquiry of the person or persons who manage the system, or those persons directly responsible
for gathering the information, the information submitted is, to the best of my knowledge and belief, true, accurate,
and complete. I am aware that there are significant penalties for submitting false information, including the possibility
of fine and imprisonment for knowing violations.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 04 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Distributors. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any person who distributes pesticides within the affected area must report the following information to EPA: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Distributor notification. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The distributor notification shall include the name, address, and telephone number of the distributor, and the name
of a responsible official of the distributor. The report shall be postmarked not later than the date the VOC limit becomes
effective (see paragraph (c)(3)(i) of this section) or 30 days after the distributor first begins distribution of
pesticides, whichever is later. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Annual report. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The annual report shall specify the type and amount of each pesticide sold, shipped, or otherwise distributed in the
affected area. The annual report shall be submitted by January 30 of each year for the preceding year's data beginning
with the year in which the effective date specified in paragraph (c)(3)(i) of this section occurs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicators. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All applicators within the affected areas shall submit a copy of all PURs to EPA at the same time the PUR is submitted
to DPR once the effective date specified in paragraph (c)(4)(ii) of this section occurs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recordkeeping. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All producers, distributors, and applicators must maintain all information necessary to demonstrate compliance
with this section for a period of five (5) years. This information includes, but is not limited to, copies of all reports
required in paragraph (d) of this section, and any technical support to those reports. Copies of this information
must be provided to EPA upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00361 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test methods.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) For the purposes of this section, the VOC content in pesticides shall be determined by the methods described in
paragraphs (f)(1) (i) or (ii) of this section or by methods as stringent in accuracy, reliability, reproducibility,
and frequency and approved by EPA.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Thermogravimetric Analysis (TGA). The ``American Standard Test Method (ASTM) for Compositional Analysis by
Thermogravimetry'' (ASTM E&hyph;1131&hyph;86) as modified in EPA's alternative control technology document
(ACT) for pesticides (``Alternative Control Technology Document; Control of VOC Emissions from the Application
of Agricultural Pesticides,'' EPA&hyph;453/R&hyph;92&hyph;011, March 1993, appendix C); or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Volatile Organics in Pesticides (VOP). The purge and trap procedure as described in EPA's ACT (EPA&hyph;453/R&hyph;92&hyph;011,
appendix C).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The exempt compound content of a pesticide may be determined by the statement of formulation required pursuant
to FIFRA (7 U.S.C. 136a(c)(1)(E)).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Pesticides that are diluted with VOC-containing material (e.g., gasoline, xylene, toluene, and other solvents),
at any point before application, are to be tested diluted with said material at the average dilution used during application.
Pesticides that are diluted with non-VOC-containing materials (e.g., water) are to be tested as sold rather than
as applied.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=3 -->
&sect;52.2961 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=3 -->
Stationary and area source rules.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(a) Solvent Cleaning Operations.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Purpose and Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The purpose of this section is to reduce emissions of volatile organic compounds (VOC) from solvent cleaning operations,
and from the storage and disposal of materials used in solvent cleaning operations. This section applies to any facility
located in the affected area that uses VOC-containing materials in the production, repair, maintenance, or servicing
of parts, products, tools, machinery, equipment, or general work areas, or that stores and/or disposes of VOC-containing
materials used in solvent cleaning operations. For the purposes of this section, the affected area includes the Ventura
County Area for ozone and the Sacramento Metro Area for ozone as described in 40 CFR 81.305.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraph (a) of this section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not defined herein
shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aerosol product 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a hand-held, nonrefillable container which expels pressurized product ingredients by means of a propellant-induced
force.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Application line 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means that portion of a motor vehicle assembly production line which applies surface and other coatings to motor vehicle
bodies, hoods, fenders, cargo boxes, doors, and grill opening panels.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Appurtenances 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means accessories to an architectural structure, including, but not limited to: hand railings, cabinets, bathroom
and kitchen fixtures, fences, rain-gutters and down-spouts, window screens, lamp-posts, heating and air conditioning
equipment, other mechanical equipment, and large fixed stationary tools and concrete forms.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Architectural coatings 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any coatings applied to stationary structures and their appurtenances, to mobile homes, to pavements, or to
curbs.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Closed container 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a container that encloses greater than 90% of the liquid surface area, except when depositing and removing objects
to be cleaned or for maintenance and repair to the container itself.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cured coatings, cured inks, and cured adhesives 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means coatings, inks, and adhesives which are dry to the touch.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Electronic components 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means circuit card assemblies, printed wire assemblies, printing wiring boards, soldered joints, ground wires,
bus bars, and other electrical fixtures, except for the actual cabinet in which the components are housed.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Flexographic printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a printing method utilizing flexible rubber or other elastomeric plate which employs rapid-drying liquid
inks.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Grams of VOC per liter of material 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the weight of VOC per volume of material and can be calculated by the following equation:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->

<!-- PJG STAG 4725 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<IMPORT>

<!-- PJG importformat s,w220,d29 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
E:GRAPHICSEP05MY94.094
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</IMPORT>

<!-- PJG /STAG -->

<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
Where:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
W
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
s
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
=weight of volatile compounds in grams;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
W
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
w
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
=weight of water in grams;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
W
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
es
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
=weight of exempt compounds in grams; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
V
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=5 f=2 -->
m
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=16 g=1 f=1 -->
=volume of material in liters.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Graphic arts 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means all screen, gravure, letterpress, flexographic, and lithographic printing processes.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gravure printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an intaglio process in which the ink is carried in minute etched or engraved wells on a roll or cylinder. The excess
ink is removed from the surface by a doctor blade.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Institutions 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
mean, but are not limited to, schools, hospitals, sanitariums, prisons, health clubs, and theaters.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Janitorial cleaning 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the cleaning of building or facility components, such as the floor, ceiling, walls, windows, doors, stairs,
bathrooms, etc.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Letterpress printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the method in which the image area is raised relative to the nonimage area and the ink is transferred to the paper
directly from the image surface.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Lithographic printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a plane-o-graphic method in which the image and nonimage areas are on the same plane.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Liquid leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a visible liquid solvent leak from a container at a rate of more than three drops per minute, or a visible liquid
mist.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Maintenance cleaning 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a solvent cleaning operation carried out to keep parts, products, tools, machinery, equipment, or general
work areas in clean and good operational condition.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00362 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Manufacturing process 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the process of making goods or articles by hand or by machinery.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Medical equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means equipment used by physicians to cure diseases or conditions requiring surgical procedures that are implanted
in the body or used during invasive medical procedures. Medical equipment includes, but is not limited to, heart valves,
catheters, oxygenenators, pressure monitors, pharmaceutical and dental equipment.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-absorbent containers 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
mean containers made of nonporous material which do not allow the migration of the liquid solvent through them.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-atomized solvent flow 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the use of a solvent to remove uncured adhesives, uncured inks, uncured coatings, and contaminants from an article
in the form of a liquid stream without atomization.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-leaking containers 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
mean containers without liquid leaks.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any operation that imparts color, design, alphabet, or numerals on a substrate.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Remote reservoir cold cleaner 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a cleaning device in which liquid solvent is pumped from a solvent container to a sink-like work area and the solvent
from the sink-like area drains into an enclosed solvent container while parts are being cleaned.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repair cleaning 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a solvent cleaning operation carried out during a repair process.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repair process 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the process of returning a damaged object or an object not operating properly to good condition.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Screen printing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a process in which the printing ink passes through a web or a fabric to which a refined form of stencil has been applied.
The stencil openings determine the form and dimensions of the imprint.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a VOC-containing liquid used to perform solvent cleaning operations.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent cleaning operation 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the removal of loosely held uncured adhesives, uncured inks, uncured coatings, and contaminants which include,
but are not limited to, dirt, soil, and grease from parts, products, tools, machinery, equipment, and general work
areas. Each distinct method of cleaning in a cleaning process which consists of a series of cleaning methods shall
constitute a separate solvent cleaning operation.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent container 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means that part of a cleaning device that holds the solvent.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent flushing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the use of a solvent to remove uncured adhesives, uncured inks, uncured coatings, or contaminants from the internal
surfaces and passages of the equipment by flushing solvent through the equipment.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stripping 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the removal of cured coatings, cured inks, and cured adhesives.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Surface preparation 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the removal of contaminants such as dust, soil, oil, grease, etc., prior to coating, adhesive, or ink applications.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Ultraviolet inks 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
mean inks which dry by polymerization reaction induced by ultraviolet energy.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
VOC composite partial pressure 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the following:
