<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Solvent requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
On and after January 1, 1996, a person shall not use a solvent to perform solvent cleaning operations, including the
use of cleaning devices or methods, unless the solvent complies with the applicable requirements set forth below.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Substrate cleaning during manufacturing processes, and surface preparation for coating, adhesive, or ink applications.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The solvents used on substrates for cleaning during the manufacturing process or for surface preparation prior to
coating, adhesive, or ink applications shall have a VOC content of 70 grams or less of VOC per liter of material. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repair and maintenance cleaning. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The solvents used for repair or maintenance cleaning shall have a VOC content of 900 grams or less of VOC per liter of
material and a VOC composite partial pressure of 20 mm Hg or less at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cleaning of coatings and adhesives application equipment.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The solvents used for cleaning coatings or adhesives application equipment shall have a VOC content of 950 grams or
less of VOC per liter of material and a VOC composite partial pressure of 35 mm Hg or less at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cleaning of polyester resin application equipment.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The solvents used for cleaning polyester resin application equipment shall comply with one of the limits specified
below: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The solvent shall have a VOC content of 200 grams or less of VOC per liter of material; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The solvent shall have a VOC content of 1,100 grams or less of VOC per liter of material and a VOC composite partial pressure
of 1.0 mm Hg or less at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cleaning of ink application equipment.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The solvents used for cleaning of ink application equipment in graphic arts shall meet the limits specified below.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The solvents used in screen printing shall have a VOC content of 1,070 grams or less of VOC per liter of material and
a VOC composite partial pressure of 5 mm Hg or less at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The solvents used in lithographic and letterpress printing not subject to provisions of paragraph (a)(3)(i)(E)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section shall have a VOC content of 800 grams or less of VOC per liter of material and a VOC composite partial
pressure of 25 mm Hg or less at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The solvents used in gravure printing, flexographic printing, and printing operations not subject to provisions
of paragraphs (a)(3)(i)(E)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
), (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
), or (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section shall have a VOC content of 100 grams or less of VOC per liter of material and a VOC composite partial
pressure of 3 mm Hg at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The solvents used to remove ultraviolet inks from application equipment in graphic arts printing operations, except
screen printing, shall have a VOC content of 800 grams or less of VOC per liter of material and a VOC composite partial
pressure of 33 mm Hg or less at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cleaning of electronic components and medical equipment.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The solvents used for manufacturing or maintenance cleaning of electronic components or medical equipment shall
have a VOC content of 900 grams or less of VOC per liter of material and a VOC composite partial pressure of 33 mm Hg or less
at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cleaning devices and methods requirements
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. On and after January 1, 1996, a person shall not perform solvent cleaning operations unless one of the following cleaning
devices or methods is used: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Wipe cleaning; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Spray bottles or closed containers from which solvents are applied without a propellant-induced force; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Cleaning equipment using solvent within a closed container, except when depositing and removing objects to be
cleaned, or for maintenance and repair to the cleaning equipment itself. This includes but is not limited to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any cleaning device or mechanism which has been determined by EPA to result in equivalent or lower emissions; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any remote reservoir cold cleaner used pursuant to the provisions of paragraph (a)(3)(iii) of this section; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Non-atomized solvent flow method where the cleaning solvent is collected in a closed container; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Solvent flushing method where the cleaning solvent is discharged into a container. The discharged solvent from
the equipment must be collected into containers without atomizing into the open air. The solvent may be flushed through
the system by air or hydraulic pressure, or by pumping. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Remote reservoir cold cleaners.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 On and after January 1, 1996, any person owning or operating a remote reservoir cold cleaner shall comply with all of
the following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Prevent solvent vapors from escaping from the solvent container by using such devices as a cover or a valve when
the remote reservoir is not being used, cleaned, or repaired; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Direct solvent flow in a manner that will prevent liquid solvent from splashing outside of the remote reservoir
cold cleaner; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Not degrease porous or absorbent materials, such as cloth, leather, wood, or rope; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Use only solvent containers free of all liquid leaks. Auxiliary equipment, such as pumps, pipelines, or flanges,
shall not have any liquid leaks, visible tears, or cracks. Any liquid leak, visible tear, or crack detected shall be
repaired within one calendar day, or the leaking section of the remote reservoir cold cleaner shall be drained of all
solvent and shut down until it is replaced or repaired. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Storage and disposal. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) All VOC-containing solvents shall be stored in non-absorbent, non-leaking containers which shall be kept closed
at all times except when filling or emptying. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) All waste solvent and waste solvent residues shall be disposed of by at least one of the following methods: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Disposal through a commercial reclamation service; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Disposal at a facility that is federally or state licensed to treat, store or dispose of such waste; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Disposal by recycling in conformance with &sect;25143.2 of the California Health and Safety Code. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission control system. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In lieu of complying with the requirements in paragraphs (a)(3)(i), (a)(3)(ii), (a)(3)(v)(A) of this section, a
person may comply by using an emission control system in association with the solvent cleaning operation regulated
by this section provided: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The emission control system maintains a capture efficiency of at least 90%, by weight, of the emissions generated
by the solvent cleaning operation and a destruction or removal efficiency of at least 95% by weight; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The emission control system maintains a capture efficiency of at least 90%, by weight, of the emissions generated
by the solvent cleaning operation and the output of the control system is less than 50 parts per million (ppm) calculated
as carbon with no dilution; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The emission control system meets the requirements of an applicable source-specific section of the Federal or
federally approved State Implementation Plan. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
