<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All information needed to demonstrate continuous 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with paragraph (a)(3)(v) of this section, such as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
temperatures, pressures, and flowrates; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Maintain records of the daily volume of each VOC-containing solvent subject to abatement by add-on control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Maintain records sufficient to demonstrate compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with paragraph (a)(3)(iv)(B) of this section including, but not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Date; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Source of waste (e.g., ``waste solvent from cold 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cleaner''); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Description of waste (e.g., ``rags in two 55 gallon 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
drums with 5&hyph;10% liquid''); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Amount of solvent in waste shipment; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Destination of each shipment of waste solvent and/or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
waste solvent residues off-site. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) All records shall be maintained for at least five years 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and shall be provided to EPA upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purpose of this section, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following test methods shall be used. VOC emissions or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
parameters determined to exceed any limits established by this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section through the use of any of the following test methods shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
constitute a violation of the section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The VOC content of materials subject to the provisions of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section shall be determined by EPA Method 24 (40 CFR part 60, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The efficiency of the collection device of the emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control system, as specified in paragraph (b)(3)(v)(A) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, shall be determined by the EPA method described at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.741(a)(4)(iii). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The efficiency of the control device of the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control system, as specified in paragraph (b)(3)(v)(B) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, shall be determined by the EPA method described at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.741(a)(4)(iv). The VOC content measured and calculated as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
carbon in the control device exhaust gases shall be determined by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA Method 25 or 25A (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The identity of components in solvents shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by EPA Method 18 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Vapor pressure of a VOC shall be determined by ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Method D2879&hyph;86 or may be obtained from a published source such as: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Boublik, T., V. Fried and E. Hala, ``The Vapor Pressure of Pure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Substances,'' Elsevier Scientific Publishing Co., New York (1973); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Perry's Chemical Engineer's Handbook, McGraw-Hill Book Company 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1984); CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, Chemical Rubber 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Publishing Company (1986&hyph;87); and Lange's Handbook of Chemistry, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
John A. Dean, editor, McGraw-Hill Book Company (1985). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood Products Coatings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This section applies to all persons 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applying coating, inks, stains, and/or strippers in wood product 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coating operations for the purpose of manufacture of wood products, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
including furniture and other coated objects made of solid wood 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and/or wood composition, and/or simulated wood material. This 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section shall not apply to residential noncommercial operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For the purposes of this section, the affected area is the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento Metro Area for ozone and the Ventura County Area for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ozone as described in &sect;81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraph (b) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aerosol-spray coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating which is sold in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hand-held, pressurized, non-refillable container of sixteen ounces 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or less and which is expelled from the container in a finely 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
divided spray when a valve on the container is depressed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Binders 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means non-volatile polymeric organic materials 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(resins) which form the surface film in coating applications. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Clean topcoat 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a final coating which contains binders, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
but not opaque pigments, and is specifically formulated to form a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transparent or translucent solid protective film. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a material which is applied to a surface and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which forms a film in order to beautify and/or protect such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surface. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Dip coat 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means to dip an object into a vat of coating material 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and drain off any excess coating. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Electrostatic application 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means charging of atomized paint 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
droplets for deposition by electrostatic attraction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
