<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(B) Emission control system.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A person or facility may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comply with the provisions of paragraph (b)(3)(i)(A) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section by using an emission control system, provided that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this system maintains a control efficiency (capture efficiency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
times destruction or removal efficiency) of the VOC emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of at least 85 (eighty-five) percent by weight. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transfer Efficiency.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A person or facility shall not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply a coating subject to this section except by means of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following application methods: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Electrostatic spray application; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Flow coat application; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Dip coat application; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Hand application methods; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) High-volume low-pressure (HVLP) spray application; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) Other coating application methods that are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrated to have a transfer efficiency at least equal to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
HVLP in the application, and which are used in such a manner 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that parameters under which they were tested are permanent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
features of the method. Such coating application methods 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be approved in writing by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Solvent cleaning operations; storage and disposal of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VOC-containing materials.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Cleanup solvents used for surface 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
preparation, equipment cleanup, and thinning operations, including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
storage and disposal of VOC-containing materials, shall be subject 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the provisions and requirements of &sect;52.2961(a), Solvent cleaning 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Prohibition of specifications.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A person shall not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specify the use in the affected area of any coating to be applied 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to any wood products subject to the provisions of this section that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
does not meet the limits and requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The requirements of this paragraph shall apply to all written or oral 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contracts. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The provisions of paragraphs (b)(3) (i) and (ii) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section shall not apply to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Aerosol-spray coatings for touch up and repair; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Facilities that use less than 1 gallon per day of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coating subject to this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The provisions of this section shall not apply to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coating operations for the purpose of manufacturing a finished wood 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
panel intended for attachment to the inside walls of buildings, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
including, but not limited to, homes and office buildings, mobile 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
homes, trailers, prefabricated buildings and similar structures, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
boats, and ships; or a finished exterior wood siding intended for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
use in construction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting and Recordkeeping.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Any source within the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
affected area that uses greater than 1 gallon of wood product 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coating materials (coatings, inks, fillers, stains, strippers, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
toners, washcoats, or solvents) per day shall comply with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Maintain a current file of each wood product coating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
material in use and storage. This file shall provide all of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
data necessary to evaluate compliance and shall include, but not be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited to, the following information, as applicable: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A data sheet or material list giving material name, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer identification, and material application; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
