<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(B) Any catalysts, reducers, or other components used 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and the mix ratio; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The VOC content limit from paragraph (b)(3) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section and the actual VOC content, as applied, or vapor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressure of the wood product coating material. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Maintain records of the monthly volume (e.g., gallons) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of each wood product coating material. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Control equipment records. Any person using an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission control system as a means of complying with this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall maintain daily records of key system operating and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintenance procedures which will demonstrate continuous operation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and compliance of the emission control device during periods of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission producing activities. Key system operating parameters are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
those necessary to ensure compliance with the requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (b)(3)(i)(B) of this section such as temperatures, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressures, and flowrates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) All records shall be maintained for at least five years 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and shall be made available to EPA upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Determination of VOC content. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The VOC content of coatings and strippers shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by using EPA Method 24 (40 CFR part 60, appendix 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The exempt compound content of coatings and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
strippers shall be determined by ASTM Method D&hyph;4457&hyph;85, which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is limited to the measurement of dichloromethane and 1,1,1- 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
trichloroethane only. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The VOC content of emissions shall be determined by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA Method 18 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Equipment test methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Capture efficiency.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The efficiency of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
collection device of the emission control system, as specified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in paragraph (b)(3)(i)(B) of this section, shall be determined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the EPA method described at &sect;52.741(a)(4)(iii). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Destruction or removal efficiency.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The efficiency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the control device of the emission control system, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in paragraph (b)(3)(i)(B) of this section, shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by the EPA method described at &sect;52.741(a)(4)(iv). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The VOC content measured and calculated as carbon in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control device exhaust gases shall be determined by EPA Method 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
25 or Method 25A (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transfer efficiency.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The transfer efficiency for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other coating application methods, as defined in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b)(3)(ii)(6) of this section, shall be determined in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with South Coast Air Quality Management District 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(SCAQMD) method ``Spray Equipment Transfer Efficiency Test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Procedure for Equipment User, May 24, 1989.'' This transfer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
efficiency (TE) test method is approved only for the limited 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purpose of comparing alternative application technologies 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under controlled conditions. The results of these tests are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
not transferable to a production setting. The test method is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
not acceptable for determining TE to establish VOC emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction credits to allow the use of higher VOC coatings, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to establish VOC credits for trading or offset purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Automotive refinishing operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 This section applies to all coating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operations of Group I vehicles and Group II vehicles and equipment, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as described in paragraph (c)(2) of this section, or their existing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
parts and components, for the purpose of on-site refinishing and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
modification except Original Equipment Manufacturer (OEM) coatings 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied at manufacturing plants. Facilities with coating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operations considered within the scope of this section include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
autobody repair/paint shops, production autobody paint shops, new 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
car dealer repair/paint shops, fleet operator repair/paint shops, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
custom-made car fabrication facilities, and truck body-builders. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For the purposes of this section, the affected area is the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento Metro Area for ozone as described in 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of paragraph (c) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Acrylic enamel
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an enamel coating derived from an acrylic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
polymer containing hydroxyl functionality. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
