<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Adhesion promoter 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating applied over both an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
existing non-sanded topcoat and the coated area immediately 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjacent to the non-sanded topcoat, to promote the adhesion of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subsequent topcoat. No topcoat, primer, primer sealer, or primer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surfacer shall be classified as an adhesion promoter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Alkyd enamel 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an enamel coating derived from any of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
several different synthetic resins made by heating together a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
polybasic acid, such as phthalic or maleic acid, and a polyhydric 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
alcohol, such as glycerin or a glycol. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Anti-glare safety coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating formulated to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
eliminate glare for safety purposes on interior surfaces of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle and which shows a reflectance of 25 or less on a 60
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir; gloss 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
meter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Basecoat 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a pigmented topcoat which is the first topcoat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied as part of a multistage topcoat system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Basecoat/clearcoat topcoat system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a topcoat system 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
composed of a basecoat portion and a clearcoat portion. The VOC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
content of a basecoat/clearcoat topcoat system shall be calculated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
according to the following formula: 
