<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Group I vehicles 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
mean passenger cars, small-sized trucks and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vans, medium-sized trucks and vans, motor homes, and motorcycles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Group II vehicles and equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
mean large-sized trucks, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
buses, street and mobile equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
High-volume, low-pressure (HVLP) spray 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means equipment used 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to spray a coating by means of a gun that operates between 0.1 and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
10 pounds per square inch gauge (psig) air pressure. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Highway 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a way or place of whatever nature, publicly 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintained and open to the public for purposes of vehicular travel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Highway includes street. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Impact-resistant coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any coating applied to a rocker 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
panel for the purpose of chip resistance to road debris. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Lacquer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating which dries primarily by solvent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evaporation and, hence, is resoluble in its original solvent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Metallic/iridescent topcoat 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a topcoat which contains 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
iridescent particles, composed of either metal as metallic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
particles or silicon as mica particles, in excess of 5 g/L (0.042 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lb/gal) as applied, where such particles are visible in the dried 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
film. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Midcoat 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a semi-transparent topcoat which is the middle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
topcoat applied as part of a three-stage topcoat system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Mobile equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means self-propelled equipment which is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
physically capable of being driven on a highway. Mobile equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
includes, but is not limited to, the following: truck bodies, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
truck trailers, utility bodies, camper shells, and miscellaneous 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hauling equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor home 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any motor vehicle originally designed, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanently altered, and equipped for human habitation as defined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in Section 362 of the California Vehicle Code. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a vehicle which is self-propelled and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which is physically capable of being driven on a highway. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

