<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Water hold-out coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating applied to the interior cavity areas of doors, quarterpanels, and rocker panels for the purpose of
corrosion resistance to prolonged water exposure.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Weld-thru coating 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating applied to metal immediately prior to welding to provide corrosion resistance.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) VOC content of coatings. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
On and after January 1, 1996, a person shall not apply a coating to Group I vehicles and Group II vehicles and equipment,
or their existing parts and components, which has a VOC content which exceeds the limits contained in paragraphs (c)(3)(i)
(A) and (B) of this section. Compliance with the VOC limits shall be based on VOC content, including any VOC material
added to the original coating supplied by the manufacturer, less water and exempt solvent, as applied to the vehicle,
mobile equipment, or parts and components.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Group I vehicles. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A person who refinishes Group I vehicles, or their existing parts or components, or replacement parts or components,
shall not apply a coating which has a VOC content in excess of the limits in the table of group 1 vehicle VOC limits. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

