<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Dip coat;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
6
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Hand application methods; or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
7
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Other coating application methods that are demonstrated to have transfer efficiency at least equal to HVLP spray
equipment in the application, and which are used in such a manner that the parameters under which they were tested are
permanent features of the method. Such coating application methods shall be approved in writing by EPA.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) A person shall not apply coatings by any of the methods listed in paragraph (c)(3)(iii)(A) of this section unless
the coating is applied with properly operating equipment and operated according to procedures recommended by the
manufacturer.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cleanup solvent use.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Solvents used for surface preparation, equipment cleanup, and thinning operations, including storage and disposal
of VOC-containing materials, shall be subject to the provisions and requirements of &sect;52.2961(a).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission control system.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A person may comply with the provisions of paragraph (c)(3)(i) of this section by using an emission control system,
provided that this system maintains a control efficiency (capture efficiency times destruction or removal efficiency)
of the VOC emissions of at least 85 (eighty-five) percent by weight.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Prohibition of specifications.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A person shall not solicit from, or require any other person to use in the affected area, any VOC-containing material
subject to the provisions of this section which, when applied as supplied or thinned or reduced according to the manufacturer's
recommendation for application, does not meet the limits and requirements of this section. The prohibition against
soliciting, or requiring the use of VOC-containing materials shall not apply with respect to solicitations from
or requirements of persons operating pursuant to an approved emission control system, as provided for in paragraph
(c)(3)(v) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The requirements of this paragraph shall apply to all written or oral agreements executed and entered into.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Exemptions.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The provisions of paragraphs (c)(3) (i) and (iii) of this section shall not apply to:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Touch-up coatings; or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Stencil coatings.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The exemptions described in paragraphs (c)(4)(i) (A) and (B) of this section shall not apply to aerosol container
applications.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Recordkeeping requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any person subject to this section shall comply with the following require
<!-- PJG 0034 unknown -->
ments:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The person shall maintain and have available during an inspection the listed category of each of the coatings and
the type of vehicle or equipment to which each coating was applied.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The person shall maintain and have available during an inspection a current list of coatings in use which provides
all of the coating data necessary to evaluate compliance, including the following information, as applicable:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Coating, catalyst, additives, and reducer used;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Mix ratio of components used; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) VOC content of coating as applied.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The person shall maintain records on a daily basis, including the following information:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Coating and mix ratio of components in the coating used; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Quantity of each coating applied.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Any person using an emission control system as a means of complying with this section shall maintain daily records
of key system operating and maintenance procedures which will demonstrate continuous operation and compliance
of the emission control device during periods of emission-producing activities. Key system operating parameters
are those necessary to ensure compliance with VOC content of coating requirements such as temperatures, pressures,
and flowrates.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) All records shall be retained at the facility for at least five years and shall be provided to EPA upon request.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test methods. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of this section, the following test methods shall be used:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
VOC content.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The VOC content of coatings shall be determined by EPA Method 24 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A);
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The VOC content of emissions shall be determined by EPA Method 18 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A); and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The exempt compound content of coatings shall be determined by ASTM Test Method D&hyph;4457&hyph;85.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Determination of iridescent particles in metallic/iridescent topcoat. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The metal and silicon content of metallic/iridescent topcoat shall be determined by SCAQMD Method 26
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(SCAQMD ``Laboratory Method of Analysis for Enforcement Samples'' manual).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Acid content in pretreatment coatings. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The acid content of pretreatment coatings shall be determined by ASTM Test Method D&hyph;1613&hyph;85 (modified).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Determination of efficiency of emission control systems.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Capture efficiency. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The efficiency of the collection device of the emission control system, as specified in paragraph (c)(3)(v) of this
section, shall be determined by the EPA method described at &sect;52.741(a)(4)(iii).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Destruction or removal efficiency. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The efficiency of the control device, as specified in paragraph (c)(3)(v) of this section, shall be determined by
the EPA method described at &sect;52.741(a)(4)(iv). The VOC content measured and calculated as carbon in the control
device exhaust gases shall be determined by EPA Method 25 or 25A (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
