<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reflectance of anti-glare safety coatings. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reflectance of anti-glare safety coatings shall be measured by ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Test Method D&hyph;523. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transfer efficiency. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The transfer efficiency for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
alternative coating application methods, as defined in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c)(3)(iii)(A)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
7
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section, shall be determined in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with the South Coast Air Quality Management District 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(SCAQMD) test method for determining transfer efficiency entitled, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
``Spray Equipment Transfer Efficiency (TE) Test Procedure for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Equipment User, May 24, 1989.'' This transfer efficiency method is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved for the limited purpose of comparing alternative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application technologies under controlled conditions. The results 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of these tests are not transferable to a production setting. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test method is not acceptable for determining transfer efficiency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to establish VOC emission reduction credits to allow the use of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
higher VOC coatings, or to establish VOC credits for trading or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
offset purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Qualification and petition for classification as an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extreme-performance topcoat.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Extreme-performance topcoat qualification. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
topcoat is an extreme-performance topcoat if it is to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applied on Group II vehicles and equipment and will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repeatedly exposed to any of the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Heavy abrasion, including mechanical wear and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repeated scrubbing with industrial-grade detergents, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cleaners, solvents, or abrasive scouring agents; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Temperatures in excess of 250 F; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Corrosive, caustic, or acidic agents, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
chemicals, chemical fumes, chemical mixtures or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
solutions; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Other similar environmental conditions as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Extreme-performance coating petition. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any person 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
seeking to use an extreme-performance coating in any coating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation which is subject to the provisions of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall comply with the following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A petition shall be submitted to EPA stating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the performance requirements, volume of coating, and VOC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
level which is attainable. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) If EPA grants written approval, such petition 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will be repeated on an annual basis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) If EPA grants written approval, such approval 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall contain volume and VOC limit conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Records shall be maintained as in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c)(5) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Adhesives and sealants.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This section applies to any person who 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
supplies, sells, offers for sale, or uses adhesives, sealants, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive primers in the affected area. This section does not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply to household adhesives which are subject to consumer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
products regulations in the California Code of Regulations (Title 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
17, Division 3, Subchapter 8.5_Consumer Products, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;&sect;94507&hyph;94517). For the purpose of this section, the affected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area refers to the Sacramento Metro Area for ozone as described 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraph (d) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions apply. All terms not defined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ABS adhesive 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any substance that is intended for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
welding acrylonitrile butadiene styrene (ABS) plastic pipe. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Adhesive 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any substance that is used to bond one 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surface to another surface by attachment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Adhesive primer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a coating that is intended by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer to be applied to a substrate, prior to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application of an adhesive, to provide a bonding surface. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aerosol adhesive 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a mixture of rubber, resins, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liquid and gaseous solvents and propellants packaged in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
disposable container for hand-held application. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aerospace component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the fabricated part, assembly of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
parts, or completed unit of any aircraft or space vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
excluding tires. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Aircraft 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any machine designed to travel through the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air without leaving the earth's atmosphere, whether heavier or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lighter than air, including airplanes, balloons, dirigibles, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
helicopters, and missiles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Automotive glass primer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any adhesive primer that is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
intended by the manufacturer to be applied to automotive glass 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prior to installation with an adhesive/sealant. This primer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
improves adhesion to the pinch weld and blocks ultraviolet light. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Ceramic tile installation 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the installation of ceramic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tile products using an adhesive formulated for that purpose. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Computer diskette manufacturing 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the process where the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fold-over flaps are glued to the body of a vinyl jacket. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Contact adhesive 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any adhesive that is intended by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer to adhere to itself instantaneously upon contact. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
This adhesive is applied to both adherents and, when dry, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
develops a bond when the adherents are brought together without 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sustained pressure. For the purpose of this section, products 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that qualify as a contact adhesive using the above definition, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and that are labelled exclusively for only one of the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applications, shall not be required to meet the VOC limit for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
``Contact adhesives'' in paragraph (d)(3)(i)(A) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Single-ply roofing material installation; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Bonding of immersible products; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Bonding of flexible vinyl to flexible vinyl. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cove base installation 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the installation of cove base 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(or wall base), which is generally made of vinyl or rubber, on a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
wall or vertical surface at floor level using an adhesive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
formulated for that purpose. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Dry wall and panel installation 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the installation of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gypsum dry wall to studs or solid surfaces using an adhesive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
formulated for that purpose. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
