<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plastic cement welding
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the use of adhesives made of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
resins and solvents which are formulated to dissolve the surfaces 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of plastic to form a bond between mating surfaces. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plastic foam
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a foam constructed of plastics. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plastics
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means various synthetic materials chemically formed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the polymerization of organic (carbon-based) substances. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Porous material
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a substance which has tiny openings, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
often microscopic, in which fluids may be absorbed or discharged. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Such materials include but are not limited to paper and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
corrugated paperboard. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Propellant
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a fluid under pressure which expels the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contents of a container when a valve is opened. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
PVC/CPVC welding adhesive
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any adhesive intended by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer to weld polyvinyl chloride (PVC) or chlorinated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
polyvinyl chloride (CPVC) plastic pipe. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rubber flooring installation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the installation of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flooring material in which both the back and top surfaces are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
made of synthetic rubber, and may not be in sheet or tile form. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Sealant products
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 mean any material with adhesive properties 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that is formulated to be used primarily to fill, seal, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
waterproof, or weatherproof gaps or joints between two surfaces. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sealant products include sealant, primers, and caulks. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Single-ply roof membrane installation/repair
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
installing or fixing, mending and/or repairing of a single-ply 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
membrane. Installation includes, as a minimum, attaching the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
edge of the membrane to the edge of the roof and flashings to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vents, pipes, and ducts that protrude through the roof. Repair 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
includes gluing the edges of the tears together, attaching a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
patch over a hole, and applying flashings to vents, pipes or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ducts installed through the membrane. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Structural glazing
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the use of an adhesive/sealant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhere glass, ceramic, metal, stone, or composite panels to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exterior building frames. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Subfloor installation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the installation of subflooring 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
material, typically plywood, over floor joists. Subflooring is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
covered by a finished surface material. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Thin metal laminating
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a process of bonding multiple 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
layers of metal to metal or metal to plastic in the production of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
electronic or magnetic components in which the thickness of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
bond line(s) is less than .025 mils. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Tire repair
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the expanding of a hole, tear, fissure, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
blemish in a tire casing by grinding or grouping, applying 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive, and filling the hole or crevice with rubber. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
VCT
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means vinyl composition tile. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
