<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The amount of adhesives, sealants, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive primers used and the VOC content of such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
products; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
iii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The amount of solvents used and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VOC content of such solvents. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Such records shall be retained in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the provisions of paragraph (d)(5) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Solvent welding operations used in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturing of medical devices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Plaque laminating operations where adhesives are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used to bond a clear, polyester acetate laminate to wood 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with lamination equipment installed prior to July 1, 1992. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Any person seeking to claim this exemption shall notify EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in writing that a complying adhesive is not available. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) Manufacturing operations of the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
products: diving suits, rubber bladders, inflatable boats, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
life preservers, or other products designed for immersion in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
water or fuels. The adhesive products used by these 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operations must be labelled: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=84 g=1 f=1 -->
For the Bonding of Immersible Products Only 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(ii) The provision of this section shall not apply to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aerospace components. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The provisions of this section shall not apply to any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive or sealant that contains less than 20 g/L of VOC per 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liter of adhesive or sealant, less water and less exempt 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compounds, as applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Paragraph (d)(5) of this section shall not apply to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities with a combined use of adhesives, sealants, adhesive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
primers, and solvents used in a total volume of less than 20 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gallons on a calendar year basis. Any facility claiming this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exemption must have information available, such as purchase 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
orders, that will allow for the verification of facility usage. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Until January 1, 1997, the provisions of paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d)(3)(i) and (ii) of this section shall not apply to any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facility using 3 gallons per day or less of adhesive used 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exclusively for thin metal laminating operations, provided that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the adhesive contains less than 600 grams of VOC per liter of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive, less water and less exempt compounds, as applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting and Recordkeeping
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Any source within the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
affected area that uses greater than 20 gallons of adhesive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and/or sealant product per year subject to paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d)(3)(i)(A)&hyph;(C) of this section shall comply with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Maintain a current file of each adhesive, sealant, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive primer, and solvent in use and in storage. The file 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall provide all of the data necessary to evaluate compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and shall include, but not be limited to, the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information, as applicable: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A data sheet or material list giving material 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
name, manufacturer identification, and material application; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Any catalysts, reducers, or other components used 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and the mix ratio; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The VOC content limit or vapor pressure limit from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (d)(3) of this section and the actual VOC content, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as applied, or vapor pressure of the adhesive, sealant, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
primer, or solvent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Maintain records of the monthly volume of each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive, sealant, primer, or solvent used. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Any person using an emission control system as a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
means of complying with this section shall maintain daily records 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of key system operating and maintenance procedures which will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrate continuous operation and compliance of the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control device during periods of emission-producing activities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Key system operating parameters are those necessary to ensure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with VOC content of coating requirements such as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
temperatures, pressures, and flowrates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) All records shall be maintained for at least five 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years and shall be available for inspection and provided to EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. For the purpose of this section, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following test methods shall be used: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
VOC content
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The VOC content of aerosol adhesives and sealants 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be determined by EPA Method 24 (40 CFR part 60, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appendix A); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The VOC content of aerosol adhesives or aerosol 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adhesive primers shall be determined using South Coast Air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Quality Management District (SCAQMD) Test Method 305 for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Aerosol Coatings; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The VOC content of emissions shall be determined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by EPA Method 18 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A); and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) The exempt compound content of coatings shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by ASTM Test Method D&hyph;4457&hyph;85. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Determination of collection efficiency of emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control systems
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Capture efficiency
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The efficiency of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
collection device of an emission control system, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in paragraph (d)(3)(iv) of this section, shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by the EPA method described at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.741(a)(4)(iii). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Destruction or removal efficiency
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The efficiency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the control device, as specified in paragraph (d)(3)(iv) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section, shall be determined by the EPA method 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
described at &sect;52.741(a)(4)(iv). The VOC content measured 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and calculated as carbon in the control device exhaust gases 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be determined by EPA Method 25 or 25A (40 CFR part 60, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The active and passive solvent losses from spray gun 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cleaning systems shall be determined using SCAQMD's ``General Test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Method for Determining Solvent Losses from Spray Gun Cleaning 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Systems,'' dated October 3, 1989. The test solvent for this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determination shall be any lacquer thinner with a minimum vapor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressure of 105 mm of Hg at 20 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C, and the minimum test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
temperature shall be 
<!-- PJG 0034 unknown -->
15
<!-- PJG 0377 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The test method used to determine plasticizer content 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and flexible vinyls shall be ASTM Method E260&hyph;73, ``General Gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Chromatography Procedures.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Can and Coil Coating Operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. This section shall apply to all metal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
container, metal closure, and metal coil coating operations 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
within the affected area except as specified in paragraph (e)(4) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section. For the purposes of this section, the affected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area is the Sacramento Metro Area for ozone as described at 40 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. For the purposes of paragraph (e) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Closure
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any component which is used to close or seal a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
filled can, jar, or bottle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coating applicator
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an apparatus used to apply a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surface coating. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coating line
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an operation or process for applying, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
drying, or baking and/or curing surface coating, together with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
associated equipment, including a coating applicator, flash-off 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area, and oven. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Coil
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any flat metal sheet or strip that is rolled or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
wound in concentric rings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Container
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any metal can, drum, pail, or tube. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00378 </DOCNO>
