<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00380 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(A) Electrostatic application; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Flow coat; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Roll coat; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Dip coat; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) High-volume, low-pressure (HVLP) spray; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) Hand application methods; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) Other coating application methods that are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrated to have a transfer efficiency at least equal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to HVLP spray equipment in the application, and which are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used in such a manner that the parameters under which they 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
were tested are permanent features of the method. Such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coating application methods shall be approved in writing by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cleanup Solvent Use. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Solvents used for surface 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
preparation, equipment cleanup, and thinning operations, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
including storage and disposal of VOC-containing materials, shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be subject to the provisions and requirements of &sect;52.2961(a), 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
solvent cleaning operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Prohibition of sale. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A person shall not sell or offer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for sale for use in the affected area any coating which contains 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VOCs in excess of the limits specified in this section for any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application governed by this section unless the label on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
product or the data sheets for the product clearly bear the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
warning that the coating shall not be used unless compliance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section can be achieved. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Prohibition of specification. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A person shall not solicit or require any other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
person to use, in the affected area, any coating or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combination of coatings to be applied to any metal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
container, metal closure, or metal coil subject to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provisions of this section that does not meet the limits 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The requirements of paragraph (e)(3)(vi)(A) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section shall apply to all written or oral agreements 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
executed, entered into, or renewed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The provisions of this section shall not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply to the spray coating of 1 gallon per day or less of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coatings at a single facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting and recordkeeping requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any person 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject to this section shall comply with the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Maintain and have available during an inspection, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
listed category of each of the coatings and the type of metal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
container, metal closure, and/or metal coil to which each coating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
was applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Maintain and have available during an inspection, a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
current list of coatings in use which provides all of the coating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
data necessary to evaluate compliance, including the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information, as applicable: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Coating, catalyst, additives, and reducer used; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Mix ratio of components used; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) VOC content of coating as applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Maintain records on a daily basis including the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following information: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Coating and mix ratio of components in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coating used; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Quantity of each coating applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Control equipment records. Any person using an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission control system as a means of complying with this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall maintain daily records of key system operating and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintenance procedures which will demonstrate continuous 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation and compliance of the emission control device during 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
periods of emission producing activities. Key system operating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
parameters are those necessary to ensure compliance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (e)(3)(ii) of this section such as temperatures, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressures, and flowrates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) All records shall be retained at the facility for at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
least five years and shall be made available to EPA upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test methods. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purpose of this section, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following test methods shall be used: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) VOC content. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The VOC content of coatings subject to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provisions of this section shall be determined by EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Method 24 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The VOC content of emissions shall be determined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by EPA Method 18 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The exempt compound content shall be determined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by ASTM Test Method D&hyph;4457&hyph;85. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00381 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(ii) Determination of efficiency of emission control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
systems. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The efficiency of the collection device of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission control system as specified in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e)(3)(ii)(B) of this section shall be determined by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA method described at &sect;52.741(a)(4)(iii). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The efficiency of the control device, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in paragraph (e)(3)(ii)(A) of this section, shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be determined by the EPA method described at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.741(a)(4)(iv). The VOC content measured and calculated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as carbon in the control device exhaust gases shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by EPA Method 25 or 25A (40 CFR part 60, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Transfer Efficiency. The transfer efficiency for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other coating application methods as defined in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e)(3)(iii)(G) of this section, shall be determined in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the South Coast Air Quality Management District (SCAQMD) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test method for determining transfer efficiency entitled ``Spray 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Equipment Transfer Efficiency Test Procedure for Equipment User, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
May 24, 1989.'' This transfer efficiency method is approved for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the limited purpose of comparing alternative application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
technologies under controlled conditions. The results of these 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tests are not transferable to a production setting. The test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
method is not acceptable for determining transfer efficiency to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
establish VOC emission reduction credits to allow the use of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
higher VOC coatings, or to establish VOC credits for trading or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
offset purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Commercial bakeries. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Except as provided in paragraph (f)(4) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section, this section is applicable to bakery ovens which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
bake yeast-leavened products. For the purposes of this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the affected area is the Sacramento Metro Area for ozone as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
described at 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraph (f) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
not defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Bakery oven 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a convection oven which bakes yeast-leavened products, including but not limited to breads, buns, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rolls. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fermentation time 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the elapsed time between adding 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
yeast to dough or sponge and placing the dough or sponge into an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
oven, expressed in hours. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Yeast percentage 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the pounds of yeast added to a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hundred pounds of total flour in the recipe. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) On and after January 1, 1997, no person shall operate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a bakery oven subject to this section, unless VOC emissions are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
controlled using an air pollution control system which: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Has been installed in accordance with an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authority to Construct issued by the applicable local air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollution control district or air quality management 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
district; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Includes an emission collection system(s) which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ducts the exhaust gases from all stacks and/or vents on all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ovens to a VOC emission control device(s). Such ducting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be maintained so as to be free of visible holes, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
breaks, openings or separations between adjoining 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
components from which fugitive VOCs would be emitted to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
atmosphere; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Has one or more VOC emission control devices, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
each with a destruction or removal efficiency of at least 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
95 percent by weight. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) For an oven which commences construction on or after 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
January 1, 1995, owners and operators shall be in compliance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (f)(3)(i) of this section by the date of commencement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of oven operation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The provisions of this section shall not apply to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
bakery ovens which are located at a facility where the combined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rated heat input capacity of all ovens is less than 2 million 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
British Thermal Units (BTUs) per hour. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The provisions of this section shall not apply to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ovens used exclusively for the baking of products leavened 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
chemically without yeast. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The provisions of paragraph (f)(3) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall not apply to bakery ovens which are located at a facility 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
where the uncontrolled actual emissions of VOCs from all ovens 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combined is less than 6.5 tons per year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Reporting and Recordkeeping.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A person operating a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
bakery oven subject to this section shall maintain records in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00382 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) Maintain current records necessary to determine emissions for each oven including, but not limited to, type of
each yeast-leavened baked product, yeast percentage for each product, and fermentation time for each product; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Maintain monthly records of production rates, by weight, of finished baked product for each yeast-leavened
product; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) For control equipment subject to paragraph (f)(3) of this section, maintain daily records of key system operating
and maintenance procedures which will demonstrate continuous operation and compliance of the emission control
device during periods of emission producing activities. Key system operating parameters are those necessary to
ensure compliance with paragraphs (f)(3) (i) and (ii) of this section such as temperature, pressure, and flow rates.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
These records shall be maintained on site for at least five years and shall be made available to EPA upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) For the purposes of this section, VOC emission factors for each yeast-leavened bakery product shall be determined
in accordance with the table of bakery emission factors in this section. Annual emission rates shall be calculated
by using those emission factors and the annual production rate for each yeast-leavened finished bakery product.
Alternatively, VOC emission factors for any yeast-leavened bakery product may be determined by the method(s) specified
in paragraph (f)(6)(ii) of this section, together with exhaust flow rates and oven throughput. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Measurement of VOC emission control device efficiency subject to paragraph (f)(3)(i)(C) of this section shall
be conducted in accordance with the EPA method described at &sect;52.741(a)(4)(iv). The VOC content measured and
calculated as carbon in the control device exhaust gases shall be determined by EPA Method 25 or 25A (40 CFR part 60,
appendix A). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



