(g) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Municipal solid waste landfills. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 This section shall apply to all municipal solid waste (MSW) landfills with a maximum design capacity of greater than
111,000 tons of solid waste, although facilities that have received less than 500,000 tons of decomposable solid
waste during their operational lifetime are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
only subject to the requirements of paragraph (g)(5)(i) of this section. The refuse density shall be assumed to be
1,300 pounds per cubic yard and the decomposable fraction shall be assumed to be 70% by weight unless other site-specific
factors are submitted to and approved by EPA. For the purposes of this section, the affected area refers to the Sacramento
Metro Area for ozone as described at 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of paragraph (g) of this section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not defined herein
shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Active landfill 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any MSW landfill which received waste at any time during the past six months. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Baseline condition
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means there are no leaks existing at: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Any location on the surface of the landfill covered by final cover; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Any location on the surface of the landfill which has been covered by intermediate cover for over 6 months; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Any location along the gas transfer path of the gas collection system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Control device
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any device that disposes of the collected gas by one or more of the following means: combustion, gas treatment
and subsequent sale, sale and processing off site, or other equivalent methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Decomposable solid waste
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any material which is not non-decomposable inert solid waste. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Design capacity
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the maximum amount of waste a landfill can accept, as specified in the construction permit issued by the county
or State agency responsible for regulating the landfill. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Destruction/treatment efficiency
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a measure of the ability of the control device to combust, transform, or otherwise prevent the emissions to the
atmosphere of non-methane organic compounds in landfill gas, expressed as a percentage. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Energy recovery equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any equipment that uses landfill gas to produce useful energy. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Excavation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any movement of landfill cover that triggers notification requirements of any government agency. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Final cover
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means cover material that is applied on areas where additional cells are not to be constructed and, therefore, must
be highly resistant to erosion. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gas collection system
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a series of collectors and associated piping and equipment which provides a gas transfer path to the control
device. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gas transfer path
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the piping, pumps, and other equipment used to transfer evolved landfill gas from the point of gas evolution
through the control device. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Household waste
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any solid waste (including garbage, trash, and sanitary waste in septic tanks) derived from households (including
single and multiple residences, hotels and motels, bunkhouses, ranger stations, crew quarters, campgrounds, picnic
grounds, and day-use recreation areas). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Industrial solid waste
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means solid waste generated by manufacturing or industrial processes, that is not a hazardous waste regulated under
subtitle C of the Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (42 U.S.C. 6901&hyph;6992k). Such waste may include, but
is not limited to, the following manufacturing processes: electric power generation; fertilizer/agricultural
chemicals; food and related products/by-products; inorganic chemicals; iron 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and steel manufacturing; leather and leather products; nonferrous metals manufacturing/foundries; organic chemicals;
plastics and resins manufacturing; pulp and paper industry; rubber and miscellaneous plastic products; stone,
glass, clay, and concrete products; textile manufacturing; transportation equipment; and water treatment. This
term does not include mining waste or oil 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and gas waste. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Intermediate cover
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means cover material that is applied on areas where additional cells are not to be constructed for extended periods
of time and, therefore, must resist erosion for a longer period of time than daily cover. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Landfill
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an area of land or an excavation in which wastes are placed for permanent disposal, and which is not a land application
unit, surface impoundment, injection well, or waste pile. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Landfill gas 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any gas derived through a natural process through the decomposition of organic waste deposited in a landfill
or from the evolution of volatile organic species in the waste. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
