<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(A) The owner of any MSW landfill subject to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements of this section shall demonstrate compliance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section no later than July 1, 1997. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) This section shall not apply to sites that have 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
received only hazardous waste. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The provisions of paragraph (g)(3)(ii) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall not apply to control devices for which a construction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permit was issued by the applicable air pollution control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
district or air quality management district before March 1, 1995, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provided that the control device has a NMOC destruction/treatment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
efficiency of at least 90% by weight or reduces the NMOC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
concentration at the outlet of the control device to 30 ppm or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
less measured as methane corrected to 3% oxygen, and annual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source testing for NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, CO and NMOC is performed simultaneously 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
using the procedures in paragraphs (g)(6)(iv) and (vi) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting and Recordkeeping. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The following reporting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements shall each apply independently: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Each owner of an MSW landfill having a maximum design 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capacity greater than 100,000 megagrams (Mg) (111,000 tons) shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submit an initial design capacity report to EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The initial design capacity report shall contain the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following information: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A map or plot of the landfill, providing the size 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and location of the landfill, and identifying all areas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
where refuse may be landfilled according to the provisions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the state or county permit; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The maximum design capacity of the landfill. Where 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the maximum design capacity is specified in the state or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
county construction or Resource Conservation and Recovery 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Act (RCRA) permit, a copy of the permit specifying the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maximum design capacity may be submitted. If the maximum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
design capacity of the landfill is not specified in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permit, the maximum design capacity must be calculated using 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
good engineering principles. The calculations must be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provided, along with such parameters as depth of refuse, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
refuse acceptance rate, and compaction practices. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
state, county, or EPA may request other reasonable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information as may be necessary to verify the maximum design 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capacity of the landfill. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) An amended design capacity report must be submitted to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA providing notification of any increase in the size of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
landfill, whether the increase results from an increase in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permitted area or depth of the landfill, a change in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operating procedures, or any other means which results in an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
increase in the maximum design capacity of the landfill. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
amended design capacity report must be submitted within 90 days 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the issuance of an amended construction or operating permit, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or the actual use of additional land, or the change in operating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedures which will result in an increase in maximum design 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capacity, whichever comes first. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Each owner who installs a gas collection system and/or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control system described in paragraph (g)(3) of this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall perform an initial performance test as described in &sect;60.8. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The initial performance test report shall include, but not be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited to, the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A diagram of the collection system showing vertical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extraction well spacing, including the locations of any areas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
excluded from collection and the proposed sites for the future 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
addition of wells; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The documentation of the presence of asbestos for each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area from which collection wells have been excluded based on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
presence of asbestos; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The sum of the gas generation rates for all areas from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which collection wells have been excluded based on the presence 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of nondegradable materials and the calculations of the gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
generation rate for each excluded area; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) The provisions for increasing gas mover capacity with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
increased gas generation rate, if the present gas mover is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inadequate to move the maximum flowrate expected over the life of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the landfill. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Each owner of a controlled landfill shall, within 48 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hours, report to EPA by telephone any malfunction, shutdown, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other event causing a reduction in the gas collection rate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) If any portion of the gas collection system is shut 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
down which results in a gas collection flowrate of less than 80% 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the target volume for longer than 24 hours due to scheduled or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unscheduled maintenance activities, equipment breakdown, or any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other reason, the owner shall notify EPA by telephone within 48 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hours of the detection of such shutdown. A written follow-up 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
report shall be forwarded to EPA within 15 calendar days 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
describing the duration and reason for the shut down. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Each owner of a controlled landfill shall submit a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
closure report to EPA. For the purposes of this section, closure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
means that refuse is no longer being placed in the landfill, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that no additional wastes will be placed into the landfill 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
without filing a notification of modification. EPA may request 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
such additional information as may be reasonably necessary to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
verify that permanent closure has taken place. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Each owner of a controlled landfill shall submit an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment removal report to EPA prior to removal or cessation of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation of the control equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The equipment removal report shall contain the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following items: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A copy of the closure report submitted in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with paragraph (g)(5)(v) of this section; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A copy of the initial performance test report 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrating that the 15-year minimum control period has 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
expired; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Dated copies of the three successive NMOC emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rate reports demonstrating that the landfill is no longer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emitting above the level of the standard. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) EPA may request such additional information as may be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonably necessary to verify that all of the conditions for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
removal have been met. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) The following records shall be maintained in written 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
form at the MSW landfill for a period of five years from the date 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of each entry and shall be made available to EPA upon request: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Records of the gas collection flowrate, in SCFM, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the oxygen concentration, for each time that baseline conditions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are established. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Records of continuous measurements (at least hourly 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
records or a chart record) of the total gas collection flowrate, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in SCFM, including notes describing the reasons for down-time. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
