<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Operation and maintenance plan. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The owner shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prepare and adhere to an operation and maintenance plan. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
plan shall be revised at least once every six months to reflect 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operating experience and changing site conditions. The plan 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be submitted to EPA upon request. This plan shall at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minimum contain: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) An engineering evaluation of the expected landfill gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
generation rate, and design specifications for the gas collection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system. Data concerning waste type, volume, tonnage and age 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be included if available. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) A map showing the location, spacing and depths of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
collection wells and/or trenches, and the direction of flow 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
through the header system to the control device. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) A map indicating areas of steep slopes and any other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
safety hazards to personnel performing the surface emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Sampling and analysis methods to be used by the owner 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to meet the requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Specific techniques to ensure that overdraw is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minimized. These may include a schedule for periodic temperature 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measurements at wellheads and a schedule for periodic gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sampling including gas analysis methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



