<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(F) A schedule detailing inspection and maintenance intervals including dates and durations of expected system
shutdowns. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) Written justification for less than continuous operation of the gas collection system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(H) Operating procedures including system start-up, balancing, optimization, and shutdown. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(I) Qualifications and training requirements for on-site personnel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(J) Safety precautions, protective clothing and equipment requirements, and emergency procedures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The following procedures shall be used to establish baseline conditions pursuant to paragraph (g)(3)(i)(B)
of this section: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The gas collection rate and landfill surface integrity shall be evaluated and brought to baseline conditions
by testing for leaks and repairing all such leaks using the repair methods listed in paragraph (g)(3)(i)(H)(1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section. Surface leak testing shall be performed using an instrument which meets the apparatus specifications
of EPA Method 21 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A). The instrument shall be calibrated before and after each test using zero
air and an approximate 500 ppm methane standard calibration gas in accordance with the instrument manufacturer's
recommendations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Surface leak testing shall be performed by holding the detector probe 2 inches from the landfill surface while
walking a pattern of parallel paths not more than 50 feet apart over all surface areas specified in paragraph (g)(3)(i)(H)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section. Cracks, holes, and other breaches in the surface as well as areas where buried waste interfaces with
undisturbed, native soil shall also be evaluated. The owner is not required to monitor surfaces on steep slopes and
other areas posing a hazard to testing personnel; however, leaks identified in such areas are not exempt from the provisions
of paragraph (g)(3)(i)(H) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Surface leak testing shall be performed only when the average wind speed is less than 5 miles per hour and instantaneous
wind speed is less than 10 miles per hour, unless EPA approves alternate wind speed limits based on demonstrated recurrent
site-specific conditions. Average wind speed shall be determined on a 10 minute average using an on-site anemometer
with a continuous recorder. Surface testing shall not be conducted when the surface is wet or when there has been rain
during the preceding 72 hours. Surface testing of landfill surfaces that are normally wet (i.e., a golf course) may
be performed when the surface is wet. EPA personnel may randomly identify leaks without regard to the above wind speed
and surface condition requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) EPA Method 21 (40 CFR part 60, appendix A) shall be used to determine leaks along the gas transfer path. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) EPA Method 2D (40 CFR part 60, appendix A) shall be used for the flowrate measurements required by paragraphs (g)(3)(i)(B)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (g)(3)(i)(D) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) EPA Method 3A (40 CFR part 60, appendix A) shall be used for the oxygen concentration measurements required by
paragraphs (g)(3)(i)(B)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (g)(3)(i)(C) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
