<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00393 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(ii) Measurement of capture efficiency shall be determined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in accordance with the EPA method
<FOOTCITE>34</FOOTCITE>
 or by an alternative method 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved in writing by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
34
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=3 -->
40 CFR 52.741(a)(4)(iii).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(i) Fugitive Emissions from Gas Processing Plants, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Refineries, Bulk Plants, Bulk Terminals, and Chemical Plants. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of paragraphs (i)(1) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
through (7) of this section shall apply to any owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operator of a refinery, bulk plant, bulk terminal, chemical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
plant, or gas processing plant. For the purposes of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the affected areas include the Sacramento Metro Area, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Los Angeles-South Coast Air Basin Area, and the Ventura 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
County Area as described for ozone in 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraphs (i)(1) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
through (7) of this section, the following definitions shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply. All terms not defined herein shall have the meaning given 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Background 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a reading expressed as methane on a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
portable hydrocarbon detection instrument which is taken at least 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
three meters upwind from any component to be inspected and which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is not influenced by any specific emission point. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Bulk plant 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any distributing facility which receives 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
organic liquid; stores it in stationary tanks; and which loads it 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
into tank trucks for delivery to other bulk plants, service 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stations or other distribution points. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Bulk terminal 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any primary distributing plant which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
receives organic liquid; stores it in stationary tanks; loads it 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
into transportable containers, excluding marine vessels, for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
delivery to bulk plants, service stations, or other distribution 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
points. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Chemical plant 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any facility engaged in producing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
organic or inorganic chemicals, and/or manufacturing chemical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
products by chemical processes. Any facility or operation that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
has 28 as the first two digits in its four digit Standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Industrial Classification (SIC) Code as defined in the SIC Manual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is included. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Closed-vent system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any system that is not open to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
atmosphere and is composed of piping, connections and, if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
necessary, flow-inducing devices that transport gases or vapors 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from a piece or pieces of equipment to a vapor recovery or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
disposal system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Commercial natural gas 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means processed natural gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
containing less than 10% VOC by weight. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any valve, fitting, pump, compressor, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressure relief device, diaphragm, hatch, sight-glass, open-ended 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
line, or meter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compressor 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any device used to compress gases and/or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vapors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Control valve 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a device that is used to regulate fluid 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressure or volume in a process unit that, upon actuation, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
releases VOC from the process stream. Control valves which are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
actuated with non-process stream compressed air are excluded from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this definition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Critical component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any component that if shut down 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would require the shutdown of the associated process unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fitting 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a component used to attach or connect pipes, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
piping details, and other equipment, such as, vessels, heat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exchangers, and condensers. These components include but are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited to flanges, threaded connections, and other connectors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gas processing plant 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any facility engaged in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
separation of liquids from field gas and/or fractionation of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liquids into gaseous products, such as ethane, propane, butane, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and natural gasoline. Excluded from the definition are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compressor stations, dehydration units, sweetening units, field 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
treatment, underground storage facilities, liquefied natural gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
units, and field gas gathering systems unless these facilities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are located at a natural gas processing plant. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Hatch 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any covered opening system that provides access 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to a tank or container, usually through the top deck. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Inaccessible component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any component located over 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fifteen feet above ground when access is required from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ground; or any component located over six feet away from a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
platform when access is required from the platform. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a major gas leak, major liquid leak, minor gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
leak, or minor liquid leak. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak minimization 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means reducing a leak to the lowest 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
achievable level using best modern practices including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tightening, adjusting, or adding sealing material and without 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shutting down the process which the component serves. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak repair 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any corrective action taken for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes of reducing a component leak to the lowest achievable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
level below the applicable standard using best modern practices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any 4-inch or larger valve, any 5-horse-power (5-hp) or larger pump, any compressor, and any 4-inch 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or larger pressure relief device. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major gas leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
for any component except pressure relief 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
devices means the detection of total gaseous organic compounds in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
excess of 10,000 ppmv as methane above background as measured 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
according to the test procedures in paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. A major gas leak for a pressure relief device means the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
detection of total gaseous organic compounds in excess of 200 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ppmv as methane above background as measured according to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test procedures in paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major liquid leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a visible mist or cloud or a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
continuous flow of liquid. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minor component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any component that is not a major 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
component. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minor gas leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
for any component means the detection of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
total gaseous organic compounds in excess of 500 ppmv (for valves 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and connectors) and 1,000 ppmv (for other components unless 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
otherwise specified) but not more than 10,000 ppmv as methane 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
above background as measured according to the test procedures in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minor liquid leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any liquid leak which is not a major 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liquid leak and drips at a rate of more than three drops per 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minute. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Owner or operator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any person who owns, operates, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
leases, controls, or supervises an emissions source or air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollution control equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Person 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any individual, corporation, copartnership, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
firm, company, partnership, joint stock company, trust, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
association, State, municipality, political subdivision, or any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other legal entity, or their legal representative, agent, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
assigns. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pipeline transfer station 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that handles the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
storage or transfer, or both, of petroleum products or crude 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
petroleum in pipelines. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Platform 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any raised, permanent, horizontal surface 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that provides access to components. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pressure relief device 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a pressure relief valve or a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rupture disc. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pressure relief valve (PRV) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any valve that is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
automatically actuated by upstream static pressure, and used for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
safety or emergency purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pump 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any device used to transport fluids by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
addition of mechanical energy. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Refinery 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that processes petroleum, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined in the Standard Industrial Classification Manual as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Industry Number 2911, Petroleum Refining. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rupture disc 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a diaphragm held between flanges for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purpose of isolating a volatile organic compound from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
atmosphere or from a downstream pressure relief valve. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00394 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unmanned facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a remote facility which has no 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanent sited personnel and is greater than five miles from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nearest manned facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unsafe-to-monitor component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a component installed at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location that would prevent its safe inspection or repair as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined by Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standards or in provisions for worker safety found in 29 CFR 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1910. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vacuum service 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
In vacuum service 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means that the equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in VOC service is operating at an internal pressure that is at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
least 5 kPa (0.73 in. Hg) below ambient pressure. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Valve 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a device that regulates or isolates the fluid 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flow in a pipe, tube, or conduit by means of an external 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
actuator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vapor control system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any system that is not open to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the atmosphere and is composed of piping, connections and, if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
necessary, flow-inducing devices that transport gas or vapor from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a piece or pieces of equipment to a vapor recovery or disposal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Visual inspection 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means performing a survey to indentify 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
signs of leaking liquid, visible mist, or audible leaks. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Specific provisions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Each owner or operator of a gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
processing plant, bulk plant, bulk terminal, refinery, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
chemical plant shall be in compliance with the requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraphs (i)(3)(i) and (i)(3)(ii) of this section by January 1, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1996. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Identification requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Components in VOC service 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall meet the following identification requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) All major and critical components shall be physically 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identified clearly and visibly for inspection, repair, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replacement, and recordkeeping purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) All major, critical, inaccessible, and unsafe-to-monitor components shall be clearly identified in Piping
and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Instrumentation (P&amp;I) flow diagrams for inspection, repair, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replacement, and recordkeeping purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) All minor components shall be individually identified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and/or grouped together functionally for identification in P&amp;I 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flow diagrams for inspection, repair, replacement, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recordkeeping purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) The EPA shall be notified of any changes in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identification of a major component within thirty days. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Inspection and maintenance (I&amp;M) program. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operator of a facility subject to this section shall implement an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
I&amp;M program that meets the requirements of paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i)(3)(ii)(A) through (i)(3)(ii)(C) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Inspection requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The I&amp;M program will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conducted with the following inspection requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All pump seals, compressor seals, and pressure relief 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
valves (PRVs) shall be visually inspected for leaks once 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
during every operating shift. Any vapor leak which is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identified during the visual inspection of components under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraphs (i)(3)(ii)(A)(1) of this section shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measured to quantify emission concentrations according to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the test method specified in paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All components, except as provided in paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i)(3)(ii)(A)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
), (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section, shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspected quarterly according to the method prescribed in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this section. The time between 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspections shall not exceed 110 consecutive days. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The components specified in paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i)(3)(ii)(A)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (i)(3)(ii)(A)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be subject to other than quarterly inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All inaccessible components shall be inspected annually 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
according to the method prescribed in paragraph (i)(7)(i) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section. The time between inspections shall not exceed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
13 consecutive months. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All fittings, including threaded connections and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flanges, shall be inspected for leaks according to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
method prescribed in paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
immediately after being placed into service and semi-annually, not to exceed 195 consecutive days between 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspections, thereafter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Unsafe-to-monitor components shall be inspected in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with an inspection plan approved by the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) PRVs shall be inspected according to the method 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prescribed in paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this section within 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
three calendar days after every pressure relief event. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
6
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The inspection frequency for all components except pump 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
seals, compressor seals, and PRVs may be changed to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
annually, not to exceed 13 consecutive months between 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspections, provided that all of the following conditions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are met: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All components at the facility have been successfully 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operated and maintained for a period of twelve consecutive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
months with no leaks exceeding the thresholds listed in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
table of leak thresholds in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The requirements specified in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i)(3)(ii)(A)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
6
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section are substantiated by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
documentation and written approval obtained from the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) Any annual inspection frequency approved in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i)(3)(ii)(A)(6)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section, shall revert to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection frequencies specified in paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i)(3)(ii)(A)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section, should liquid 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
leaks or major gas leaks exceed 0.5 percent of the total 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
components inspected per inspection period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
8
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A brightly colored, weather-proof tag shall be affixed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to all leaking components showing the date of leak detection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and the hydrocarbon concentration determined according to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the method prescribed in paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repair and maintenance requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The I&amp;M program 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be conducted in accordance with the following repair and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintenance requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All component leaks shall be immediately minimized 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following detection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All leaks from noncritical components shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
successfully repaired or replaced within the time period 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following detection of the leak, as specified in the table 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of repair periods in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) For leaks from critical and unsafe-to-monitor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
components, the leaking component shall be replaced with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Best Available Control Technology (BACT) equipment as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined by EPA within one year or during the next process 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
turnaround, whichever occurs first. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
