4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any repaired or replaced component shall be re-inspected in accordance with the method prescribed in paragraph
(i)(7) of this section by the owner or operator within 30 days of the repair or replacement. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A component or parts thereof which incur five repair actions for a major gas or liquid leak within a continuous twelve
month period shall be replaced with BACT equipment as determined by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak control requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The owner or operator of any facility subject to this section shall comply with the following leak control requirements.
The requirements of paragraphs (i)(3)(ii)(C) (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section shall not apply to components being repaired or replaced within the specified repair or replacement
period, as given in the table of repair periods in this section or paragraph (i)(3)(ii)(B)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section, if the requirements for leak minimization under paragraph (i)(3)(ii)(B)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section have been met. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any liquid leak detected during an inspection by EPA shall constitute a violation of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any leak detected during an inspection by EPA, within any continuous 24-hour period, and numbering in excess of the
leak thresholds for that component listed in the table of leak thresholds in this section, shall constitute a violation
of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any open-ended line or valve found to be leaking shall be sealed with a second valve, blind flange, cap, plug, or a second
closed valve except during operations requiring process fluid flow through the open-ended line or valve. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Hatches shall be closed at all times except during sampling, addition of process material, or attended maintenance
operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Effective twelve months after the adoption of this section, control valves shall be replaced or retrofitted so that
a major leak shall not occur during valve actuation or at any other time. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
6
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Effective twelve months after the adoption of this section, any component leak that is vented through a stack or other
confined air stream shall be transported in a closed-vent system with a collection efficiency of at least 95% to a VOC
control device with a control efficiency of at least 95%. The determination of control efficiency shall be made in
accordance with the test method specified in paragraph (i)(7)(iv) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The provisions of paragraphs (i)(3)(i) and (ii) of this section shall not apply to the following components: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Pressure relief valves, pump seals, and compressor seals that are equipped with a closed-vent system with a VOC
collection efficiency of at least 95% that transports the VOC emissions to a vapor control system with a VOC control
efficiency of at least 95%. The determination of control efficiency shall be made in accordance with the test method
specified in paragraph (i)(7)(iv) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The following cases, where the person seeking the exemption shall supply proof of the applicable criteria to
the satisfaction of the EPA: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Components buried below ground. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Components, except those at gas processing plants, exclusively handling fluids with a VOC concentration of 10
percent by weight or less, as determined by the test method specified in paragraph (i)(7)(ii) of this section; or components
exclusively handling fluids, if the weight percent evaporated is 10 percent or less at 150 degrees Celsius, as determined
by the test method specified in paragraph (i)(7)(iii) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) One-half inch and smaller stainless steel tube fittings which have been demonstrated to the EPA to be leak-free
based on an initial inspection in accordance with paragraph (i)(7)(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Components in vacuum service. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any owner or operator of a facility subject to this section shall comply with the following reporting requirements.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) A compliance plan shall be prepared and submitted to the EPA by July 1, 1995. The plan shall include the following
information: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Component identification methodology to meet the requirements of paragraphs (i)(3)(i)(A) through (C) of this
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) An inspection schedule for all unsafe-to-monitor components pursuant to paragraph (i)(3)(ii)(A)(4) of this
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) A description of all components meeting the exemption requirements of paragraphs (i)(4)(i) through (iv) of this
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) An annual certification of compliance shall be submitted to the EPA on or before January 1, 1996, and annually
thereafter. The certification of compliance shall include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A declaration that the facility is in compliance with all of the requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) A summary of any changes that have been made to component identification in the original compliance plan. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recordkeeping. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Each facility operator shall maintain an inspection log containing, at a minimum, the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Name, location, type of components, and description of any unit where leaking components are found. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Date of leak detection, emission level (ppmv) of leak, and method of leak detection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Date of leak repair and description of repair action. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Date and emission level of re-check after leak is repaired. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Identification of leaks from critical components that cannot be repaired until the next process turnaround.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) If applicable, the API gravity of petroleum process fluids. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) The VOC content of leaking process fluids or gases. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(H) Total number of components inspected, and total number and percentage of leaking components found by component
type. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Records of leaks detected by a quarterly or annual operator inspection and each subsequent repair and reinspection
shall be submitted to the EPA upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) All records of operator inspection and repair shall be maintained at the facility for the previous two year period
and be made available at the time of inspection by the EPA or immediately upon EPA request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
