(7) Test Methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Measurements of total gaseous organic compounds in leak concentrations shall be conducted according to EPA Reference
Method 21. The analyzer shall be calibrated with methane. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The VOC content of fluids shall be determined using procedures that conform to ASTM Methods E 168, E 169, or E 260
or any other procedure that conforms to the above ASTM methods and is approved by the EPA in writing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Determination of the evaporated compounds of liquids shall be performed in accordance with ASTM Method D 86&hyph;82.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Determination of the control efficiency of any VOC control equipment shall be performed in accordance with 40
CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 25 or 25A, or South Coast Air Quality Management District (SCAQMD) Test Method 25.1,
which is available from EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Determination of the API gravity of crude oil shall be performed in accordance with ASTM Method D 287. 
