2 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 007 0146 intable -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=5 f=1 -->
a
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=1 f=1 -->
Day means a 24 hour period from the time of leak detection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 007 0146 intable -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=5 f=1 -->
b
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=1 f=1 -->
Unless prohibited by state safety standards or 29 CFR part 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1910. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</TABLE>

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(j) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gasoline Transfer and Dispensing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of paragraphs (j)(1) through (j)(7) of this section shall apply to any owner or operator of a gasoline
dispensing facility. For the purposes of this paragraph, the affected areas include the Sacramento Metro Area, the
Los Angeles-South Coast Air Basin Area, and the Ventura County Area as described for ozone in 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraph (j) of this section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not defined herein
shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Alteration(s) and/or repair(s) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
of a gasoline storage and/or dispensing facility is any of the following: the replacement of one or more existing storage
tank(s); the removal or addition of storage tank(s) or dispensing nozzle(s), piping or any other component; the replacement
of storage tanks, dispensing nozzle(s), piping or any other component with different characteristics from those
of the existing or original equipment; or any excavation (exposure to view by digging) of an existing gasoline storage
tank and/or the underground liquid piping from the storage tank(s) to the gasoline dispenser(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Balance system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is a Phase II (Stage II) vapor recovery system that operates on the principle of vapor displacement. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00397 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
CARB certified vapor recovery system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any Phase I or Phase II vapor recovery system which has been certified by the California Air Resources Board (CARB)
pursuant to section 41954 of the California Health and Safety Code as capable of recovering or processing displaced
gasoline vapors to an efficiency of ninety-five (95) percent or greater. For the purpose of this section, the term
certified shall refer to CARB certification. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
CARB executive orders(s)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 is the procedure, pursuant to Sections 39600, 39601, and 41954 of the California Health and Safety Code and Title 17
Section 94001 of the California Code of Regulations, used by the California Air Resources Board (CARB) to approve
the certification, modification of a certification, or recertification of vapor recovery systems and/or related
equipment. Copies of CARB Executive Orders can be obtained from CARB, Compliance Division, P.O. Box 2815, Sacramento,
CA, 95812.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gasoline 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any petroleum distillate and/or mixture of petroleum distillates and oxygenates used as a fuel in spark ignition
engines and having a Reid vapor pressure of four pounds per square inch or greater.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gasoline storage and dispensing facility means 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
an aggregate of one or more stationary storage tanks, any of which is subject to the provisions of paragraphs (j)(3)
through (j)(7) of this section, together with dispensers and control equipment required by the section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Hold-open latch 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is a certified device which is an integral part of the dispensing nozzle and is manufactured specifically for the purpose
of dispensing gasoline without requiring the consumer's constant physical contact with the nozzle during fueling
operations.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Insertion interlock 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any certified mechanism which is an integral part of a bellows-equipped dispensing nozzle which prohibits the
dispensing of fuel unless the bellows is compressed.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Liquid removal device 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is a device designed specifically to remove liquid from the vapor return portion of a coaxial hose.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Liquid tight 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a liquid leak rate not exceeding three drops per minute.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Motor vehicle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any self-propelled vehicle registered or which requires registration for use on the highway.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Owner/operator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any person who owns, leases, operates, controls or supervises the operation of a gasoline dispensing facility.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Phase I 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stage I 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is gasoline vapor recovery during the transfer of gasoline into or out of stationary tanks at a gasoline dispensing
facility.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Phase II 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stage II 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is gasoline vapor recovery during motor vehicle or utility equipment fueling operations from stationary tanks at
gasoline dispensing facilities.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rebuilt equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any component of a vapor recovery system that has undergone repair or replacement of any or all of its internal parts.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reid vapor pressure 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the absolute vapor pressure of volatile crude oil and volatile non-viscus petroleum liquids, except liquified
petroleum gases, as determined by ASTM D323&hyph;89.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Submerged fill tube 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any fill tube, the discharge opening of which is entirely submerged, when the liquid level above the bottom of the
tank is: 15.2 cm (6 inches), for tanks filled from the top, except for flat bottom tanks where the liquid level above
the bottom is 7.6 cm (3 in.); or 45.7 cm (18 inches) for tanks filled from the side.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Top off 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is the attempt to dispense gasoline to a motor vehicle or utility equipment fuel tank after the dispensing nozzle primary
shutoff mechanism has engaged. The filling of those class of vehicle tanks which, because of the configuration of
the fill pipe, cause premature activation of the primary shutoff, shall not be considered topping off.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vacuum assist system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any Phase II vapor recovery system that utilizes a pump, blower, or other vacuum-producing device. Vacuum assist
systems may also incorporate an incinerator to process any excess vapors generated by the collection system.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vapor tight 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the detection of less than 10,000 ppm hydrocarbon concentration, as determined by 40 CFR part 60, appendix A,
Method 21, using an appropriate analyzer calibrated with methane. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00398 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Gasoline Transfer Into Stationary Storage Tanks (Phase I). 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An owner/operator shall not transfer, permit the transfer or provide equipment for the transfer of gasoline into
from any tank truck, trailer or railroad car into any stationary storage tank with a capacity of 950 liters (251 gallons)
or more unless all of the following conditions are met:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Such tank is equipped with a permanent submerged fill tube.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Such tank is equipped with a CARB certified vapor recovery system at, or above 95 percent control efficiency, which
is maintained and operated according to the manufacturers specifications.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) All vapor return lines are connected between the tank truck, trailer or railroad tank car, and the stationary storage
tank and all associated hoses, fittings, and couplings are maintained in a vapor tight condition.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) The hatch on any tank truck, trailer, or railroad tank car shall not be opened for more than three minutes for each
visual inspection, provided that:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Transfer or pumping has been stopped for at least 3 minutes prior to opening; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The hatch is closed before transfer or pumping is resumed.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Underground tank lines are gravity drained, and above-ground tanks are equipped with dry breaks such that upon
line disconnect the liquid leak rate does not exceed 3 drops per minute.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) As of [Insert date of publication of the final rule], an owner/operator shall not install a coaxial Phase I vapor
recovery system at a gasoline dispensing facility unless the Phase I system was certified after January 1, 1994. In
addition, an owner/operator shall not install a Phase I vapor recovery system unless that system incorporates certified
poppetted drybreaks or spring-loaded vapor check valves on the vapor return coupler of the system.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) As of one year after [Insert date of publication of the final rule], all open vent pipes on stationary tanks at gasoline
dispensing facilities shall be equipped with a pressure-vacuum relief valve. Unless otherwise specified in the
applicable CARB executive order, pressure relief shall be set at 3 inches water column and vacuum relief shall be set
at 8 inches water column. For the purposes of this paragraph (j), vent pipes of gasoline storage tanks may be manifolded
to a single valve when the storage tanks are manifolded according to the applicable CARB executive order.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(H) As of [Insert date of publication of the final rule], any time a gasoline storage tank or associated piping is replaced
or installed this spill box must be equiped with an intregal vapor-tight drain valve to return spilled gasoline to
the storage tank.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(I) Equipment subject to this paragraph (j) is operated and maintained, according to all of the following requirements:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All fill tubes are equipped with vapor-tight covers, including gaskets;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All dry breaks are equipped with vapor-tight seals and dust covers;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Fixed or Spring-Loaded coaxial fill tubes are operated so that there is no obstruction of vapor passage from the storage
tank back to the tank truck, trailer, or railroad tank car;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The fill tube assembly, including fill tube, fittings and gaskets, is maintained to prevent vapor leakage from any
portion of the vapor recovery system;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All storage tank vapor return lines without dry breaks are equipped with vapor-tight covers, including gaskets.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gasoline Transfer Into Vehicle Fuel Tanks (Phase II). 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An owner/operator shall not transfer, or permit the transfer, or provide equipment for the transfer of gasoline from
a stationary storage tank into any motor vehicle fuel tank of greater than 19 liters (5 gallons) capacity unless all
of the following conditions are met:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The dispensing unit used to transfer the gasoline from the stationary storage tank to the motor vehicle fuel tank
is equipped with a CARB certified vapor recovery system.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The vapor recovery system and associated components are operated and maintained in a vapor-tight and liquid-tight
manner in accordance with the manufacturer's specifications and the applicable CARB certification.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) As of [Insert date of publication of the final rule], an owner/operator shall not install any balance system vapor
recovery nozzle unless a vapor check valve is located in the nozzle. In addition, a balance system shall not be operated
with more than one check valve per nozzle and hose assembly.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) As of one year after [Insert date of publication of the final rule], the nominal inside diameter of the connection
between the riser and dispenser cabinet shall not be less than 0.75 inches. If flexible tubing is used for this connection,
the material shall be listed for use with gasoline and shall be capable of maintaining electrical continuity between
the riser and dispenser.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) As of one year after [Insert date of publication of the final rule], an owner/operator shall not sell, offer for
sale, or install a bellows-equipped vapor recovery nozzle unless it is equipped with a certified insertion interlock
mechanism.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) As of one year after [Insert date of publication of the final rule], an owner/operator shall not install or operate
a vapor recovery nozzle unless it is equipped with a coaxial hose.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) As of one year after [Insert date of publication of the final rule], all liquid removal devices required by CARB
executive orders shall be maintained to achieve a minimum liquid removal rate of five milliliters per gallon transferred.
This standard shall apply at dispensing rates exceeding five gallons per minute, unless a higher removal rate is specified
by the Executive Order.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(H) As of [Insert date of publication of the final rule], any gasoline storage or dispensing facility that commences
alterations or repairs shall comply with the equipment standards of paragraphs (j)(3)(ii) (C) through (G) of this
section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(I) Equipment subject to this section shall be operated and maintained with none of the following defects:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Absence or disconnection of any component required to be used in the CARB executive order(s) that certified the system.

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00399 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A vapor hose which is crimped or flattened such that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the vapor passage is blocked, or the pressure drop through 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the vapor hose exceeds by a factor of two or more the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements in the system certified in the CARB Executive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Order(s) applicable to the system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A nozzle boot which is torn in one or more of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following manner: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Triangular-shaped or similar tear 1/2 inch or more 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to a side, or hole 1/2 inch or more in diameter or, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Slit 1 inch or more in length. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Faceplate or flexible cone which is damaged in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following manner: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) For balance nozzles and for nozzles for aspirator 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and educator assist type systems, damage shall be such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that the capability to achieve a seal with a fill pipe 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
interface is affected for 1/4 of the circumference of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the faceplate (accumulated). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) For nozzles for vacuum assist-type systems, more 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than 1/4 of the flexible cone missing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Nozzle shutoff mechanisms which malfunction in any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manner. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
6
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Vapor return lines, including such components as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
swivels, anti-recirculation valves and underground piping, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which malfunction or are blocked, or restricted such that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressure drop through the lines exceeds by factor of two or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
more requirements specified in the CARB Executive Order(s) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that certified the system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
7
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Vapor processing unit which is inoperative. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
8
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Vacuum producing device which is inoperative. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
9
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Pressure/vacuum relief valves, vapor check valves, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dry breaks which are inoperative. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
10
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any equipment defect which is identified in an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Executive Order certifying a system pursuant to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Certification Procedures incorporated in Section 94001 of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Title 17, California Code of Regulations, as substantially 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
impairing the effectiveness of the system in reducing air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contaminants. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
