<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) For permanent (non-decal) signs, two single-sided 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or one double-sided sign(s) per two (2) dispensers. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
iii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All signs shall be readable from a distance of 6 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
feet or more. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) A dispenser that is never used to fuel motor vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall have a sign posted on it restricting its use for vehicles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) Gasoline shall not be stored in open container(s) of any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
size or handled in any other manner (spillage, spraying, etc.) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that permit gasoline or gasoline vapors to enter the atmosphere, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contaminate the ground, or the sewer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(H) The failure of an owner/operator to meet any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements of paragraphs (j)(3) (i), (ii), or (iii) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section shall constitute a violation. Such equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined to be in violation shall be tagged ``Out-of-Order.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(I) Except during repair activity, the ``Out-of-Order'' tag 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in paragraph (j)(3)(iii)(H) of this section shall not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be removed and the tagged equipment shall not be used, permitted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to be used, or provided for use unless all of the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions are satisfied: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The tagged equipment has been repaired, replaced, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
adjusted, as necessary; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The District, Office of Operations, has been notified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the repairs by completing and signing the form supplied 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the District; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) The tagged equipment has been reinspected and/or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authorized for use by the District. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Exemptions. The provisions of this section shall not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply to the transfer of gasoline into or from any stationary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tank if its monthly throughput is used exclusively for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fueling of implements of husbandry, such as vehicles defined in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Division 16 (Section 36000 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
et seq.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of the California Vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Code, provided such a tank is equipped with a submerged fill tube 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and its storage capacity is less than or equal to 550 gallons 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2,082 liters). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compliance Schedule. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The owner/operator of a new facility subject to this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section shall comply with the provisions of this section at the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
time gasoline receiving and/or dispensing is initiated. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The owner/operator of any altered and/or repaired 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facility, who was previously exempted from Phase I or Phase II 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vapor control requirements shall comply with the provisions of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section at the time gasoline receiving and/or dispensing is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
initiated after completion of the alteration and/or repair. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The owner/operator of any other existing facility, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
who was previously exempt from Phase I or Phase II vapor control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements, and who has not earlier been required to come into 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance, shall achieve compliance by January 1, 1996. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) Testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) For new or altered gasoline storage or dispensing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities, once the system is in operational condition and ready 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for use, testing to verify the proper installation and function 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the entire system (both infrastructure plumbing and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aboveground equipment) shall be conducted. Tests of Phase II 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
systems at gasoline dispensing stations shall be conducted in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with the following test procedures as found in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appendix J of the EPA document, ``Technical Guidance_Stage II 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Vapor Recovery Systems for Control of Vehicle Refueling Emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a Gasoline Dispensing Facilities,'' Vol. II (EPA&hyph;450/3&hyph;91&hyph;022b), 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
November 1991: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Bay Area Source Test Procedure ST&hyph;30, Leak Test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Procedure, or San Diego Test Procedure TP&hyph;91&hyph;1, Pressure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Decay/Leak Test Procedure. In addition, CARB Test Procedure TP&hyph;201.3 may be used. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Bay Area Source Test Procedure ST&hyph;27, Dynamic Back 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Pressure, or San Diego Test Procedure TP&hyph;91&hyph;2, Pressure Drop vs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Flow/liquid Blockage Test Procedure. In addition, CARB Test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Procedure TP&hyph;201.2 may be used; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Bay Area Source Test Procedure ST&hyph;37, Liquid Removal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Devices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) In addition to the above tests, Phase I efficiency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
testing will be done in accordance with CARB TP&hyph;201.1. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Testing may be done by the facility or by a testing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
company provided that the testing meets the minimum criteria 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
established by CARB for such tests. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Reverification of the function of the Phase I or Phase 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
II vapor recovery system shall be performed as shown below or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upon alteration or repair of any gasoline storage or dispensing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facility. Functional tests may also be performed upon request by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA or the local Air Pollution Control District. Where multiple 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tests are specified, a leak or blockage found by any method 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
constitutes a violation of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
