<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(A) A static pressure leak test using ST&hyph;30, TP&hyph;91&hyph;2 or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
CARB TP&hyph;201.3 shall be performed at least once per calendar year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or upon alteration or repair of facilities equipped with a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vacuum-assist Phase II system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) A static pressure leak test using ST&hyph;30, TP&hyph;91&hyph;2 or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
CARB TP&hyph;201.3 shall be performed at least once every two years or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upon alteration or repair of facilities equipped with a balanced 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Phase II system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) A liquid blockage test using ST&hyph;27, TP&hyph;91&hyph;2, or CARB 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
TP&hyph;201.2 shall be performed at least every five years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) For existing gasoline storage and dispensing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities, if the facility has not been verified for functional 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Phase I or Phase II vapor recovery systems within the last four 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years before the date of promulgation of this section, then 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
functional tests shall be performed at the facility within one 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
year of the date of promulgation of this section. Facilities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which have been tested within four years and have the test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
results documented, shall perform the reverification tests within 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
five years from the date of the tests. All other existing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities shall be tested within one year of the date of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
promulgation of this section. Reverification of static pressure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
integrity shall be performed within one year after promulgation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section for vacuum-assist systems or two years after 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
promulgation or after the last test, whichever is earliest, for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
balanced systems. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) Recordkeeping.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All permits or licenses to operate the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facility or to operate a specific system at the facility shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
current at all times. The records required in paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(j)(7) (i) through (iv) of this section shall be maintained 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at each facility for a minimum of five years, and should be made 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
available to EPA and local enforcement personnel upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Verification that the vapor recovery system meets or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exceeds the requirements of the tests specified in paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(j)(6) (i), (ii), and (iv) of this section shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintained. The test results shall be dated and shall contain 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
names, addresses, and telephone numbers of the parties 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
responsible for the system installation and/or testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) All maintenance conducted on any part of the vapor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recovery system shall be logged on a maintenance record 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintained in chronological order showing dates, description of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any equipment replaced with its location, and a description of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the system problem which resulted in repairs. The log shall also 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
indicate the time period and duration of each malfunction of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) A file of all inspection reports issued by inspecting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agencies shall be maintained in chronological order. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) A chronologically organized file of all compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
records issued by regulating agencies shall be maintained 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
separately from the inspection reports. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(k) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emissions from Waste Burning. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 On or after January 1, 1996, any person 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conducting agricultural burning or open burning shall comply with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the requirements of paragraphs (k) (4) and (5) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
For the purposes of this section, the affected areas include the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento Metro Area, the Los Angeles-South Coast Air Basin 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Area, and the Ventura County Area as described for ozone in 40 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of paragraph (k) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Agricultural burning
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means open outdoor fires used in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following operations: agricultural operations; forest 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
management; range improvement; improvement of land for wildlife 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and game habitat; disease or pest prevention; operation or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintenance of a system for the delivery of water used in any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agricultural operation, forest management, range improvement, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
land improvement for wildlife and game habitat, and disease or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pest prevention operation; wildland vegetation management. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Agricultural operations
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the production of materials 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
produced wholly from operations in the growing and harvesting of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
crops or raising of fowl or animals for the primary purpose of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
making a profit, of providing a livelihood, or of conducting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agricultural research or instruction by an educational 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
institution. In connection with open burning of materials 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
produced from agricultural operations are the burning of grass 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and weeds in or adjacent to fields in cultivation or being 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prepared for cultivation, and the burning of materials not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
produced wholly from agricultural operations, but which are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
intimately related to the growing or harvesting of crops and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which are used in the field (e.g., trays for drying raisins, date 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
palm protection paper, and fertilizer and pesticide sacks or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
containers where the sacks or containers are emptied in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
field.) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Designated agency
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any agency designated by the State 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Air Resources Board as having authority to issue agricultural 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
burning permits. The U.S. Forest Service, the California 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Department of Forestry, local air districts, local fire control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agencies are designated for their respective jurisdictions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Forest management burning
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the use of open fires, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
part of a forest management practice, to remove forest debris or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for forest management practices which include timber operations, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
silvicultural practices or forest protection practices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Local air district
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any of the following districts: El 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Dorado County Air Pollution Control District (APCD), Feather 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
River Air Quality Management District (AQMD), Placer County APCD, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento Metropolitan AQMD, South Coast AQMD, Ventura County 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
APCD, Yolo-Solano APCD. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
No-burn day
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a day on which agricultural burning and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
open burning are prohibited by the EPA, State Air Resources 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Board, or local air district due to a predicted exceedence of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
State ambient air quality standard (0.09 ppm) for ozone. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Open burning
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means planned open burning of trash, leaves, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and refuse from all activities except agricultural operations, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
forest management, range improvement, improvement of land for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
wildlife and game habitat, disease or pest prevention, operation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or maintenance of a system for the delivery of water used in any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agricultural operation, forest management, range improvement, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
land improvement for wildlife and game habitat, and disease or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pest prevention operation, and wildland vegetation management 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
where the products of combustion are not directed through a flue. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Permissive-burn
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 day means a day on which agricultural 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
burning and open burning are allowed by the EPA, State Air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Resources Board, or local air district. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Range improvement burning
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the use of open fires to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
remove vegetation for a wildlife, game or livestock habitat or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for the initial establishment of an agricultural practice on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
previously uncultivated land. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Silvicultural practices
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means establish, development, care 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and reproduction of stands of timber. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Timber operations
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means cutting or removal of timber or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other forest vegetation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Waste burning
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means agricultural burning, range management 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
burning, forest management burning, and open burning. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wildland vegetation management burning
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the use of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prescribed burning conducted by a public agency, or through a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cooperative agreement or contract involving a public agency, to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
burn land predominantly covered with chaparral, trees, grass, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standing brush. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
No-burn day determination.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A no-burn day may be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
declared by the USEPA, State Air Resources Board, or local air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
district if an exceedence of the State ambient air quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard for ozone (0.09 ppm) is predicted. The following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions will be evaluated each day for predicting the ozone 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
level for the following day. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

