criteria specified in paragraph (m)(4)(ii) of this section shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comply with the monitoring requirements of paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m)(6)(ii)(C) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Any owner or operator of a diesel stationary internal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion engine that claims an exemption from the standards of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (m)(3) of this section because of the exemption 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
criteria specified in paragraph (m)(4)(viii) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall comply with the monitoring and reporting requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (m)(4)(viii) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. For the purposes of paragraphs (m)(1) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
through (m)(7) of this section, the following definitions shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply. All terms not defined herein shall have the meaning given 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Diesel engine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a compression ignited two or four-stroke 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine in which liquid fuel injected into the combustion chamber 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ignites when the air charge has been compressed to a temperature 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sufficiently high for auto-ignition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emergency standby engine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an internal combustion engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used only when normal power line or natural gas service fails, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for the emergency pumping of water for either fire protection or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flood relief. An emergency standby engine may not be operated to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
supplement a primary power source when the load capacity or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rating of the primary power source has been either reached or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exceeded. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Engine rating
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the output of an engine as determined by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the engine manufacturer and listed on the nameplate of the unit, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regardless of any derating. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Higher heating value (HHV)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the total heat liberated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
per mass of fuel burned (Btu per pound), when fuel and dry air at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard conditions undergo complete combustion and all resultant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
products are brought to their standard states at standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions. If certification of the HHV is not provided by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
third party fuel supplier, it shall be determined by one of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following test methods: ASTM D2015&hyph;85 for solid fuels; ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D240&hyph;87 or ASTM D2382&hyph;88 for liquid hydrocarbon fuels; or ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D1826&hyph;88 or ASTM D1945&hyph;81 in conjunction with ASTM D3588&hyph;89 for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gaseous fuels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Lean-burn engine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any two or four-stroke spark-ignited 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine that is not a rich-burn engine. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Maintenance operation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the use of an emergency standby 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine and fuel system during testing, repair and routine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintenance to verify its readiness for emergency standby use. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Output
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the shaft work output from an engine plus the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
energy reclaimed by any useful heat recovery system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Peak load
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the maximum instantaneous operating load. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Permitted capacity factor
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the annual permitted fuel 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
use divided by the manufacturers specified maximum fuel 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
consumption times 8,760 hours per year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rich-burn engine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a two or four-stroke spark-ignited 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine where the manufacturers original recommended operating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air/fuel ratio divided by the stoichiometric air/fuel ratio is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
less than or equal to 1.1. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Shutdown
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the period of time a unit is cooled from its 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
normal operating temperature to cold or ambient temperature. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Startup
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the period of time a unit is heated from cold 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or ambient temperature to its normal operating temperature as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified by the manufacturer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stationary internal combustion engine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any internal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion engine of the reciprocating type that is either 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
attached to a foundation at a facility or is portable equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operated at a specific facility for more than 90 days in any 12-month period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stoichiometric air/fuel ratio
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the air/fuel ratio where 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all fuel and all oxygen in the air/fuel mixture will be consumed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any diesel, lean-burn, or rich-burn stationary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
internal combustion engine as defined in this paragraph. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Waste gas
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the fuel gas produced at either waste-water/sewage treatment facilities or landfills containing no more 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than 25 percent by volume supplemental gas. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



