<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of paragraphs (m) (3), 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5), (6), and (7) of this section shall not apply to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following, unless otherwise specified: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Engines rated at less than 50 brake horsepower. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Engines operated at less than 200 hours per calendar 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
year. Owners or operators that claim an exemption from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standards of paragraph (m)(3) of this section by means of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph shall comply with the monitoring requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (m)(6)(ii)(C) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Emergency standby engines operated during either an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emergency or maintenance operation. Maintenance operation shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be limited to 50 hours per calendar year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Engines used in a laboratory for the sole purpose of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conducting research or teaching. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Engines used directly and exclusively for agricultural 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operations necessary for the growing of crops or the raising of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fowl or animals. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Engine test stands used for evaluating engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) Diesel engines used to power cranes necessary for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emergency evacuation or safety of personnel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) Diesel engines rated at less than 125 brake 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
horsepower and operated at less than 200,000 horsepower-hours per 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calendar year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) To demonstrate that a unit is operated less than 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
200,000 horsepower-hours in a calendar year, the owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operator shall install, operate, and maintain in calibration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment that continuously monitors and records elapsed time of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation. For each year, the owner or operator shall also keep 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an operating log of start and stop times, type and quantity of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fuel used, and cumulative annual hours and horsepower-hours of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation for each unit. Each operating log shall be maintained 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at the plant at which the unit is located for a period of five 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years. The operating log shall be made available to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The owner or operator of any unit that claims an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exemption from the requirements of paragraph (m)(3) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section under paragraph (m)(4)(viii)(A) of this section shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notify the Administrator within 7 days if the unit is ever 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operated equal to or greater than 200,000 horsepower-hours in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calendar year. If the unit is ever operated equal to or greater 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than 200,000 horsepower-hours in a calendar year, the exemption 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be permanently withdrawn and the owner or operator shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject to the compliance schedule in paragraph (m)(5)(iv) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section and the applicable requirements of paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m) (3), (6), and (7) of this section. Nothing in this paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall prevent EPA from bringing enforcement action for violation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of paragraph (m)(3) of this section or for failure to demonstrate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with this paragraph (m)(3) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compliance schedule. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Any owner or operator of a unit in existence prior to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the date of adoption of this section that does not need to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
retrofit the unit, install new control equipment, or decrease 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
annual operating hours to comply with the requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (m)(3) of this section shall demonstrate compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with all of the applicable requirements of this section by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
May 15, 1995. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any owner or operator of a unit in existence prior to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the date of adoption of this section that must retrofit the unit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to comply with the requirements of paragraphs (m)(3)(i) (A), (C) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or (D), (m)(3)(ii), and (m)(3)(iii) of this section, shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrate compliance in accordance with the applicable schedule 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in paragraph (m)(5)(ii) (A) or (B) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Any owner or operator that chooses to convert the unit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to electric power shall demonstrate compliance with all of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable requirements of this section by May 15, 1999. Any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owner or operator of a unit to which this paragraph is applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall meet the following increments of progress: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) By January 1, 1997, apply for all authority-to-
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
construct permits required by the local Air Pollution Control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
District for conversion of the unit to electric power, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) By January 1, 1999, commence conversion of the unit to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
electric power, as approved by the local Air Pollution Control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
District, to demonstrate compliance by May 15, 1999. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Any owner or operator that chooses to retrofit the unit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with combustion controls or install new control equipment shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrate compliance with all of the applicable requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section by May 15, 1997. Any owner or operator of a unit to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which this paragraph is applicable shall meet the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
increments of progress: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) By January 1, 1996, apply for all authority-to-
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
construct permits required by the local Air Pollution Control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
District for all retrofits and/or additions of new control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) By January 1, 1997, commence construction of all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
retrofits and/or additions of new control equipment, as approved 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the local Air Pollution Control District, to demonstrate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance by May 15, 1997. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Any owner or operator of a new unit that is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
constructed on and after the date of adoption of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall apply for, and receive approval of, all authority-to- 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
construct permits required by the local Air Pollution Control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
District prior to beginning construction of the unit. The owner 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or operator shall demonstrate that the unit will be operated in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with all of the applicable requirements of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section within 60 days after the date of the initial startup of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) On and after the date of adoption of this section, any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owner or operator of a diesel engine that claims an exempt from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the requirements of paragraph (m)(3) of this section which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operates the unit equal to or greater than 200,000 brake 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
horsepower hours in a calendar year shall demonstrate compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in accordance with the applicable schedule specified in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m)(5)(iv) (A) or (B) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
