<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iv) The ppmv CO and VOC emission limits required by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraphs (m)(3) (ii) and (iii) of this section, respectively, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be established during the initial compliance test for NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions. The CO and VOC emission limits established for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determining subsequent compliance shall be documented in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable certification report required under paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m)(6)(i)(C) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(n) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Biomass boilers or steam generators. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Any owner or operator of a biomass 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
boiler or steam generator with a rated heat input capacity equal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to or greater than 5 million British thermal units per hour 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(mmBtu/hr) and an annual heat input equal to or greater than 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
9 billion British thermal units per year (10
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
9
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Btu/yr) shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comply with the applicable requirements of paragraphs (n) (1) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
through (7) of this section. For the purposes of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph, the affected area includes the Sacramento Metro Area 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as described for ozone in 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(2) Definitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of paragraphs (n)(1) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
through (n)(7) of this section, the following definitions shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply. All terms not defined herein shall have the meaning given 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Annual heat input
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the actual amount of heat released 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by fuels burned in a unit during a 12 calendar month rolling 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
period, based on the fuel's higher heating value. The annual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
heat input shall be calculated as the sum of the previous 12 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
monthly fuel use rates multiplied by the fuel's higher heating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
value. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Biomass
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any solid organic material used as a fuel 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source for boilers or steam generators including, but not limited 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to, wood, almond shells, or agricultural waste. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Biomass boiler or steam generator
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any combustion 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment used in any institutional, commercial, or industrial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation that is designed to burn biomass to produce steam, heat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
water and/or other fluids, and/or generate electricity. A 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
biomass boiler or steam generator does not include any waste heat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recovery boiler that is used to recover sensible heat from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exhaust of a combustion turbine or any unfired waste heat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recovery boiler that is used to recover sensible heat from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exhaust of any combustion equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
British thermal unit (Btu)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the amount of heat required 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to raise the temperature of one pound of water from 59
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F to 60
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at one atmosphere. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heat input
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the chemical heat released due to fuel 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion in a unit, using the higher heating value of the fuel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
This does not include the sensible heat of incoming combustion 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Higher heating value (HHV)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the total heat liberated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
per mass of fuel burned (Btu per pound), when fuel and dry air at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard conditions undergo complete combustion and all resultant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
products are brought to their standard states at standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions. If certification of the HHV is not provided by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
third party fuel supplier, it shall be determined by one of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following test methods: ASTM D2015&hyph;85 for solid fuels; ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D240&hyph;87 or ASTM D2382&hyph;88 for liquid hydrocarbon fuels; or ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D1826&hyph;88 or ASTM D1945&hyph;81 in conjunction with ASTM D3588&hyph;89 for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gaseous fuels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Municipal-type solid waste means household, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
commercial/retail, and/or institutional waste. Household waste 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
includes material discarded by single and multiple residential 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dwellings, hotels, motels, and other similar permanent or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
temporary housing establishments or facilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Commercial/retail waste includes material discarded by stores, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
offices, restaurants, warehouses, nonmanufacturing activities at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
industrial facilities, and other similar establishments or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities. Institutional waste includes material discarded by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
schools, hospitals, nonmanufacturing activities at prisons and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
government facilities and other similar establishments or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
emissions means the sum of nitric oxides and nitrogen 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dioxide in the flue gas, collectively expressed as nitrogen 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dioxide. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rated heat input capacity
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the heat input capacity 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified on the nameplate of the combustion unit. If the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion unit has been altered or modified such that its 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maximum heat input is different than the heat input capacity 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified on the nameplate, the new maximum heat input shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered as the rated heat input capacity. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Shutdown
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the period of time a unit is cooled from its 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
normal operating temperature to cold or ambient temperature. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Startup
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the period of time a unit is heated from cold 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or ambient temperature to its normal operating temperature as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified by the manufacturer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unit
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any biomass boiler or steam generator as defined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in this paragraph. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means wood, wood residue, bark, or any derivative fuel 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or residue thereof, in any form, including but not limited to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sawdust, sanderdust, wood chips, scraps, slabs, millings, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shavings, and processed pellets made from wood or other forest 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
residues. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(3) Standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) No owner or operator of a biomass boiler or steam 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
generator shall cause to be discharged into the atmosphere any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gases that contain NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 in excess of one of the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standards, which ever is less stringent: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 70 parts per million (ppm) corrected to 12 percent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
volume stack gas carbon dioxide (CO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) on a rolling 3 hour average 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dry basis; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) 50 percent (0.50) of the NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 concentration in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
uncontrolled exhaust gas stream. A controlled ppm NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 limit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be established in accordance with the requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (n)(7)(ii) of this section for the purpose of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrating continuous compliance with the 50 percent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The owner or operator of any biomass boiler or steam 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
generator subject to one of the standards in paragraph (n)(3)(i) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section shall establish a controlled ppm carbon monoxide 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
