<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (n)(6)(i)(C) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(o) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emissions of oxides of nitrogen from stationary gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
turbines. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of paragraph (o) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section, the affected area includes the Sacramento Metro 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Area as described for ozone in 40 CFR 81.305. Any owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operator of a stationary gas turbine with a rated heat output 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capacity equal to or greater than 0.3 megawatt (MW) shall comply 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the applicable requirements of paragraphs (o) (1) through 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (7) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of paragraph (o) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
British thermal unit (Btu)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the amount of heat required 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to raise the temperature of one pound of water from 59
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F to 60
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at one atmosphere. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Chemical processing stationary gas turbine unit
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
turbine that vents its exhaust gases into the operating stream of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a chemical process. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cogeneration cycle stationary gas turbine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 unit means a gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
turbine that is operated both for the simultaneous production of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shaft work and for the recovery of useful thermal energy from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exhaust gases or waste steam as defined by Section 25134 of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California Public Resources Code. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Combined cycle stationary gas turbine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 unit means a gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
turbine that is operated both for the production of electrical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
energy from shaft work and the useful energy produced from heat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recovered from its exhaust gases. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emergency standby stationary gas turbine
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 unit means a gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
turbine that is operated only as a mechanical or electrical power 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source for a facility when the primary power source has been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rendered inoperable, except due to power interruption pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an interruptible power supply agreement. This does not include 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
utility company electrical power plant units. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exhaust after treatment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a control method for the post- 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion reduction of NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emissions, such as selective 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
catalytic reduction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Higher heating value (HHV)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the total heat liberated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
per mass of fuel burned (Btu per pound), when fuel and dry air at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard conditions undergo complete combustion and all resultant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
products are brought to their standard states at standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions. If certification of the HHV is not provided by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
third party fuel supplier, it shall be determined by one of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following test methods: ASTM D2015&hyph;85 for solid fuels; ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D240&hyph;87 or ASTM D2382&hyph;88 for liquid hydrocarbon fuels; or ASTM 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
D1826&hyph;88 or ASTM D1945&hyph;81 in conjunction with ASTM D3588&hyph;89 for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gaseous fuels. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
LHV
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the lower heating value of a fuel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
emissions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the sum of nitric oxides and nitrogen 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dioxide in the flue gas, collectively expressed as nitrogen 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dioxide. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
