<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The requirements of paragraphs (o) (3), (5), (6), and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) of this section shall not apply to the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Laboratory units used in research and testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Units operated exclusively for firefighting and/or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flood control. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Chemical processing gas turbine units. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Peaking Units and Emergency Standby Units. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The requirements of paragraphs (o) (3), (5), (6), and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) of this section shall not apply to peaking units or emergency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standby units that operate less than 200 hours per calendar year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
To demonstrate that a unit is operated less than 200 hours in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calendar year, the owner or operator shall install, operate, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
