<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Retention of Records. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All records maintained pursuant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to this section shall be retained and available for inspection by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Administrator for the previous five-year period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(q) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reasonably Available Control Technology for Emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of Volatile Organic Compounds at SierraPine, Ltd. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of paragraph (q) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section shall apply to the owner or operator of SierraPine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Limited (SierraPine), a medium density fiberboard plant, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conducting operations at 4300 Dominguez Road, Rocklin, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraph (q) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fiber drier 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a device which uses steam-generated heat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to reduce the moisture content of wood fibers. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fiberboard press 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a device which uses heat and pressure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to form fiberboard from a preformed mat of wood fiber and resin. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Press line 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a series of operations occurring within the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
press building including mat forming, fiberboard pressing, board 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unloading, and board cooling. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Press vent 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a device used to exhaust fiberboard press 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
line emissions from the press line building. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood waste-fired boiler 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a combustion device which uses 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
wood, wood fiber, sanderdust, or other wood byproducts as fuel to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
produce steam for process operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The owner or operator of SierraPine shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrate compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(q)(3) (i) through (iii) of this section by January 1, 1996. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Emissions of unburned gaseous combustibles, including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VOC and carbon monoxide, from the wood waste-fired boiler shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be minimized by maintaining proper combustion conditions. Proper 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion conditions include but are not limited to optimum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion temperature, fuel moisture content, fuel firing rate, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and sufficient secondary air. The owner or operator of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facility shall submit for approval by EPA a determination of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proper combustion conditions. The source shall incorporate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
additional combustion conditions as recommended in writing by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) A capture and control system shall be installed and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operated to reduce VOC emissions from the wood fiber driers and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which meets the following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The capture and control system shall achieve a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minimum 95% VOC control efficiency. Demonstration of VOC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control efficiency shall be performed in accordance with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
methods specified in paragraph (q)(6) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The VOC capture and control system shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operated at all times during the operation of the wood fiber 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
driers. The capture and control system shall be maintained 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and operated in a manner which consistently achieves the VOC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control efficiency stated in paragraph (q)(3)(ii)(A) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) A capture and control system shall be installed and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operated to reduce VOC emissions from press vents and which meets 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The VOC capture and control system shall achieve 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a minimum 90% overall VOC control efficiency. Demonstration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of VOC control efficiency shall be performed in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the methods specified in paragraph (q)(6) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The VOC capture and control system shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operated at all times during the operation of the press 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vents. The VOC capture and control system shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintained and operated in a manner which consistently 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
achieves the overall VOC control efficiency stated in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (q)(3)(iii)(A) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The owner or operator of SierraPine shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be subject to the following reporting requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) A compliance plan shall be submitted to the EPA prior 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to installation of any VOC capture and control system or by July 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1, 1995, whichever comes first. The compliance plan shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
include a description of how the requirements of paragraph (q) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section shall be met, including: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A description of the proposed VOC capture and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control system to be installed at the facility including the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following information at a minimum: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
