<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to meet the requirements of paragraphs (q)(3)(ii)(B) and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(q)(3)(iii)(B) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Compliance test dates and test methods to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used to satisfy the requirements of paragraph (q)(3)(ii)(A) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) An annual certification of compliance shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submitted to the EPA on or before January 1 of each year. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certification of compliance shall include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A declaration that the facility is in compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with all of the requirements of paragraph (q) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The results of any compliance testing performed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
during the previous year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) A description of any process upsets that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
occurred during the previous year that resulted in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
noncompliance with the emission limit or proper combustion 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions as approved by EPA stated in paragraph (q)(3) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section and corrective actions taken to correct the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
noncompliance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) By January 1, 1996, the owner or operator of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facility shall submit for approval by EPA a determination of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proper combustion conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recordkeeping. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The owner or operator of SierraPine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall maintain records on site sufficient to show compliance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (q) of this section for a period of five years. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Records shall be made available to the EPA upon request. At a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minimum the following information shall be recorded: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Process data sufficient to show that efficient 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion practices are being utilized at the wood waste-fired 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
boiler. These data will include, at a minimum, the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Fuel feed rate and composition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Combustion temperature. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Fuel moisture content. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Percentage of overfire air. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Boiler load. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) VOC capture and control system operating parameters 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identified by the EPA following review and approval of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance plan submitted pursuant to paragraph (q)(4)(i) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Measurements of destruction or removal efficiency shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be determined in accordance with 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Method 25. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

