<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(r) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
RACT Determination_Michigan-California Lumber 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Company. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The provisions of paragraph (r) of this section shall apply 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the ``Michigan-California Lumber Company'' or any subsequent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owner or operator of the Michigan-California Lumber Facility 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
located at 3970 Carson Road, Camino, California. All provisions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are RACT and the emissions standards only apply to the main wood 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
waste-fired boiler (Boiler 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=6 f=1 -->
#
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
3) at the facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purpose of paragraph (r) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Air Pollution Control Officer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the Executive Officer, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or his or her delegate, or an air quality management district or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an air pollution control district. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Boiler 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any external combustion equipment fired with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any fuel used to produce heat or steam. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Production rate 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is the total steam output of a boiler in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pounds of steam per hour (lbs-steam/hour) of boiler operation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reasonably Available Control Technology 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
RACT, 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes of paragraph (r) of this section, means the lowest 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission limitation that a particular boiler is capable of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
meeting by using measures that are reasonably available in terms 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of technological and economic feasibility. Such measures may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
include either control system(s) or improved combustion 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions, or both. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Total organic gases 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
are any compounds that contain at least 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
one carbon atom. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Wood wastes 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
include bark, sawdust, shavings, hogged wood, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and other wood refuse generated during processing operations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Emission limits (ppmv). 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
VOC emissions from wood waste 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
boiler operations at a production rate exceeding an annual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(calendar year) average of 50,000 lbs-steam per hour as defined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in paragraph (r)(2)(i) of this section must meet the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limit of 150 ppmv of VOC in the stack exhaust stream. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission limit maintenance. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The VOC emission limit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
presented in paragraph (r)(3)(i) of this section shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintained through any one or more of the following provisions: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Use of fuel with a maximum moisture content of 50%; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Operation of the boiler at optimal combustion 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Proper operation and maintenance of pollution control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Periodic inspection, maintenance, and repairs on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
boiler and other equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compliance Schedule. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The VOC emission limit defined 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in paragraph (r)(3)(i) of this section shall be achieved upon publication of the final rule.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test Methods and Calculations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Determination of VOC content of exhaust stream. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VOC content of the exhaust gas stream subject to the provisions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of paragraph (r) of this section, excluding exempt compounds, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be analyzed as prescribed by 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Methods 25 and 25A. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Determination of exempt compounds. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Measurement of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exempt compounds shall be conducted and reported in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 18. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Administrative requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Emissions testing and records. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The facility subject to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the standards of paragraph (r)(3) of this section shall, at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minimum, conduct sample analysis for VOC pollutants at least once 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
each year. The Air Pollution Control Officer (APCO) shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provided with adequate advance notification at least 2 weeks 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
before any scheduled emissions tests. The analysis results must 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be submitted to the Administrator and APCO within 60 days of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions test. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
