<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
RACT, 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes of paragraph (s) of this section, means the lowest 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission limitation that a particular coating line is capable of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
meeting by using measures that are reasonably available in terms 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of technological and economic feasibility. Such measures may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
include either control system(s) or coating reformulation(s) or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
both. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Tab press lubrication 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is the process which uses a lubricated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
mechanical press to create beverage container lid tabs from flat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aluminum metal stock. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Limits. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Tab press lubricant cannot exceed a VOC content 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of 5.73 pounds per gallon of lubricant used, less water and less 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exempt compounds, as defined in paragraph (s)(2) of this section; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and VOC emissions from tab press lubricant usage cannot exceed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1.2 &times; 10
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=1 -->
^5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 pounds of VOC per tab produced. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission control system. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Alternatively, a facility may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comply with the provisions of paragraph (s)(3)(i) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by using an emission control system, provided that the overall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
efficiency of the system (capture efficiency multiplied by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
destruction efficiency) shall not be less than 85% by weight in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reducing organic compounds. The emission control system, as well 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as the operation and maintenance plan necessary to ensure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance on an ongoing basis, shall be approved in writing by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compliance schedule. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Limits as defined in paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(s)(3)(i) or (ii) of this section shall be achieved upon publication of the final rule.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test methods. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Determination of VOC content of lubricants. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The VOC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
content of coatings subject to the provisions of paragraph (s) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section, excluding exempt compounds, shall be analyzed as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prescribed by 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Method 24. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Determination of exempt compounds. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Measurement of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exempt compounds shall be conducted and reported in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with ASTM D 4457&hyph;85. For exempt compounds where no reference 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test method is available, a facility requesting the exemption 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall provide appropriate test methods approved by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Determination of destruction efficiency. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Destruction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
efficiency as specified in paragraph (s)(3)(ii) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be determined by 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, Methods 25 and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
25A. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Determination of capture efficiency. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Measurement of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capture efficiency of the emission control system as specified in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (s)(3)(ii) of this section shall be conducted and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reported in accordance with the U.S. EPA protocols,
<FOOTCITE>37</FOOTCITE>
 or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capture efficiency methods approved by the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

