40 CFR 52.741(a)(4)(iii).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Administrative requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Material usage records. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The facility shall maintain a current list of lubricants 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and solvents in use which include the following information: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Name and manufacturer information; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Mixing instructions; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) VOC content of tab press lubricants as applied; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Weight percent water; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Weight percent exempt solvent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The facility shall maintain records of the amounts of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lubricants and VOCs used according to the following schedule: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Monthly records showing the types and amounts of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lubricants used that meet the standards in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(s)(3)(i) of this section; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Daily records showing the types and amounts of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lubricants used when such usage was in conjunction with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission control equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The facility shall maintain monthly records of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
number of tabs produced by each type of tab press. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission control equipment records. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Any facility 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
complying with the provisions of paragraph (s)(3)(ii) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section by using air pollution control equipment shall maintain 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
daily records of key system operating parameters, such as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
temperatures, pressures, and/or flow rates, for the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Proof of compliance. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The facility shall prove 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with the standards of paragraph (s)(3) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by conducting annual source testing of tab press lubrication 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operations and analyzing VOC content of the lubricants as per 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (s)(4)(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Retention of records. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All records maintained pursuant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to this section shall be retained and available for inspection by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Administrator for the previous five-year period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(t) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fugitive emissions from oil and gas production 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities and conveying stations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of paragraph (t) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section shall apply to any owner or operator of an oil or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gas production field or conveying station. For the purposes of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this paragraph, the affected areas include the Sacramento Metro 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Area, the Los Angeles-South Coast Air Basin Area, and the Ventura 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
County Area as described for ozone in 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraphs (t)(1) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
through (t)(7) of this section, the following definitions shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply. All terms not defined herein shall have the meaning given 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
them in &sect;52.2950. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Background 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the ambient concentration of organic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compounds expressed as methane as determined by a portable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hydrocarbon detection instrument when the reading is taken at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
least three meters upwind from any component to be inspected and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which is not influenced by any specific emission point. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Closed-vent system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any system that is not open to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
atmosphere and is composed of piping, connections and, if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
necessary, flow-inducing devices that transport gases or vapors 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from a piece or pieces of equipment to a vapor recovery or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
disposal system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Commercial natural gas 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means natural gas containing less 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than 10% VOC by weight. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any valve, fitting, pump, compressor, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressure relief device, diaphragm, hatch, sight-glass, open-ended 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
line, or meter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compressor 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any device used to compress gases and/or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vapors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Control valve 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a device used to regulate the fluid 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pressure or volume in a process unit that, upon actuation, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
releases process stream VOCs. Excluded from this definition are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control valves that are actuated by non-process stream compressed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Conveying station 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any compressor station, metering 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
station, or other transfer station located between the extraction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
well and the refinery or gas processing plant. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Critical component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any component that if shut down 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would require the shutdown of a critical process unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Critical process unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a process unit that has no 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standby equipment available, that cannot be bypassed, and that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would be technically infeasible to repair leaks from without 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shutting down the associated process. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
