piping details, and other equipment, such as, vessels, heat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exchangers, and condensers. These components include but are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited to flanges, threaded connections, and other connectors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gas processing plant 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any facility engaged in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
separation of liquids from field gas and/or fractionation of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liquids into gaseous products, such as ethane, propane, butane, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and natural gasoline. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gas production facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility at which petroleum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gas or natural gas extraction and handling are conducted, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined in the Standard Industrial Classification Manual as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Industry Number 1311, Crude Petroleum and Natural Gas. This 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
definition includes, but is not limited to, compressor stations, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dehydration units, sweetening units, field treatment units, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liquefied natural gas units, extraction wells, flow lines, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gathering lines, separators, and other auxiliary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nontransportation equipment used in petroleum gas or natural gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extraction and handling. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Hatch 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any covered opening system that provides access 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to a tank or container, usually through the top deck. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Inaccessible component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any component located over 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fifteen feet above ground when access is required from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ground; or any component located over six feet away from a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
platform when access is required from the platform. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a major gas leak, major liquid leak, minor gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
leak, or minor liquid leak. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak minimization 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means reducing a leak to the lowest 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
achievable level using best modern practices including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tightening, adjusting, or adding sealing material and without 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shutting down the process which the component serves. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Leak repair 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any corrective action taken for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes of reducing a component leak to the lowest achievable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
level below the applicable standard using best modern practices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any 4-inch or larger valve, any 5-horse-power (5-hp) or larger pump, any compressor, and any 4-inch 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or larger pressure relief device. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major gas leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
for any component means the detection of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
total gaseous organic compounds in excess of 10,000 ppmv as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
methane above background as measured according to the test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedures in paragraph (t)(7)(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major liquid leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a visible mist or cloud or a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
continuous flow of liquid. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minor component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any component that is not a major 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
component. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minor gas leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means for any component, except stuffing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
boxes and control valves, the detection of total gaseous organic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compounds in excess of 1,000 ppmv but not more than 10,000 ppmv 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as methane above background as measured according to the test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedures in paragraph (t)(7)(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minor liquid leak 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
is any liquid leak which is not a major 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liquid leak and drips at a rate of more than three drops per 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
minute. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Oil production facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility at which crude oil 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extraction and handling is conducted, as defined in the Standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Industrial Classification Manual as Industry Number 1311, Crude 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Petroleum and Natural Gas. This definition includes, but is not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited to, extraction wells, flow lines, gathering lines, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
separators, and other auxiliary nontransportation equipment used 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in petroleum extraction and handling. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Open ended line 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any valve, except safety relief 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
valves, having one side of the valve seat in contact with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
process fluid or gas and one side open to the atmosphere. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Owner or operator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any person who owns, operates, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
leases, controls, or supervises an emissions source or air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollution control equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Person 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any individual, corporation, copartnership, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
firm, company, partnership, joint stock company, trust, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
association, State, municipality, political subdivision, or any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other legal entity, or their legal representative, agent, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
assigns. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pipeline transfer station 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that handles the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
storage or transfer, or both, of petroleum products or crude 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
petroleum in pipelines. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Platform 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any raised, permanent, horizontal surface 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that provides access to components. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pressure relief device (PRD) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a pressure relief valve, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rupture disc, or any other equipment designed to relieve pressure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
within process a line when the static pressure reaches a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
setpoint. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pressure relief event 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a release from a pressure relief 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
device resulting when the static pressure reaches the setpoint of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the pressure relief device. A pressure relief event is not a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
leak. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pressure relief valve (PRV) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any valve that is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
automatically actuated by upstream static pressure, and used for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
safety or emergency purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Pump 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any device used to transport fluids by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
addition of mechanical energy. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Refinery 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a facility that processes petroleum, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined in the Standard Industrial Classification Manual as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Industry Number 2911, Petroleum Refining. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repair 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any corrective action taken for the purposes of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reducing a leak to below the applicable standard. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rupture disc 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a diaphragm held between flanges for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purpose of isolating a volatile organic compound from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
atmosphere or from a downstream pressure relief valve. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stuffing box 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a packing gland, a chamber or ``box'' which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
holds packing material compressed around a moving pump rod or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
valve stem. For the purposes of paragraph (t) of this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stuffing box seals are considered to be pump seals. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unmanned facility 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a remote facility which has no 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanent sited personnel and is greater than five miles from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nearest manned facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unsafe-to-monitor component 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a component installed at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location that would prevent its safe inspection or repair as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined by Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standards or in provisions for worker safety found in 29 CFR part 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1910. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
