<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vacuum service
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
In vacuum service
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means that the equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in VOC service is operating at an internal pressure that is at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
least 5 kPa (0.73 in. Hg) below ambient pressure. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Valve
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a device that regulates or isolates the fluid 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
flow in a pipe, tube, or conduit by means of an external 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
actuator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vapor control system
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any system that is not open to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the atmosphere and is composed of piping, connections and, if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
necessary, flow-inducing devices that transport gas or vapor from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a piece or pieces of equipment to a vapor recovery or disposal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Visual inspection
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means performing a survey to identify 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
signs of leaking liquid, visible mist, or audible leaks. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Specific provisions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Each owner or operator of an oil 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or gas production field or conveying station shall be in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with the requirements of paragraphs (t)(3) (i) and (ii) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section by January 1, 1996. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Identification requirements.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Components in VOC service 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall meet the following identification requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) All major and critical components shall be physically 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identified clearly and visibly for inspection, repair, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replacement, and recordkeeping purposes. The physical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identification shall consist of labels, tags, or other system 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved by the EPA which enables the EPA and the operator to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
locate each individual component. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) All major, critical, inaccessible, and unsafe-to-monitor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
components shall be clearly identified in Piping and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Instrumentation (P&amp;I) diagrams for inspection, repair, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replacement, and recordkeeping purposes. For identical field 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
production units, the following items will satisfy the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements of this paragraph: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A single P&amp;I diagram representing the typical component 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A listing of field production units by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identification number which is located on a lease map in use 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the owner/operator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) A list of all components subject to paragraph (t) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section shall be prepared which includes separate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identification of inaccessible, unsafe-to-monitor, and critical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
components. The list shall include component identification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information as specified under paragraph (t)(3)(i)(A) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the number of minor components by component type, and a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
description of the VOC service for each component or component 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
type. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) The EPA shall be notified of any changes in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identification of a major component within thirty days. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notification shall include necessary amendments to the compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
plan specified under paragraph (t)(5)(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Inspection and Maintenance (I&amp;M) program.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Any owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operator of a facility subject to this section shall implement an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
I&amp;M program that meets the requirements of paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(t)(3)(ii)(A) through (C) of this section within twelve months 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
after [
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Insert date of publication of the final rule
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
]. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Inspection requirements.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The I&amp;M program will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conducted in accordance with the following inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Visual inspection requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All pumps, compressors, and pressure relief valves 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(PRVs) shall be visually inspected for leaks once during 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
every operating shift, except for components located at oil 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and natural gas production fields. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All pumps, compressors, PRVs, and stuffing boxes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
located at manned oil and gas production fields shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
visually inspected for leaks once per day and the same 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
components located at unmanned fields shall be inspected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
once per week. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
iii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Any vapor leak which is identified during the visual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection of components under paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(t)(3)(ii)(A)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
)(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
i
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) and (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ii
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measured to quantify emission concentrations according to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the test method specified in paragraph (t)(7)(i) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) All components, except as provided in paragraphs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(t)(3)(ii) (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
), (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
), (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
), and (
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
5
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) of this section, shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspected quarterly according to the method prescribed in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (t)(7)(i) of this section. The time between 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspections shall not exceed 110 consecutive days. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
