<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(u) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emissions of oxides of nitrogen from large institutional, commercial, and industrial boilers, steam generators,
and process heaters.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of this paragraph, the affected area includes the Sacramento Metro Area as described for ozone in
40 CFR 81.305.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Any owner or operator of a boiler, steam generator, or process heater with a rated heat input capacity equal to or
greater than 5 million British thermal units per hour (mmBtu/hr) shall comply with the applicable requirements standards
of paragraphs (u)(1) through (u)(7) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any owner or operator of a boiler, steam generator, or process heater with a rated heat input capacity equal to
or greater than 5 million British thermal units per hour (mmBtu/hr) that claims an exemption from the standards of
paragraph (u)(3) of this section because of the exemption criteria specified under paragraph (u)(4)(ii) of this
section shall comply with the applicable requirements of paragraph (u)(6)(iii)(I) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of paragraph (u)(1) through (u)(7) of this section, the following definitions shall apply. All terms
not defined herein shall have the meaning given them in &sect;52.2950.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Annual heat input
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the actual amount of heat released by fuels burned in a unit during a 12 calendar month rolling period, based on
the fuel's higher heating value. The annual heat input shall be calculated as the sum of the previous 12 monthly fuel
use rates multiplied by the fuel's higher heating value.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Boiler or steam generator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any combustion equipment used in any institutional, commercial, or industrial operation that is designed
to burn gaseous and/or liquid fuel and used to produce steam, heat water and/or other fluids, and/or generate electricity.
A boiler or steam generator does not include any waste heat recovery unit that is used to recover sensible heat from
the exhaust of a combustion turbine or any unfired waste heat recovery boiler that is used to recover sensible heat
from the exhaust of any combustion equipment.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
British thermal unit (Btu)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the amount of heat required to raise the temperature of one pound of water from 59
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F to 60
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F at one atmosphere.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heat input
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the chemical heat released due to fuel combustion in a unit, using the higher heating value of the fuel. This does
not include the sensible heat of incoming combustion air.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Higher heating value (HHV)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the total heat liberated per mass of fuel burned (Btu per pound), when fuel and dry air at standard conditions
undergo complete combustion and all resultant products are brought to their standard states at standard conditions.
If certification of the HHV is not provided by the third party fuel supplier, it shall be determined by one of the following
test methods: ASTM D2015&hyph;85 for solid fuels; ASTM D240&hyph;87 or ASTM D2382&hyph;88 for liquid hydrocarbon
fuels; or ASTM D1826&hyph;88 or ASTM D1945&hyph;81 in conjunction with ASTM D3588&hyph;89 for gaseous fuels.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-gaseous fuel
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any fuel which is not a gas at 68 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F and one atmosphere.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
 emissions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the sum of nitric oxides and nitrogen dioxide in the flue gas, collectively expressed as nitrogen dioxide.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Process heater
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any combustion equipment used in any institutional, commercial, or industrial operation that is designed
to burn gaseous and/or liquid fuel and which transfers heat from combustion gases to water, heat transfer medium,
or process streams. Process heater does not include any kiln or oven used for drying, baking, cooking, calcining or
vitrifying; any unfired waste heat recovery heater that is used to recover sensible heat from the exhaust of any combustion
equipment; or any fuel-fired degreasing or metal finishing equipment.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Rated heat input capacity 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the heat input capacity specified on the nameplate of the combustion unit. If the combustion unit has been altered
or modified such that its maximum heat input is different than the heat input capacity specified on the nameplate,
the new maximum heat input shall be considered as the rated heat input capacity. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Shutdown 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the period of time a unit is cooled from its normal operating temperature to cold or ambient temperature.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stack gas oxygen trim system 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the system of monitors that is used to measure stack excess combustion air, typically consisting of flue gas
oxygen and/or carbon monoxide monitors that automatically provide a feedback signal to the combustion air controller
that maintains the stack excess air at the desired level.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Startup 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the period of time a unit is heated from cold or ambient temperature to its normal operating temperature as specified
by the manufacturer.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any boiler, steam generator, or process heater as defined in this definition.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Any owner or operator that operates a unit with an annual heat input rate equal to or greater than 9 billion British
thermal units per year (109 Btu/yr) shall:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Not cause to be discharged into the atmosphere any gases that contain NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emissions in excess of the following:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) For gaseous fuels, 30 parts per million (ppm) corrected to 3 percent volume stack gas O
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 on a dry basis averaged over a period of 15 consecutive minutes; or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) For liquid fuels, 40 ppm corrected to 3 percent volume stack gas O
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 on a dry basis averaged over a period of 15 consecutive minutes; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Demonstrate initial compliance with the NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emission standard in accordance with the requirements of paragraph (u)(7)(i) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Establish a controlled ppm carbon monoxide (CO) emission limit that represents good operating and combustion
practices. No owner or operator shall cause to be discharged into the atmosphere any gases that contain CO in excess
of the lowest of one of the following limits: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
