<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
New
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, when applied to motor vehicles, means a motor vehicle, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the equitable or legal title to which has never been transferred 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to an ultimate purchaser. It is conclusively presumed that the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equitable or legal title to a motor vehicle, other than a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
motorcycle, with an odometer reading of 7,500 miles or more, has 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
been transferred to an ultimate purchaser, and that the equitable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or legal title to a motor vehicle, other than a motorcycle, with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an odometer reading of less than 7,500 miles has not been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transferred to an ultimate purchaser. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Obvious abuse or tampering 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the deliberate removal of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the catalyst or evaporative emissions canister, turbocharging of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a naturally aspirated engine, operation with less than one half 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the recommended level of oil in the engine, or damage to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine or emission controls resulting from a vehicular accident. 
