<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Application for certification.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) A separate application for a certificate of conformity 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be made for each set of standards and each class of new 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
motor vehicles or new motor vehicle engines. Such application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be made to the Administrator by the manufacturer and shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be updated and corrected by amendment. The application shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
meet all of the requirements set forth in 40 CFR 86.094&hyph;21, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unless otherwise provided in the California application specified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in paragraph (d)(2) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The application shall contain a copy of the application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for certification specified in &sect;1960.1 of title 13 of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California Code of Regulations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The application shall also demonstrate that throughout 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all testing conducted by the manufacturer in fulfilling the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application for certification specified in &sect;1960.1 of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
title 13 of the California Code of Regulations, and such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
additional testing as may be necessary, that the vehicle(s) for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which certification is being requested meet all the applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission standards and design specifications specified in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) The applications shall also contain a statement by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer that the vehicle(s) for which certification is being 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requested will meet the emission standards specified in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section over its full useful life (or half life, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable) in the absence of obvious abuse or tampering, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined in paragraph (e)(iii)(B) of this section. Vehicles found 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to not do so under the provisions of paragraph (e) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section will be subject to recall per the provisions of paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Enhanced in-use recall provisions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (e) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the provisions of subpart S or 40 CFR part 85, and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
associated established practices of EPA, shall apply to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recall of vehicles subject to the requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Vehicle selection. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Vehicles shall be selected by EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for purposes of recall testing from the portion of the vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
population subject to enhanced inspection and maintenance testing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
described in &sect;52.2963. EPA may test vehicles at any time or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
mileage within their applicable useful life. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vehicle testing. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) Selected vehicles will be tested 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unless EPA determines that a selected vehicle(s) has been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subjected to obvious abuse or tampering. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) For purposes of paragraph (e) of this section, obvious 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
abuse or tampering includes the following conditions: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The presence of less than one half of the recommended 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
volume of motor oil in the engine crankcase; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The deliberate removal of the catalyst or evaporative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
canister; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The addition of a turbocharger to a naturally aspirated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) The presence of damage to the engine or emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
controls resulting from a vehicular accident; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Other factors which the Administrator may consider 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appropriate for determining the presence of obvious abuse or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tampering. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The manufacturer may be present at the time of vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procurement and testing and request that a vehicle not be tested 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
due to obvious abuse or tampering. The Administrator may request 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that such a request from a manufacturer be supported by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appropriate documentation, though the final determination rests 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Vehicles that EPA determines have been subject to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
obvious abuse or tampering will be removed from the test sample. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) EPA will test vehicles in the condition in which the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles are received from the owner. No repair or maintenance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will be conducted on the vehicle prior to testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Vehicles shall be tested according to the same test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedures prescribed in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) (i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Discretionary recall authority. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Based on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
criteria contained in 40 CFR 85.1802, the Administrator may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determine that a nonconformity with an applicable standard under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (c) of this section exists for a vehicle engine family. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
In addition, the Administrator may make such a determination of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nonconformity when the average emissions of the test vehicles for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any pollutant exceeds the applicable recall emission standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in paragraph (c) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any vehicle recall conducted by a manufacturer under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (e) of this section shall apply to all vehicles of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
affected engine family which have been sold in the State of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
