<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(5) (i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Prohibitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Should the Administrator make a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determination of nonconformity under paragraph (e)(4) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The Secretary of State of California, the California 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Department of Motor Vehicles, its employees, and any other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
persons representing the State of California are prohibited from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registering any vehicle covered by this nonconformity unless 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evidence is presented that the required remedies have been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performed on that vehicle; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Operators of motor vehicles covered by this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nonconformity are prohibited from registering the vehicle without 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
first obtaining the required remedies for their vehicle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The penalties contained in Section 43016 of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California Health and Safety Code for the failure by a vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owner to have needed repairs made to a recalled vehicle shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply to the failure by a vehicle owner to have needed repairs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
made to a recalled vehicle under paragraph (e) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
I/M-based selective recall requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Liability for I/M-related repairs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Except as noted in paragraphs (f)(1) (v) and (vi) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section, the manufacturer of a vehicle shall be responsible 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for its repair sufficient for it to pass an emission inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performed as part of a FIP I/M program, including the enhanced 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in-use I/M standards specified in paragraph (f)(2) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, and for obtaining official certification of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
successful passage of the above emission inspection (i.e., repeat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test) if: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) That vehicle has failed an emission inspection performed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as part of a FIP I/M program for the pollutant for which the I/M 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
based selective recall liability threshold has been exceeded in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (f)(1)(i)(B) of this section; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) At least one model year's sales of that vehicle's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exhaust engine family has exceeded a liability threshold for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
either HC or NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emissions, as defined in paragraph (f)(4) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) This liability shall begin 30 days after receipt of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notification of exceedance of a liability threshold from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) (A) The vehicle manufacturer shall be liable to remedy 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the defects and for the repairs necessary for the vehicle to pass 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all aspects of an emission inspection which is part of a FIP I/M 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
program applicable to that vehicle at the time of the failure of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the I/M emission inspection referred to in paragraph (f)(1)(i)(A) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section, regardless of whether the liability threshold 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for only one of the two pollutants was exceeded or both were 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exceeded. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) At minimum, manufacturers must allow the repairs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
required under paragraph (f)(1)(i) of this section to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performed at any of its manufacturer authorized repair 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities. Nothing here shall be construed to limit the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performance of such repairs to only manufacturer dealerships. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) In performing the repairs conducted under this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the manufacturer shall promptly schedule and expeditiously repair 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the vehicle. In doing so, the manufacturer shall provide a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
loaner vehicle of equivalent or better quality free of charge to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the owner of the vehicle being repaired: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) During the period of time when the vehicle is at the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer authorized repair facility whenever the repairs will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
require more than one day to complete, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Starting 14 days after the vehicle owner initially 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contacted the manufacturer authorized repair facility regarding 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the repair of the vehicle and continuing to the time the vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is delivered to the vehicle owner along with official 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certification that the vehicle has successfully passed the repeat 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission inspection, if the vehicle has not already been so 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
delivered by this time. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) (A) In lieu of performing the repairs required in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (f)(1)(i) of this section, a manufacturer may purchase 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the vehicle and remove it from use in California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The manufacturer's responsibility for performing the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repairs required in paragraph (f)(1)(i) of this section ends if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the vehicle owner declines to sell the vehicle to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer at a price equal to Average Retail Value listed in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the N.A.D.A. Official Used Car Guide published by the National 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Automobile Dealers Used Car Guide Co., 8400 Westpark Dr., McLean, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
VA 22102&hyph;9985 for the month containing the date of the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection failure referred to in paragraph (f)(1)(i)(A) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section and for the smallest geographical area covered by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
above Guide which contains the area covered by the FIP 
<!-- PJG 0034 unknown -->
 I/M 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exempted repairs.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (A) Manufacturers are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
responsible for repairs to vehicles to which there has been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
obvious abuse or tampering, as defined in paragraph (e)(3)(i) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section and determined by the FIP I/M program test provider. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Manufacturers are not responsible for repairs of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles that have exceeded their useful life. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicable enhanced in-use I/M standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) (A) The enhanced in-use I/M standards for exhaust HC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions specified in paragraph (c) of this section shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
