<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iii) Provide the vehicle owner with a written copy of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test results and the determination that the vehicle was not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
obviously abused or tampered with. This document shall be signed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the certified emission inspector and the manager or an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
assistant manager of the FIP I/M test facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exceedance of an I/M-based selective recall liability 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
threshold. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The liability threshold is 5.0 percent for vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that have not exceeded 50.0 percent of their useful life and 10.0 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
percent for vehicles that have not exceeded 100.0 percent of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
their full useful life. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) An exhaust engine family is deemed to have exceeded the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liability threshold for NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 or HC if the NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 or HC failure rate for any model year of that exhaust engine family, per paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f)(5) of this section, exceeds the half- or full-life liability 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
threshold at any time, after three months of data have been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submitted for that model year's vehicles. Exceedance of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
liability thresholds for HC and NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 are determined independently. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Calculation of failure rates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The failure rate (in percent) for a specific pollutant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for each model year of each exhaust engine family will consist of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the total number of failing vehicles for that pollutant divided 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the total number of vehicles multiplied by 100, where: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The total number of vehicles refers to the sum of all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles from a specific model year and exhaust engine family 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which have been tested in a FIP I/M program, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The total number of failing vehicles includes those 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles included under paragraph (f)(5)(i)(A) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) At any time exceeded the applicable IM240 exhaust NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard specified in paragraph (c)(1)(vi) or (c)(2)(iv) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, as applicable, (considered a failure for NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
); or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) At any time exceeded the applicable IM240 exhaust HC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard specified in paragraph (c)(1)(vi) or (c)(2)(iv) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, as applicable, or failed either the purge or pressure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
functional tests described in &sect;52.2963(t) and (u), respectively 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(considered a failure for HC). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Separate failure rates for each pollutant will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calculated for vehicles which have not exceeded 50.0 percent of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
their full useful life and for vehicles which have not exceeded 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
100.0 percent of their full useful life. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Failure rates shall be expressed as a percentage, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rounded to one figure after the decimal. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) On a monthly basis, the Administrator will calculate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the HC and NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 failure rates for each exhaust engine family and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notify each vehicle manufacturer, as applicable, of the results 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for their engine families. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Within thirty days after a liability threshold for an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exhaust family has been determined to be exceeded, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator shall, by registered mail, notify the manufacturer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the affected vehicles and managers of enhanced I/M test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facilities required to meet the requirements of &sect;52.2963. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(g) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Enhanced ILEV fleet program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Fleet operators which control 10 or more vehicles which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operate at any time in the South Coast Air Basin Nonattainment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Area for Ozone as defined in 40 CFR 81.305 shall determine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whether they are a covered fleet operator. This determination is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to be made as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The fleet operator shall not count the following types 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of vehicles: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Vehicles with a GVWR greater than 26,000 pounds; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Law enforcement and other emergency vehicles; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Nonroad vehicles; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Vehicles garaged at a private residence that are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
centrally fueled; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Vehicles held for lease or rent to the general public; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) Vehicles held for sale by motor vehicle dealers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(including demonstration vehicles); and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) Vehicles used for motor vehicle manufacturer product 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrations and tests. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Fleet operators shall determine the number of vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
not exempted in paragraph (g)(1)(i) of this section that can be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
centrally fueled (as defined in 40 CFR 88.302&hyph;94). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) If a fleet operator determines under paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(g)(1)(ii) of this section that 10 or more non-exempt vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
can be centrally fueled, then the fleet operator shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered to be a covered fleet operator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Except as provided in paragraph (g)(3) of this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
covered fleet operators acquiring vehicles to replace vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
meeting the provisions of paragraph (g)(1) of this section, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
acquiring additional vehicles which meet the same provisions, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall acquire a number of enhanced ILEVs equal to the number of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
such vehicles acquired multiplied by the appropriate percentage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) For model year 1999 light-duty vehicles, light-duty 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
trucks, and medium-duty vehicles, 50 percent; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) For model year 2000 and later light-duty vehicles, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
light-duty trucks, and medium-duty vehicles, 70 percent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Enhanced ILEV purchase credits. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Covered fleet 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operators may satisfy the enhanced ILEV purchase requirements 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provided in paragraph (g)(2) of this section wholly or in part by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
redeeming an appropriate number of enhanced ILEV purchase 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
credits. Enhanced ILEV purchase credits may be generated as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) A covered fleet operator which purchases enhanced ILEVs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in excess of the enhanced ILEV purchase requirement may receive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
one enhanced ILEV purchase credit for each excess vehicle; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) A covered fleet operator which purchases enhanced 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ILEVs earlier than required may receive one enhanced ILEV 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purchase credit for each such vehicle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The Administrator shall issue a credit document or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
documents to a covered fleet operator which requests enhanced 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ILEV credit or credits and which provides evidence of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appropriate purchases. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The Administrator shall approve the reduction of any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
covered fleet operator's enhanced ILEV purchase requirement by a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
number equal to the number of credits presented to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator for redemption, subject to confirmation of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
legitimacy of the credit documents so presented. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
