<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Fleet operators which control 10 or more vehicles which operate at any time in the South Coast Air Basin Nonattainment
Area for Ozone as defined in 40 CFR 81.305 shall submit the following information to the Administrator by January 1
of each year beginning January 1999: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Total number of vehicles operated in the covered area; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Numbers of vehicles by class (e.g., LDV, LDT) and fueling characteristics (e.g., centrally fueled) acquired
during the previous calendar year; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Numbers of vehicles by class and fueling characteristics expected to be acquired in the coming calendar year;

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Numbers of enhanced ILEVs purchased during the previous calendar year and expected during the coming calendar
year; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Vehicle Information Numbers (VINs) and engine family designations (see 40 CFR 86.092&hyph;24) for each of the
vehicles reported in paragraphs (g)(4)(ii) through (iv) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) The identity of the responsible party which has control of vehicle acquisition decisions; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) The covered fleet operator's calculated minimum purchase requirement from paragraph (g)(2) of this section.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Violations.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The following shall be considered violations of the enhanced ILEV fleet program: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Failure to submit required data to the Administrator; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Failure to meet the appropriate purchase requirements; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Counterfeiting or commerce in counterfeit enhanced ILEV purchase credit documents. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Penalties.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Any person which the Administrator finds in violation of the provisions of paragraph (g)(4)(v) of this section shall
be subject to a civil penalty of not more than $25,000. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;52.2963 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Enhanced inspection/maintenance program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicability of 40 CFR part 51, subpart S.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of this section, except as otherwise provided, the definitions and requirements of 40 CFR part 51,
subpart S (Inspection/Maintenance Program Requirements) apply. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Additional definitions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Centralized inspection network
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a network of vehicle inspection facilities owned and operated by a single, identifiable entity, such as a state
or other governmental entity, or an agreed upon agent of a state or other governmental entity. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Certificate of compliance
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a serially numbered instrument (either paper-based or electronic) indicating that a vehicle has met the requirements
of this section, either by passing all applicable emission tests, or by being granted a waiver (see ``Waiver'' in paragraph
(b) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Certified emission inspector
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a person who has successfully completed all necessary training and who is certified by the Administrator or
his/her designee as qualified to perform emission inspections on subject vehicles. Such certification must be periodically
renewed, and is subject to suspension and permanent revocation as a result of violating the requirements of this section.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission inspection
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the full range of emission-related inspections a vehicle is subject to as a result of participating in an I/M
program, including the sampling and analysis of tailpipe exhaust, purge and pressure testing of the evaporative
system, and any visual inspections for the presence and proper connection of specific emission control devices.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission inspection test report
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an automated report of a vehicle's emission inspection results, coded to a specific vehicle through the use
of unambiguous vehicle identifiers, such as the license plate number and vehicle identification number (VIN). The
emission inspection test report is a separate document and distinguished from the certificate of compliance by virtue
of the fact that a test report shall not be accepted as valid for registration purposes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00448 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Enhanced I/M program
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a program meeting the enhanced I/M performance standard as established under EPA's I/M rule (40 CFR 51.351).

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Farm equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a vehicle designed or adapted and determined by the Administrator to be used exclusively for agricultural operations
and only incidentally operated or moved upon highways. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Gross vehicle weight rating (GVWR)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the value specified by the manufacturer on the Federal weight certification label as the loaded weight of a single
vehicle. For the purposes of the FIP's I/M program, California-certified vehicles shall be considered to fall under
the same gross vehicle weight ratings as comparable, 49-state vehicles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Heavy-duty vehicles
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means trucks weighing more than 8,500 pounds GVWR. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Light-duty trucks 1 (LDT1)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means trucks weighing less than 6,000 pounds GVWR. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Light-duty trucks 2 (LDT2)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means trucks weighing from 6,000 to 8,500 pounds GVWR. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Light-duty vehicles
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means passenger cars or multi-purpose vehicles weighing less than 6,000 pounds GVWR. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Onboard diagnostic device (OBD)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a system for monitoring the in-use emission performance of a vehicle which provides feedback to the driver concerning
actual or potential malfunctions through the illumination of a malfunction indicator light (MIL). The event triggering
MIL illumination is also stored on the OBD computer as a trouble code which can be downloaded at a vehicle testing or
repair facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Oversight contractor(s)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a contractor or contractors who have been awarded a contract by the Administrator to conduct and report the results
of overt and covert audits of the test provider(s) sites and personnel. The information generated by the oversight
contractor shall be used by the Administrator to substantiate enforcement actions taken by EPA against the test provider
and its employees. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Qualifying repairs
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means those vehicle repairs necessary to correct the deficiencies which resulted in a vehicle's failure of an emissions
inspection and which count toward the minimum dollar amount required before a waiver may be issued. For those repairs
where repair or replacement of emission-related parts requires replacement of other non-emission related equipment
constructed as one indivisible unit by the manufacturer, the total replacement costs or repair costs may be counted
toward qualifying repairs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recognized repair facility
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a business engaged in the diagnosis and repair of automotive engines and related systems. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recognized repair technician
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a person who has received and has proof of formal training in the diagnosis and repair of automotive engines and
related systems, or holds a valid license issued by the California Bureau of Automotive Repair, or is employed by a
recognized repair facility primarily for the purpose of diagnosing and repairing automotive engines and their related
systems. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00449 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Remote Sensing Devices (RSD)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a transportable system of devices designed for the remote gathering of vehicle emissions and identification
data while vehicles are being operated on public roads. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Special mobile equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means vehicles not designed or used primarily for the transportation of persons or property and only incidentally
operated or moved over a highway, including ditch digging apparatus; well boring apparatus; earth moving and road
construction and maintenance machinery, such as asphalt spreaders, bituminous mixers, bucket loaders, ditchers,
graders, finishing machines, road rollers, scarifiers, earth moving carryalls, scrapers, power shovels and draglines;
and self-propelled cranes and tractors, other than truck tractors. The term does not include house trailers; dump
trucks; truck-mounted transit mixers, cranes or shovels; or other vehicles designed for the transportation of persons
or property to which machinery has been attached. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test provider(s)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means one or more entities with whom the Administrator has entered into a legal agreement, for the purposes of providing
vehicle emission testing and other FIP I/M program activities except those activities which would clearly constitute
a conflict of interest or are otherwise impractical, such as overt and covert auditing of the testing element, program
effectiveness evaluation, and enforcement. As part of this legal agreement, the test provider(s) would be reimbursed
for operating expenses and allowed a reasonable profit by way of a test fee to be collected directly from motorists
at the time of testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transient test
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a vehicle emission test in which exhaust emissions are sampled and analyzed under conditions simulating actual
on-road driving conditions, including the use of loaded operation simulation, and a standardized driving cycle.
For the purposes of the FIP I/M program, a transient test known as the IM240 shall be used for vehicle exhaust emissions
testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Unsafe condition
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a defect, malfunction or other condition of a vehicle which may expose an emission inspector to harm in the performance
of an emission inspection of that vehicle. A vehicle which is presented for testing in an unsafe condition may be rejected
from testing until such time as the factors contributing to the vehicle's unsafe condition have been corrected. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vehicle model year
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the date of manufacture of a vehicle as specified by the vehicle identification number (VIN), or, if this number
is not available or cannot be interpreted for the year, the annual production period of the vehicle as designated by
the manufacturer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Waiver
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a notation on the emission inspection certificate of compliance indicating that the requirement of passing
the otherwise required reinspection test has been waived. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Subject vehicles.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Subject vehicles include all model year 1966 to 1998 gasoline-fueled vehicles to 19,500 pounds GVWR (including vehicles
with engine-based certification), and all model year 1999 and newer vehicles of all fuel types to 14,000 pounds GVWR
(excluding vehicles with engine-based certification from 8,500 to 14,000 pounds GVWR) which are: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Registered in or required to be registered in a FIP I/M program area. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Leased vehicles with registration or titling in the name of an equity owner other than the lessee or user where the
motor vehicle is registered or required to be registered in a FIP I/M program area. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Available for rent in a FIP I/M program area or used in a FIP I/M program area, regardless of where the vehicles are
registered. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) part of a fleet registered in and/or primarily operated within a FIP I/M program area. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Federally-owned vehicles operated within a FIP I/M program area, with the exception of tactical military vehicles.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) Vehicles owned, leased or operated by civilian and military personnel on Federal installations, except for vehicles
belonging to or operated by visiting agency, employee or military personnel whose stays do not exceed a total of 60
calendar days per calendar year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exempted vehicles.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Exempted vehicles shall include vehicles operated or registered as one of the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Special mobile equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Farm equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Motorcycles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Motorized pedalcycles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Vehicles repossessed by a financier or debt collector through the use of miscellaneous motor vehicle business
registration plates. This vehicle exemption will no longer hold once a repossessed vehicle has been resold or leased
or is otherwise being operated on a routine basis in the FIP I/M program area. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Prohibitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 (1) The Secretary of State of California, the California Department of Motor Vehicles, its employees, and any other
persons representing the State of California are prohibited from reregistering any subject vehicle registered
in the name of an owner or lessee whose primary residence is located within one of the FIP I/M areas unless evidence is
presented that the EPA Administrator or his/her designee has issued such a vehicle a certificate of compliance with
or a waiver from the applicable requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Operators of subject motor vehicles registered in the FIP I/M areas are prohibited from obtaining vehicle registration
without first meeting all applicable FIP I/M program requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The test provider(s) and its employees, as part of an agreement with the Administrator, shall be prohibited from
the intentional improper testing or retesting of vehicles subject to the FIP I/M program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Commencement date.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The enhanced I/M program, as described in this section, will commence with 100 percent vehicle testing coverage on
January 1, 1997. Given the lateness of this starting date, no phase-in of vehicle coverage shall be assumed, contrary
to the provisions of 40 CFR 51.373. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(g) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vehicle emission inspection cycle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00450 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(1) Biennial inspection.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Vehicles subject to the current 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California I/M program which are registered in the FIP 
<!-- PJG 0034 unknown -->
 I/M areas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be subject to the FIP I/M program and will be tested on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
same biennial schedule as is currently used, with the exception 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that such vehicles shall go to official FIP I/M program test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provider(s) for valid testing. New vehicles which are registered 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in the FIP I/M areas shall be tested in the next even numbered 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calendar year after the initial titling if the model year is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
even, or in the next odd numbered calendar year after the initial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
titling if the model year is odd, and shall be subject to regular 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FIP I/M testing every two years thereafter. Once a vehicle has 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
been tested as part of the FIP I/M program, it will remain on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
same biennial testing schedule until such time as the FIP I/M 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
program is discontinued. The sale of a vehicle shall not change 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that vehicle's regularly scheduled testing date. Vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
previously registered in California but outside the FIP I/M areas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which move into a FIP I/M area shall be tested in time to meet 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the I/M requirement for their first registration as residents of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a FIP I/M area, and shall be tested every two years thereafter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Out-of-cycle inspection.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Vehicles otherwise subject to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the FIP I/M program's requirements which are targeted as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
potential high emitters as a result of RSD detection must be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
presented for an enhanced I/M inspection within 30 days of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notification of the failure (or sooner, if the regularly 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
scheduled inspection deadline occurs first). If the vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fails this confirmatory test, it shall be subject at that time to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the same repair, retest, and waiver requirements as apply to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles which fail the regularly scheduled biennial inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Failure to comply with this out-of-cycle testing requirement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall result in the assessment of a late fee to be collected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prior to testing whenever the vehicle is next presented for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regular testing. A late fee of $10 will be assessed for each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
full week past the testing deadline. Being subject to an out-of-cycle inspection does not change the deadline for
the vehicle's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regularly scheduled biennial inspection, unless it occurs within 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
30 days of the out-of-cycle test. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(h) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Notification of requirement for emission inspection.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
letter of notification shall be sent to subject vehicle owners or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lessees such that the letter shall have been received by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
individual owner or lessee no later than 45 days prior to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regularly scheduled test deadline and no later than 30 days prior 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to an out-of-cycle confirmatory test deadline. In the case of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the out-of-cycle inspection requirement, the notification shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be sent by registered mail to ensure documentation of the owner 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or lessee's receipt of notification. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission inspection period.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The period during which a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject vehicle may be presented for an I/M inspection shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stated on the emission inspection notification form along with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the deadline for completing the inspection process. Subject 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles presented for an initial inspection or reinspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
after the time period shown on the emission inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notification shall be charged a late fee of $10 for each full 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
week that a vehicle is late. This late fee shall be collected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prior to the initiation of testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00451 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(j) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Inspection failure. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) If a subject vehicle fails any phase of the enhanced 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission inspection, the vehicle owner shall have the vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repaired and submit the vehicle for retesting along with a repair 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
form supplied by the test provider (to be completed by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle repair provider). No reinspection shall occur without a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
completed repair form. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) If the subject vehicle fails the retest, and it 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
otherwise meets the waiver requirements for enhanced I/M programs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
addressed under 40 CFR 51.360(a), the vehicle owner may apply for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a waiver. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(k) Enhanced I/M program requirements.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The FIP I/M program 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
design shall include the following program elements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Network type.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Testing shall be performed through a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
centralized system of official emission inspection stations which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be operated by one or more test provider(s) under agreement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test-only.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Official emission inspection stations shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conduct vehicle emission testing only and shall not perform 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle repairs, except to restore the vehicle to the as-received 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
condition after testing (including the reattachment of hoses 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
disconnected for the evaporative system check). Official 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission inspection stations shall meet all the requirements for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test-only stations established in 40 CFR 51.353. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Geographic coverage.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The FIP I/M program shall cover 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the same geographic areas within the Sacramento, Ventura and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
South Coast FIP areas as are covered by the existing California 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Smog Check program as of [
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Insert date of publication of the final 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rule
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
]. (See 40 CFR part 52, subpart GGG, appendix A for a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
detailed listing of I/M FIP area coverage by zip code.) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exhaust emission test type.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All 1966 and newer subject 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles shall be tested using the IM240 transient mass emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test as specified by EPA guidance and regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission control device visual inspection.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All 1971 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and newer subject vehicles shall be visually inspected for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
presence and proper connection of the air pump and positive 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
crankcase ventilation (PCV) systems. The visual inspection of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
these components shall be conducted in compliance with procedures 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
established by EPA guidance and regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Evaporative system tests.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All 1971 and newer subject 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles shall be subject to an evaporative system pressure test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and an evaporative system purge test conducted as specified by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA guidance and regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Onroad testing.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Onroad testing shall be conducted on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approximately 10 percent of the subject fleet using RSD on an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
annual basis. Subject vehicles have been targeted by RSD as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
potential high-emitters shall be subject to out-of-cycle testing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements as specified in paragraph (t) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(l) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Documentation of compliance for vehicles operated on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Federal installations.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Federal installations located within the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
FIP I/M program area shall provide annual documentation of proof 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of compliance with paragraphs (c)(5) and (c)(6) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to EPA. This documentation shall be updated periodically, but at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
least once per inspection cycle. The installation shall use one 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the following methods to establish proof of compliance: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Presentation of a valid certificate of compliance with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or waiver from the FIP I/M program or a comparable I/M program 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i.e., one meeting the enhanced I/M performance standard as set 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
forth in 40 CFR 51.351). In the event the FIP 
<!-- PJG 0034 unknown -->
I/M program adopts 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an electronic-based instrument for certifying vehicle compliance, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the test provider(s) shall make arrangements for issuing a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
special ``Federal vehicle,'' paper-based certificate of compliance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Such a certificate of compliance shall clearly read ``Not Valid 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for Vehicle Registration in the State of California'' in a point 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
size and location which will make it impossible to remove this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
message without destroying the certificate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Presentation of proof of vehicle registration for each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle operating on the grounds of the Federal installation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which is already registered within the geographic area covered by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the FIP I/M program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission inspection criteria for vehicles operated with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
miscellaneous motor vehicle business registration plates or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dealer registration plates.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A subject vehicle which displays a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
miscellaneous motor vehicle business registration plate or a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dealer registration plate shall be exempt from the requirements 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for emission inspection until it reaches two years of age (based 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on model year) at which that time it shall be subject to emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(n) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repair technician training.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Repair technician training 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be provided to all qualified applicants. This training 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will include, at a minimum: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
