<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00452 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) Diagnosis and repair of malfunctions in computer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
controlled close-loop vehicles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Application of emission control theory and diagnostic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
data to the diagnosis and repair of failures of the transient 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission test and the evaporative system function tests. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Utilization of diagnostic information on systematic or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repeated failures observed in the transient emission test and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evaporative system function tests. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Generalized training on the various subsystems related 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to emission control. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(o) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission test procedures.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Emission tests and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
functional tests shall be subject to the following requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Flexibly fueled vehicles (i.e., those capable of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operating both on gasoline and other fuels) shall at a minimum be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject to testing and shall be tested while operating in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gasoline mode unless the vehicle is never operated with gasoline. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) An initial test is the emission test that occurs the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
first time in a test cycle. The initial test shall be performed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
without repair or adjustment at the emission inspection station 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prior to the test, except as provided for in the evaporative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system integrity test. An emission inspection performed after 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
failure of the initial test in a test cycle shall be considered a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
retest. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) An official test, once initiated, shall be performed in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
its entirety regardless of intermediate outcomes except in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
case of an invalid test condition or unsafe conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Tests involving measurements shall be performed with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved equipment that has been calibrated according to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
quality control procedures contained in EPA guidance or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Vehicles shall not be tested if the exhaust system is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
missing or leaking, or if the vehicle is in an unsafe condition. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) The vehicle owner or driver shall have access to an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area in the inspection station which permits observation of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
entire official inspection procedure. This access may be limited 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
but it may not prevent full observation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) In the inspection process, vehicles that have been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
altered from their original certified configuration shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tested in the same manner as other subject vehicles, in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Vehicles with engines other than the engine originally 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
installed by the manufacturer, or an identical replacement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine, shall be subject to the test procedures and standards for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the chassis type and model year, regardless of the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replacement, including visual equipment inspections for parts 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that are part of the original certified configuration and part of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the normal inspection for such configuration. An exception may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be made if the vehicle meets new certification standards for that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
chassis and model year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Vehicles which are switched to a fuel type for which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
there is no certified configuration shall be tested according to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the emission standards established for that vehicle type and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
model year. Emission control device requirements may be waived 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
if the Administrator determines that the alternatively fueled 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle configuration would meet the new vehicle standards for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that model year without these devices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(p) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission standards.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Subject vehicles shall be tested 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and passed or failed according to the IM240 cutpoints provided in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appendix B of subpart GGG of this part. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(q) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission inspection test report.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The test provider(s) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall provide the vehicle owner or driver with a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
computer-generated emission inspection test report which includes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) A vehicle description, including license plate number, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle title number, VIN, vehicle make and model and odometer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reading. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The date and time of the test. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The name or identification number of the individuals 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performing the tests and the location of the test station and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lane number. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) The type of tests performed, including emission tests, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
visual checks for the presence of emission control components, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and functional, evaporative system checks. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) The applicable test standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) The test results, including exhaust concentrations and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pass/fail results for each mode measured, pass/fail results for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evaporative system checks, and which emission control devices 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspected were passed, failed or not applicable. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) A statement indicating the availability of warranty 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coverage as required in section 207 of the Clean Air Act (42 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
U.S.C. 7525). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00453 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(8) A certification that tests were performed in accordance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(9) For vehicles that fail the tailpipe emission test, any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
available information on the possible causes of the specific 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pattern of high emission levels found during the test. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(10) For vehicles that fail the enhanced I/M test, a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
description of the consumer complaint procedure, including a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
statement indicating that any administrative challenge regarding 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the performance or results of the test must be made by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle owner or operator within 10 days of the failure of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(r) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Retest. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Procedure. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Vehicles that fail the initial test or a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
retest shall be retested after repair to determine if the repairs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
were effective for any portion of the inspection that was failed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on the previous test. To the extent that repair to correct a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
previous failure could lead to failure of another portion of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
test, that portion shall also be retested. Evaporative system 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repairs performed as a result of the vehicle's failing either the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evaporative system purge or pressure test shall be cause for a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
complete retest covering all of the initial test requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Prerequisites. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For a retest, the vehicle owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
driver shall present to the inspection station the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection test report and a completed repair data form. If the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repairs were performed by the owner or someone other than a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recognized repair technician, the repair data form shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
completed by the person performing the repair. If the repairs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
were performed at a recognized repair facility, the repair data 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
form completed by the repair facility shall be presented to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission inspection station. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Content of repair data form. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The repair data form shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
include the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The repairs performed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The cost of repairs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The repair technician's number or name if the person 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
who made the repairs does not have a license number issued by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California Bureau of Automotive Repair. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Any repairs recommended by the repair facility that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
were not performed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The name, address and telephone number of the repair 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(s) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Issuance of a waiver. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The emission inspection station 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall issue a certificate of emission inspection with an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
indicator to show that the vehicle has received a waiver if all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the following are complied with: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The subject vehicle has failed the initial emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection, qualifying repairs have been completed and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject vehicle has failed the retest. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Emission control devices, as originally equipped, are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
installed. Vehicles with emission devices which are obsolete and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cannot be obtained through the original equipment manufacturer, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aftermarket manufacturers or suppliers of used parts are exempt 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from this paragraph. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The amount spent on qualifying repairs shall: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Be at least $450 adjusted annually in January by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
percentage by which the Consumer Price Index for the current year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
differs from the 1989 Consumer Price Index. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Include parts costs and labor costs paid for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
qualifying emission repair services performed on the vehicle if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paid by the vehicle owner and if the qualifying repairs were 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performed by a recognized repair technician. For qualifying 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission repair services performed on pre-1980 vehicles, by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
someone other than a recognized repair technician, parts costs 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
but not labor costs shall be counted toward the minimum cost 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limit. For qualifying emission repair services performed on 1980 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and newer vehicles, by someone other than a recognized repair 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
technician, neither parts costs nor labor costs may be counted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
toward the minimum cost limit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Be considered qualifying if they are appropriate to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the cause of the test failure. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Exclude expenses which are incurred in the repair of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission control devices which are found to be tampered with, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rendered inoperative, or not installed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Exclude costs recoverable under an emission warranty, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
insurance policy or prepaid maintenance agreement. These 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recoverable cost repairs shall be completed before necessary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repair costs can be applied toward the waiver cost limitations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The operator of a vehicle within the statutory age and mileage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
coverage under section 207(b) of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
7525(b)) shall present a written denial of warranty coverage from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the manufacturer or authorized dealer for this provision to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
waived. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Exclude the fee for emission inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) Exclude charges for giving a written estimate of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
needed repairs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) Exclude charges for checking for the presence of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission control devices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ix) Exclude costs for repairs performed on the vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
before the initial test failure. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) The vehicle owner or driver shall present the original 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of repair bills to the inspection station to demonstrate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with the qualifying dollar amount for that year. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
bills shall: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Include the name, address and phone number of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repair facility. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Describe the repairs that were performed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) State the labor and parts costs separately for each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repair. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Upon completion of waiver requirements and a visual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
check to determine that repairs were actually made, a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certification of emission inspection, with a waiver indicator, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be made for the subject vehicle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(t) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Onroad testing. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Onroad testing of subject vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be conducted using RSD in each FIP I/M program area using a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
carbon monoxide (CO) cutpoint of 4 percent to screen for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
potential gross emitters. The onroad testing program will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
aimed at identifying 10 percent of the subject fleet for follow-up, out-of-cycle confirmatory testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00454 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Failure of onroad emission test. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The owner or operator 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of a subject vehicle that fails an onroad emission test shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notified by registered mail to report for an out-of-cycle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
confirmatory test. The notification of the need for confirmatory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
testing shall be received by the vehicle owner or lessee no later 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than 30 days prior to the confirmatory test deadline. If the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject vehicle does not have a valid emissions test waiver and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fails the confirmatory test, the owner or operator shall have 30 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
days following the initial confirmatory test failure in which to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
have the failed vehicle repaired and retested. The vehicle owner 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or operator shall be notified of this obligation as part of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
initial RSD-failure notification process. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Failure to produce proof of correction of onroad 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission test failure. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
If the owner of the subject vehicle fails 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to comply with a notice of RSD failure within 30 days of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
receiving the notice by registered mail, a late penalty will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
assessed at the time the vehicle is presented for confirmatory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
testing, or at the time of the next regularly scheduled test, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whichever comes first. The late penalty is a $10 fee for each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
full week beyond the 30-day deadline after initial notification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the need for confirmatory testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Failure to procure repairs and retest after initial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
confirmatory test failure. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
If a subject vehicle fails an initial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
confirmatory test and the owner or lessee fails to procure the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
necessary repairs and retest within 30 days of the initial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
confirmatory test failure, a late penalty shall be assessed at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the time the vehicle is presented for retesting, or at the time 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the next regularly scheduled test, whichever comes first. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
late penalty is a $10 fee for each full week beyond the 30-day 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
deadline for receiving a passing retest or waiver after the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
initial confirmatory test failure. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(u) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Certified emission inspectors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) General. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Personnel who perform emission inspections at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
each emission inspection station operated by the test provider(s) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be certified by the Administrator as emission inspectors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The emission inspection shall only be performed by certified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission inspectors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Certified emission inspector requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An inspector 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
desiring to be certified shall: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Be at least 18 years of age. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Have completed an emission inspection training course, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved by the Administrator, that includes, at a minimum, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information on the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The air pollution problem, including its cause and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
effects. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The purpose, function and goal of the inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Emission inspection regulations and procedures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Technical details of the test procedures and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rationale for their design. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Emission control device function, configuration and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) Test equipment operation, calibration and maintenance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) Quality control procedures and their purpose. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(H) Public relations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(I) Safety and health issues related to the inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
process. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Passed a required written test addressing the above 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
elements with a minimum of 80 percent correct test responses. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Demonstrated the ability to properly utilize test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment and to follow other required procedures by means of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hands-on test addressing the complete emission inspection. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inability to properly conduct the test procedures shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
constitute failure of the test. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Renew the certification every 2 years under procedures 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
established by the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Identification. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
While conducting inspections, a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certified emission inspector shall have in his/her possession a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
currently valid inspector certification card issued by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test provider(s) obligations and responsibilities. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Personal liability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The test provider(s) or those 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
acting as agents of the test providers(s) shall assume full 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
responsibility for: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Conducting the business of the official emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection station honestly and in a manner consistent with this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, and making every reasonable effort to inspect all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles upon request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Making official emission inspection regulations and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
supplements available for the use of certified emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspectors and other employees involved in the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection process. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Notifying EPA and the oversight contractor when a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certified emission inspector is hired, resigns or is dismissed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Maintaining emission inspection records for examination 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by EPA or the oversight contractor. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Providing the vehicle emission inspection test report to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
motorists after testing and having the repair requirements stated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on a form provided to the vehicle owner or operator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Insuring full compliance with this section with respect 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Every emission inspection conducted at the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection station. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Every emission inspection waiver issued at the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection station. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Every certification of emission inspection made to and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by each emission inspection station. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Every provision of this section related to emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspections performed by an employee of the emission inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
station. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Assuring the proper maintenance and calibration of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission inspection equipment according to procedures established 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in EPA's high-tech procedures guidance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) Completing and retaining emission equipment maintenance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and calibration records as required by EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) Placing emission equipment out of service when 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calibration cannot be performed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(H) Maintaining computer records of each inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



