<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(I) Making records available to EPA or the oversight 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contractor during periodic station audits. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission test data
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The requirements for data 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
collection and transmission shall be as specified in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agreement between the Administrator and the test provider(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repair performance monitoring
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The test provider(s) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be responsible for collecting and maintaining emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repair information concerning subject vehicles that have failed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the emission inspection and have been returned for a retest. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
particulars of this requirement will be detailed in the agreement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
between the EPA Administrator and the test provider(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(w) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality control
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality control requirements for test provider(s)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Quality control measures shall be implemented by the test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provider(s) and shall ensure that emission measurement equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is calibrated and maintained according to the procedures in this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section and in the agreement between the EPA Administrator and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the test provider(s). Inspection, calibration records and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control charts shall be accurately created and recorded and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintained as prescribed in this section and in the agreement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
between the Administrator and the test provider(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
General requirements
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. General requirements for quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control practices for test equipment shall be as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The practices described in this section, in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agreement and in 40 CFR part 51, subpart S, appendix A (relating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to calibrations, adjustments and quality control), and EPA's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
high-tech procedures document shall be followed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Preventive maintenance on inspection equipment shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performed on a periodic basis, as provided by in the agreement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
between the Administrator and the test provider(s) consistent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the equipment manufacturer's requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) To assure quality control, computerized analyzers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall automatically record quality control check information, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lockouts, attempted tampering with test equipment and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
circumstances which require a service representative to work on 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) To assure test accuracy, equipment shall be maintained 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
according to demonstrated good engineering practices. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Computer control of quality assurance checks and quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control charts shall be used whenever possible. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirements for transient exhaust emission testing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Calibration and maintenance procedures for transient 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exhaust emission testing equipment shall be conducted as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in EPA guidance and regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirements for the purge analysis system
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Calibration and maintenance procedures for the purge analysis 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
system shall be conducted as specified in EPA guidance and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirements for evaporative system pressure test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Calibration and maintenance procedures for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evaporative system pressure test equipment shall be conducted as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in EPA guidance and regulation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(x) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quality assurance
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Performance audits
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The oversight contractor(s) will 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conduct performance audits on a periodic basis to determine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whether inspectors are correctly performing the tests and other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
required functions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Performance audits shall be of two types: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Overt performance audits which shall include the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A check for appropriate document security. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A check to see that required recordkeeping practices 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are being followed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) A check for licenses or certificates and other required 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
display information. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
4
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Observation and written evaluation of each inspector's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ability to properly perform an inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Covert performance audits which shall include the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Remote visual observation of inspector and inspection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
station personnel performance, which may include the use of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
binoculars or video cameras. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Site visits using covert vehicles presented for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Other activities deemed appropriate by the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The test provider(s) and the employees of the test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provider(s) shall make available information requested by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
oversight contractor(s) and shall fully cooperate with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
oversight contractor's personnel who conduct the audits and other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authorized EPA representatives or agents. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00456 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Document security
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Measures shall be taken to maintain 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the security of documents and/or instrumentation by which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with the inspection requirements is established. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(y) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Penalties for test provider(s)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The test provider(s) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall assume full responsibility, with or without actual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
knowledge, for the complete operation of an official emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection station, including the actions of emission inspectors. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Failure to comply with the appropriate provisions of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or the provisions prescribed in the agreement between the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator and the test provider(s) will be considered 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sufficient cause for imposing civil penalties for violation of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the applicable implementation plan or damages under the contract, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as applicable. In addition thereto, intentional violations may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be subject to criminal prosecution where they meet the grounds 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for prosecution under any federal criminal statute. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(z) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Penalties for emission inspectors
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) An emission inspector shall assume full responsibility 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for his/her acts as an emission inspector. Failure to comply 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the appropriate provisions of this section will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered sufficient cause for suspension of an emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspector's certification. In addition, intentional violations 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
may also be subject to criminal prosecution where they meet the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
grounds for prosecution under any federal criminal statute. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
After providing the emission inspector with an opportunity for a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hearing, the Administrator may impose suspensions or penalties 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upon the emission inspector for the following categories of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
offenses: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Category 1. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Issuance or possession of altered, forged, stolen or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
counterfeit certificates of emission inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Furnishing, lending, giving, selling or receiving a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certificate of emission inspection without inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Fraudulent recordkeeping. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) Fraudulent inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Category 2. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Improper recordkeeping. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Improper inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Improper assigning of certificate of emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Duration of suspension
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Category 1. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) First offense: 1 year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Second offense: permanent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Category 2. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) First offense: 3 months. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Second offense: 6 months. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Third offense: 1 year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Multiple violations
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Violations affecting more than one 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle will be treated as separate violations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Opportunity for an EPA hearing
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Except for a penalty or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sanction imposed directly under the terms of the agreement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
between the EPA Administrator and the test provider(s), a person 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
charged with a violation of this section shall have the right to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
request a hearing regarding the charges. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;52.2964
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Importation of vehicles into California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) The State of California may not permit California 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
residents to register for the first time in California any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle that was previously registered in another state, unless 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that vehicle was originally certified to the FIP's durable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicle standards for its class. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) California residents may not own and keep a car in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California that is currently registered in another state. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) As an exception to paragraphs (a) and (b) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the State of California may allow recent immigrants to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California (defined as residents of California for less than 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
three months) to register a car, over 7500 miles, that they had 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
previously registered for at least three months in another state 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
while a resident of that state. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Implementation date
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. This program shall be implemented 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on January 1, 1999. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;52.2965
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Requirements for engines past their useful life. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
General applicability
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Heavy-duty on-highway engines 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certified to applicable engine standards contained in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.2966(c) and (d) and nonroad engines certified to applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine standards contained in &sect;52.2975 (c) and (d) shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject to the provisions contained in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions and abbreviations
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 The definitions and abbreviations of parts 86 and 89 of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
chapter, the definitions contained in &sect;52.2966(b), and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
definitions contained in the Clean Air Act apply to this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unless a term is also defined in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Engine configuration
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a complete set of engine and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions control system parts, components, specifications, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calibrations, and other items deemed necessary by a engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifier to restore an engine to its original 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration or another configuration meeting applicable recall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Useful life renewal
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the period in years and miles or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hours specified by the engine configuration certifier over which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the engine configuration certifier assumes recall liability for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engines of the certified configuration. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Owner requirements
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. An owner of a vehicle or equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipped with an engine subject to the provisions of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, at all times must be able to demonstrate either: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) That the engine in the vehicle or nonroad equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
being registered is within its original useful life, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) That the engine in the vehicle or nonroad equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
being registered is within the useful life renewal period as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
defined by the certifier of the engine's configuration pursuant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to paragraph (d) of this section. The owner shall make this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstration by presenting the useful life renewal certificate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
furnished by the engine configuration certifier pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (f) of this section. Failure to provide such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstration at time of vehicle or equipment registration shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
result in the denial of vehicle or equipment registration. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Useful life renewal
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The certifier of an engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration shall define the useful life renewal period in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years and miles or hours over which the engine configuration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certifier accepts liability for an engine(s) that does not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conform to applicable recall standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Useful life renewal certificate
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. (1) The certifier of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an engine configuration shall provide to the owner a certificate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with each engine that is restored to the certified engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration. The certificate shall contain the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The useful life renewal period; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00457 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(ii) For on-highway engines, the effective date and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
odometer mileage of the useful life renewal period; For nonroad 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engines, the effective date and hours; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The vehicle or equipment identification number. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The engine configuration certifier shall designate an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
office or officer to receive a copy of completed certificates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The certificates shall be stored in an adequately organized and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
indexed file or the information required by paragraph (e)(1) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section shall be entered into a database completely and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stored. The certificate or information in the database shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stored for a period not less than the useful life renewal period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Engine configuration certification
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifiers shall demonstrate certification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test procedure and emission results
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Certification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions testing of engine configurations shall be conducted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
using new engine certification testing procedures specified in &sect;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
52.2966(e) for on-highway heavy-duty engines and &sect;52.2975(e) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for nonroad engines. Certification emissions testing must be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
carried out using representative production equipment as provided 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in paragraph (f)(2) of this section. The test results must 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
demonstrate that engines restored to the engine configuration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
being certified will comply with the applicable recall standards 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
over the useful life renewal period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emissions test engine selection
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The test engine shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be an engine representative of the engine family and that is at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or beyond the end of its original useful life. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) To demonstrate compliance with the applicable recall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standards, the test engine shall be restored to the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration being certified in accordance with the instructions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that are to be followed when restoring actual in-use engines. No 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other maintenance or adjustments shall be performed on the test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test fuel
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The engine configuration shall be certified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
using the same fuel used for new engine certification as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in &sect;52.2966 (f) for heavy-duty on-highway engines and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.2975 (f) for nonroad engines. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Component selection
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Where replacement components are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used to restore an engine to the configuration being certified, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certification shall be based upon tests utilizing representative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
production parts and components selected in a random manner. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Replacing original equipment parts
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Changes to an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine shall not result in the permanent removal or rendering 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inoperative of any original equipment emission related part other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than the part(s) being replaced. Furthermore, engine changes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall not cause or contribute to an unreasonable risk to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
public health, welfare or safety, or result in any additional 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
range of parameter adjustability or accessibility to adjustment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than that of the vehicle or equipment manufacturer's emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
related part. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Effects on engine on-board diagnostic system
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Changes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to an engine shall not alter or render inoperative any feature of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the on-board diagnostic system incorporated by the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer. The engine configuration being certified may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
integrate with the existing diagnostic system if it does not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
alter or render inoperative any features of the system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(g) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
In-use recall
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Engines restored to an engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certified pursuant to paragraph (f) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
within its useful life renewal period, shall be subject to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recall provisions contained in &sect;52.2966(g). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(h) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Notification of intent to certify
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. (1) Prior to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
issuance of any useful life renewal certificate, notification of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the intent to certify must be approved by the MOD Director. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) All notifications shall include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Identification and description of the candidate engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration to be certified, including a list of replacement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
parts and part numbers; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Identification of the engine family including make(s), 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine model(s), model year(s), engine size(s) and all other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specific configuration characteristics; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Identification and description of any emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
related component(s) not being replaced and rationale as to why 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
its replacement is unnecessary; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00458 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iv) All results and documentation of tests and procedures 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used by the engine configuration certifier as evidence of compliance with applicable recall emission standards;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) A description of the test replacement part selection criteria used, and a statement that the replacement parts
used for certification testing is representative production equipment consistent with paragraph (f)(1)(v) of
this section;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) A description of the test engine selection criteria used, and rationale that supports the technical judgment
of the engine configuration certifier that the engine meets the requirements of paragraphs (f)(1)(ii) and (f)(1)(iii)
of this section;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) Results of durability testing and an engineering analysis showing that the emissions performance of engines
can be expected to be maintained over the useful life renewal period;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) A copy of any written installation instructions that are to be used and a copy of the warranty to be provided to
the owner;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ix) A copy of the written instructions for proper maintenance and use of the engine during the useful life renewal
period;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(x) A copy of the useful life renewal certificate to be provided to the owner pursuant to paragraph (e) of this section;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(xi) A statement of commitment and willingness to comply with all the relevant terms and conditions of this section;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(xii) A statement by the engine configuration certifier that changes done to an engine to bring it to the engine configuration
being certified will not cause a substantial increase to engine emissions in any normal driving mode not represented
during certification testing; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(xiii) The office or officer of the engine configuration certifier authorized to receive correspondence regarding
certification requirements pursuant to this subpart.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The notification shall be signed by an officer of the engine configuration certifier attesting to the accuracy
and completeness of the information supplied in the notification.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Notification to the Agency shall be by certified mail or another method by which date of receipt can be established.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Two complete and identical copies of the notification and any subsequent industry comments on any such notification
shall be submitted by the engine configuration certifier to: MOD Director, MOD (6405J), Attention: Engine Configuration
Certification, 401 ``M'' Street SW, Washington, DC 20460.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) [Reserved].
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(j) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Objections to certification. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) At any time prior to certification, the MOD Director may notify the engine configuration certifier that such its
engine configuration shall not be certified pending further investigation. The basis upon which this notification
shall be made may include, but not be limited to, information or test results submitted by the engine configuration
certifier including:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The test procedure used to demonstrate compliance with the applicable recall standards does not meet the requirements
of paragraph (f) of this section;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Use of the candidate engine configuration could cause or contribute to an unreasonable risk to public health,
welfare or safety in its operation or function;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Installation of the candidate replacement parts requires procedures or materials which would likely cause
such parts to be improperly installed under normal conditions or would likely result in an engine being misadjusted;
or
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Information and/or data required to be in the notification of intent to certify as provided by paragraph (h) of
this section have not been provided or may be inadequate.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The engine configuration certifier must respond in writing to the statements made in the notification by the MOD
Director, or the MOD Director shall withdraw the notification of intent to certify.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The MOD Director may, at his or her discretion, allow oral presentations by the engine configuration certifier.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) If notification has been provided to an engine configuration certifier pursuant to paragraph (j) of this section,
the MOD Director shall, after reviewing all pertinent data and information, render a decision and inform the engine
configuration certifier in writing as to whether such engine configuration may be certified and, if so, under what
conditions the engine configuration may be certified. The written decision shall include an explanation of the reasons
therefor.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The decision by the MOD Director shall be provided to the engine configuration certifier after receipt of all necessary
information by the certifier or interested parties, or of the date of any oral presentation regarding the certification,
whichever occurs second.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Within 20 days of receipt of a decision made pursuant to paragraph (j)(4)(i) of this section, any party may file
a written appeal to the Office Director. The Office Director may, in his or her discretion, allow additional oral or
written submissions, prior to rendering a final decision.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) If no party files an appeal with the Office Director within 20 days, then the decision of the MOD Director shall
be final.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The Office Director shall make a final decision regarding the certification of engine configuration after receipt
of all necessary information by the engine configuration certifier or from the date of any oral presentation, whichever
occurs later.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(k) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Changes after certification. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The engine configuration certifier shall recertify any engine configuration which was certified pursuant to paragraph
(f) of this section and to which modifications are made affecting emissions or the capability of the engine to meet
any other requirement of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(l) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Labeling requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) All engine configurations certified pursuant to this section shall contain a label affixed to the rebuilt engine
that states:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Identification of the engine configuration; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00459 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(ii) The useful life renewal period provided by the certifier pursuant to paragraph (d) of this section;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) A place for the certifier to record the date and the mileage of the useful life renewal period. The label containing
the information must be made durable and readable for at least the useful life renewal period; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The statement:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=81 g=1 f=1 -->
Certified to EPA In-Use Recall Emissions Standards
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=10 g=1 f=1 -->
contains:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(2) The certifier shall ensure that all of the information that is entered on the label supplied by the engine configuration
certifier pursuant to paragraph (l)(1) of this section is accurate and complete and that the label is securely affixed
to the engine, upon the completion of all activities necessary to bring the engine to the certified configuration.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The package in which any replacement parts are contained, or an insert as described in paragraph (j)(4) of this
section, must have the following information conspicuously placed thereon:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The statement ``Certified by (name of engine configuration certifier) to EPA In-use Recall Emission Standards'';
and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The engine family for which the parts are certified.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) The package in which the parts are contained must include the following information provided on a written insert:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The engine family for which the parts are certified, unless such information is provided as specified in paragraph
(j)(2) of this section;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) A list of all of the parts and identification numbers for the parts included; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00460 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iii) The instructions for proper installation of the parts; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) A description of the maintenance necessary to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performed on the engine during its useful life renewal period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Maintenance and submittal of records by engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifiers. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) For each certified engine configuration, the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifier must establish, maintain and retain for 5 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years from the date of certification the following adequately 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
organized and indexed records: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Detailed production drawings showing all dimensions, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tolerances, performance requirements and material specifications 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and any other information necessary to completely describe the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine configuration; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) All data obtained during testing of the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration and subsequent analyses based on that data, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
including the mileage and the vehicle or engine configuration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determinants; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) All information used in determining the engine for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which the replacement parts or components are represented as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
being equivalent from an emissions standpoint to the original 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment parts being replaced; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) A description of the quality control plan used to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
monitor production and assure compliance of in-use engines with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the applicable requirements; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) All data taken in implementing the quality control plan, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and any subsequent analyses of that data; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) All in-service data, analyses performed by the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifier and correspondence with rebuilders, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vendors, distributors, consumers, retail outlets or engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturers regarding any design, production or in-service 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
problems associated with 25 or more engines of the same engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The records required to be maintained in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m)(1) of this section shall be made available to the Agency upon 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the written request of the MOD Director. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(n) Decertification. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The MOD Director may notify a engine configuration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certifier that the Agency has made a preliminary determination 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that a certain engine configuration should be decertified. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Such a preliminary determination may be made if there is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reason to believe that the engine configuration has failed to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
comply with the requirements of this section. Information upon 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which such a determination will be made includes but is not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited to the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The engine configuration was certified on the basis of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions tests, and the procedures used in such tests were not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in substantial compliance with a portion or portions of the test 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedures required to be used pursuant to paragraph (e)(1) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Use of the certified engine configuration is causing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions to exceed any in-use recall emission standard; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Use of the engine configuration causes or contributes to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an unreasonable risk to public health, welfare or safety or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
severely degrades driveability operation or function; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) The engine configuration has been modified in a manner 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requiring recertification pursuant to paragraph (k) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) The engine configuration certifier has not established, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintained or retained the records required pursuant to paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m)(1) of this section or fails to make the records available to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the MOD Director upon written request pursuant to paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m)(2) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Notice of a preliminary determination to decertify 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall contain: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A description of the noncomplying engine configuration; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The basis for the MOD Director's preliminary decision; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) The date by which the certifier must: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Terminate the issuance of useful life renewals; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
2
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Make the necessary change (if so recommended by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Agency); or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
3
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
) Request an opportunity in writing to dispute the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
allegations of the preliminary decertification. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (2) If the engine configuration certifier requests an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
opportunity to respond to the preliminary determination, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer and other parties interested in the MOD Director's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
decision whether to decertify the engine configuration shall, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
within 15 days of the date of the request, submit written 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
presentations, including the relevant information and data, to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the MOD Director. The MOD Director, in his or her discretion, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
may provide an opportunity for oral presentations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

