<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00461 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) Any interested party may request additional time to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
respond to the information submitted by the engine configuration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certifier. The MOD Director upon a showing of good cause by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
interested party may grant an extension of time to reply up to 30 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
days. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The engine configuration certifier may have an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extension of up to 30 days to reply to information submitted by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
interested parties. Notification of intent to reply shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submitted to the MOD Director within 10 days of the date 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information from interested parties is submitted to the MOD 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Director. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) If a engine configuration certifier has disputed the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
allegations of the preliminary decisions, the MOD Director shall, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
after reviewing any additional information, notify the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifier of his or her decision whether the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration may continue to be sold as certified. This 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notification shall include an explanation upon which the decision 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
was made and the effective date for decertification, where 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appropriate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Within 20 days from the date of a decision made pursuant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to paragraph (n)(3) of this section, any adversely affected party 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
may appeal the decision to the Office Director. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) A petition for appeal to the Office Director must state 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all of the reasons why the decision of the MOD Director should be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reversed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The Office Director may, in his or her discretion, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
allow additional oral or written testimony. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) If no appeal is filed with the Office Director within 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the permitted time period, the decision of the MOD Director shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be final. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) If a final decision is made to decertify an engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration under paragraph (n)(4) of this section, the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifier shall notify his immediate customers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that, as of the date of the final determination, the engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration in question has been decertified. The engine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
configuration certifier shall offer to replace engines of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
decertified engine configurations in the customer's inventory 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with certified replacement engines or, if unable to do so, shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at the customer's request repurchase such inventory at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable price. The immediate customers must stop selling the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engines once the certifier has notified the customer that the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
engine configuration has been decertified. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) Notwithstanding the requirements of paragraph (n)(5) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section, an engine purchased by an owner prior to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
decertification, shall be considered certified pursuant to this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;52.2966 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Enhanced in-use compliance heavy-duty engine and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 vehicle program. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
General applicability.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 New 1999 model year and later 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
heavy-duty vehicles and engines, other than medium-duty vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certified to the standards contained in &sect;52.2962, that are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registered exclusively in California or that are offered for sale 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in California, shall meet the standards and requirements 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specified in paragraphs (c) through (h) of this section, and in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.2965. Other state and federal requirements may also apply 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to these vehicles and engines. Heavy-duty vehicles that are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registered in California and that are also registered in other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
states shall be subject to the requirements specified in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (h) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions and abbreviations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The definitions and abbreviations of parts 86 and 88 of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
chapter and the definitions contained in the Clean Air Act apply 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to this section unless a term is also defined in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
New,
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 when applied to motor vehicles, means a motor vehicle, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equitable or legal title to which has never been transferred to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an ultimate purchaser. It is conclusively presumed that the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equitable or legal title to a motor vehicle, other than a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
motorcycle, with an odometer reading of 7,500 miles or more, has 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
been transferred to an ultimate purchaser, and that the equitable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or legal title to a motor vehicle, other than a motorcycle, with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an odometer reading of less than 7,500 miles has not been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transferred to an ultimate purchaser. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission standards.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 For the purposes of certification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and recall testing, exhaust emissions shall not exceed the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-methane hydrocarbons.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 0.2 to 0.6 grams per brake 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
horsepower-hour, as measured under transient operating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Oxides of nitrogen.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 1.5 grams per brake horsepower-hour, as measured under transient operating conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00462 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(d)(1) For the purposes of certification and recall testing, evaporative hydrocarbon emissions shall not exceed
the applicable federal heavy-duty engine evaporative emissions standards described in 40 CFR part 86. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Manufacturers' applications for certification shall include test results or an engineering evaluation demonstrating
compliance with the inherently low evaporative emission requirements of &sect;88.311&hyph;93(a)(1)(ii) and
(a)(2) of this chapter. Diurnal emission levels shall be adjusted to reflect corresponding results for a nominal
20 gallon fuel tank volume. This demonstration may be based on a diurnal temperature excursion of 65
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F to 105
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F and California certification fuel rather than the EPA conditions and test fuel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test procedures. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) The exhaust emission standards set forth in paragraph (c) of this section refer to the exhaust emissions collected
under the conditions and measured in accordance with the procedures set forth in 40 CFR part 86, subpart N, except as
specified in paragraph (f) of this section. Assembly line testing procedures are those set forth in 40 CFR part 86,
subpart K, except as specified in paragraph (f) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The evaporative standards set forth in paragraph (d)(1) of this section refer to the evaporative emissions collected
under the conditions and measured in accordance with the procedures set forth in 40 CFR part 86, subpart M, except as
specified in paragraph (f) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test fuels. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All certification, assembly line, and recall testing performed on vehicles and engines covered under this section
shall use the fuels provided for by California as found in the California regulations. Testing performed to demonstrate
compliance with the inherently low evaporative emission requirements of paragraph (d)(2) of this section may, as
an alternative, be conducted with fuels meeting the federal specifications of 40 CFR part 86. Assembly line and recall
testing shall use the same type of fuel as used in certification testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(g) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recall program. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) Engines certified to the standards set forth in this section shall be subject to the recall provisions described
in this paragraph. For purposes of recall testing under this section, the term ``engine'' includes all emissions
control systems. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The recall provisions for light-duty vehicles contained in &sect;52.2962(e) shall apply to engines subject
to the provisions of this paragraph as well, with appropriate references to applicable standards and test procedures,
except that: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Engines shall be selected by EPA for purposes of recall testing from the vehicle population of the entire state
rather than only from areas subject to enhanced inspection and maintenance testing; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The provisions of &sect;52.2965 shall also apply. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(h) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fleet averaging program. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
General applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of this program apply to all heavy-duty vehicles of over 19,500 pounds GVWR that are registered in
California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Effective January 1, 2000, any person who owns one or more heavy-duty vehicles of over 19,500 pounds GVWR that are
registered in California shall submit the following information on each of these affected fleet vehicles to EPA by
January 31st of every calendar year. The submittal shall reflect the owner's affected fleet as it existed on January
1st of the same calendar year. Owners may combine their affected vehicles with those of other vehicle owners for the
purposes of this program. Required information per affected vehicle: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Vehicle license number; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Engine model year; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Engine identification number; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) GVWR. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3)(i) The results of the following Fleet Average Emissions (FAE) calculations contained in Tables 2966&hyph;1
and 2966&hyph;2 shall be submitted concurrently with the per vehicle information specified in paragraph (h)(2)
of this section; separate calculations shall be performed, and results submitted, for affected vehicles of GVWR
between 19,501&hyph;33,000 pounds and for affected vehicles of over 33,000 pounds GVWR: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
