<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iv) NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emissions from locomotives owned or operated by a railroad company and operated in the South Coast shall average 5.5
g/bhp-hr or less effective January 1, 2007. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 emissions from locomotives owned or operated by a railroad company and operated in the South Coast shall average 4
g/bhp-hr or less effective January 1, 2010. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test methods and procedures. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Test methods and procedures which will be adopted for the national locomotive emission control program shall apply
in this South Coast Locomotive FIP. The applicable reference for the national locomotive emission control program
will be provided when promulgated. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Enforcement. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Inspections. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All sources subject to provisions of this section shall be subject to unannounced inspections by representatives
of EPA pursuant to section 114 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7401&hyph;7671q). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Information requests. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Documentation maintained by all sources, facilities, and persons subject to paragraph (c) of this section must be
sufficient to demonstrate compliance with all the requirements of paragraph (b) of this section and must be provided
to representatives of EPA in response to information requests pursuant to section 114 of the Clean Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Testing. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All sources subject to provisions of this section shall be subject to testing by representatives of EPA pursuant to
section 114 of the Clean Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Failure to comply with any provisions of this section is a violation of the applicable implementation plan for
purposes of section 113 of the Clean Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
