<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00472 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting and recordkeeping. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Each owner or operator of a locomotive emission source which is subject to the limitations of this section, shall submit
to the administrator by April 1, of each calendar year, beginning in 2007, a certification of compliance with this
section for the previous calendar year. This certification shall include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) A declaration that the company is in compliance with all the requirements of this section, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Documentation of the methods used to meet the NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 fleet emission average required in paragraph (a)(4) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Each owner or operator of locomotive emission sources which is subject to the limitations of this section shall
collect and record all information necessary to demonstrate compliance with this section. These records shall be
maintained for a period of 5 years. The information shall be collected and recorded for each year starting in 2007.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Testing and monitoring. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The Administrator may require, at any time, any owner or operator of a locomotive emission source subject to the limitations
of this section to perform tests using the applicable test methods defined in the national locomotive emission control
program when finalized, to demonstrate compliance with the limitations of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fees and noncompliance penalties. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Railroad companies that own and/or operate a locomotive within the confines of the South Coast which is designated
as a South Coast locomotive engine shall pay an annual fee for each locomotive engine they operate in the South Coast.
[Such fee is to be developed in this rulemaking.] 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Any engine that EPA finds operating in the South Coast that is not properly identified as a designated South Coast
locomotive or without proper maintenance shall be fined an amount not to exceed $25,000 per day of improper operation.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) A noncompliance penalty for each ton of emissions produced by a railroad company above its emission cap as provided
for in paragraph (a)(4) of this section, shall be assessed at a rate of $10,000 per ton of emissions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=3 -->
&sect;52.2972 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=3 -->
Military aircraft operations. [Implementing program described in section III(D)(4)(e)(2)(c) of the Supplementary
Information section.] 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=3 -->
&sect;52.2973 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=3 -->
Ships and ports. [Implementing program described in Section III(D)(4)(e)(iv) of the Supplementary Information
section.] 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=3 -->
&sect;52.2974 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=3 -->
[Reserved] 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=3 -->
&sect;52.2975 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=3 -->
Enhanced in-use compliance program for nonroad engines over 37 kw. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(a) General applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) New 1999 model year and later nonroad engines, except those exempted in paragraph (a)(2) of this section, that
are operated in the Los Angeles-South Coast Air Basin, Ventura, or in the Sacramento Metropolitan ozone nonattainment
areas as defined in 40 CFR 81.305 shall meet the requirements specified in paragraphs (c) through (g) of this section,
in paragraph (j) of this section, and in &sect;52.2965. Other state and federal requirements may also apply to these
engines. Owners of nonroad engines of any model year, except those exempted in paragraph (a)(2) of this section, that
are operated in the Los Angeles-South Coast Air Basin, Ventura, or Sacramento Metropolitan ozone nonattainment
areas as defined in 40 CFR 81.305 shall meet the requirements specified in paragraphs (h) and (j) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exempted nonroad engines. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The following nonroad engines are exempted from the requirements of this section: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Engines rated below 37 kw; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Compression-ignition engines used in marine applications that have a rated speed at maximum torque of 1200 RPM
or less; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Spark-ignition engines used in marine applications; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Engines used in aircraft as defined in &sect;87.1(a) of this chapter; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Engines used in underground mining equipment and regulated by the Mining Safety and Health Administration (MSHA)
in 30 CFR parts 7, 31, 32, 36, 56, 70, and 75; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Engines used to propel locomotives, as defined in &sect;85.1602 of this chapter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3)(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Labeling requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(A) For 1999 and later model year nonroad equipment, the equipment manufacturer shall affix a label meeting the requirements
of paragraph (j) of this section to every piece of nonroad equipment operated, stored, or transported in the South
Coast Air Basin, in Ventura County, or in the Sacramento Metropolitan ozone nonattainment areas as defined in 40 CFR
81.305, except those pieces of equipment and associated engines exempted in paragraphs (a)(2) and (a)(3)(ii) of
this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) For 1998 and earlier model year nonroad equipment, effective March 15, 2000, a label meeting the requirements
of paragraph (j) of this section shall be affixed to every piece of nonroad equipment operated, stored, or transported
in the South Coast Air Basin, in Ventura County, or in the Sacramento Metropolitan ozone nonattainment areas as defined
in 40 CFR 81.305, except those pieces of equipment and associated engines exempted in paragraph (a)(2) and (a)(3)(ii)
of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Labeling exceptions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The labeling requirements of paragraph (a)(3)(i) of this section do not apply to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Equipment stored on the premises of an equipment dealer or leaser, unless such location is on or adjacent to a site
at which work is being done that could gainfully employ the equipment; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Equipment transported through or out of the FIP area that is not unloaded from its carrier while in the FIP area.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions and abbreviations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The definitions and abbreviations of &sect;52.2966 and parts 86 and 89 of this chapter, and the definitions contained
in the Clean Air Act apply to this section unless the term is defined in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) Exhaust emission standards. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purposes of certification, assembly line, and recall testing, exhaust emissions from nonroad engines to
which these requirements apply shall not exceed the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-methane hydrocarbons. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
1.2 grams per brake horsepower-hour, as measured under steady-state operating conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Oxides of nitrogen. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) For engines operated in the South Coast Air Basin or in Ventura County: 1.5 grams per brake horsepower-hour, as
measured under steady-state operating conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00473 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(ii) For engines operated in the Sacramento Metropolitan ozone nonattainment areas as defined in 40 CFR 81.305: 2.5
grams per brake horsepower-hour, as measured under steady-state operating conditions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Evaporative emission requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Manufacturers' applications for certification shall include test results or an engineering evaluation demonstrating
compliance with the inherently low evaporative emission requirements of &sect;88.311&hyph;93 (a)(1)(ii) and
(a)(2) of this chapter. Diurnal emission levels shall be adjusted to reflect corresponding results for a nominal
20 gallon fuel tank volume. This demonstration may be based on a diurnal temperature excursion of 65 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F to 105 
<!-- PJG 0040 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F and California certification fuel rather than the EPA conditions and test fuel. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test procedures. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The exhaust standards set forth in paragraph (c) of this section refer to the exhaust emitted over the operating schedule
set forth in the Federal nonroad regulations, and measured and calculated in accordance with the procedures set forth
in the Federal nonroad regulations. Assembly line testing procedures are those set forth in 40 CFR part 86, subpart
K, except as specified in paragraph (f) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Test fuels. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
All certification, assembly line, and recall testing performed as described in paragraph (e) of this section shall
use the fuels provided for by California as found in the California nonroad regulations. Testing performed to demonstrate
compliance with the inherently low evaporative emission requirements of paragraph (d) of this section may, as an
alternative, be conducted with fuels meeting the federal specifications of 40 CFR part 86. Assembly line and recall
testing shall use the same type of fuel as used in certification testing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(g) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recall program. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(1) Engines certified to the standards set forth in paragraphs (c) and (d) of this section shall be subject to the recall
provisions of part 89, subpart H of this chapter and the associated established practices of EPA, except as otherwise
provided in paragraph (g) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) For purposes of the recall testing under this section, the term ``engine'' includes all emissions control systems.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The recall provisions for light-duty vehicles contained in paragraphs (e) (3), (4), and (5) of this section shall
apply to engines subject to the provisions of paragraph (g) of this section as well, with appropriate references to
applicable standards and test procedures, except that: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Engines shall be selected by EPA for the purposes of recall testing from the equipment population of the South Coast,
Ventura, and Sacramento nonattainment areas; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The prohibitions on registering vehicles contained in paragraph (e)(5)(i) of this section shall apply to equipment
used in the South Coast, Ventura, and Sacramento nonattainment areas; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(h) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fleet averaging program. (1) General Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The requirements of this program apply to owners of equipment equipped with a nonroad engine that is operated in the
South Coast Air Basin, in Ventura County, or in the Sacramento Metropolitan ozone nonattainment areas as defined
in 40 CFR 81.305, except those pieces of equipment and associated engines exempted in paragraph (a)(2) of this section.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Effective January 1, 1999, any person who owns one or more pieces of equipment described in paragraph (h)(1) of
this section shall submit the following information on each such piece of equipment to EPA by January 31st of every
calendar year. The submittal shall reflect the owner's affected fleet as it existed on January 1st of the same calendar
year. Owners in the South Coast Air Basin and Ventura County may combine their affected equipment with that of other
equipment owners in the South Coast Air Basin and Ventura County for the purposes of this program.
<FOOTCITE>44</FOOTCITE>
 Required information per affected piece of equipment: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
44
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Owners in the Sacramento ozone nonattainment area may combine their affected equipment with that of other equipment
owners in the Sacramento ozone nonattainment area for the purposes of this program.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) Type of equipment and equipment class as specified in Table 2975&hyph;1; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Engine model year; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Engine serial number; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 certification level (for 1999 and later model year engines only); 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The useful life renewal certificate as described in &sect;52.2965(d) (for 1999 and later model year engines beyond
their original useful life period only); and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Proof that remedial actions have been performed by an authorized party for any engine subject to a recall action
as described in paragraph (g) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
