(5) Within 30 days of receipt of an adequate owner's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submittal, including sufficient payment, EPA shall send a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certificate of compliance to the designated mailing address. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certificate shall indicate the serial numbers of the engines to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which it applies. Inadequate owners' submittals, including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
insufficient payment of fees, shall be returned to the designated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
mailing address, along with an explanation of why the submittal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
was found inadequate, within 30 days of receipt. Resubmittals by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owners shall be responded to by EPA within 30 days of receipt. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) Certificates of compliance shall be valid only through 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
March 1st of the calendar year following the year in which they 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are issued. Expiration dates shall be indicated on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certificates. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) Effective January 1, 2000, no piece of nonroad 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment that is equipped with an engine of model year 1998 or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
earlier, except equipment and associated engines exempted in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (a)(2) of this section, shall be allowed to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registered unless it was included in the 1999 information 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submittal specified in paragraph (h)(2) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(8) Effective January 1, 1999, no piece of nonroad 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment that is equipped with an engine of model year 1999 or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
later, except equipment and associated engines exempted in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (a)(2) of this section, shall be allowed to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registered for use in the FIP areas without proof that it meets 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the enhanced in-use compliance program engine standards of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraphs (c) and (d) of this section. 
