<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Employee commute options program rule (Sacramento). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) Applicability. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 This section applies to all employers in the Sacramento ECO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
program area as defined in paragraph (c) of this section who 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employ 100 or more employees at a work location unless exempted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under the provisions of paragraph (d)(2) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Purpose. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The purpose of this section is to reduce work 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
trips by requiring employers of 100 or more employees to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
implement work trip reduction plans designed to attain an average 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
passenger occupancy (APO) target which is 25% over the average 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
occupancy for all peak period work trips in the area. This 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section will increase the average vehicle occupancy (AVO) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
work-related trips and reduce the number of work-related trips 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and miles traveled. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 For the purposes of this section, the following definitions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall apply: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the Administrator of the U.S. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Environmental Protection Agency or a designated and delegated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
representative. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Average passenger occupancy (APO)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the average 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
passenger occupancy of commuting vehicles arriving at an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employer's work location during the peak travel period. The APO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is equal to the number of employees arriving at the location 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
during the peak travel period divided by the number of vehicles 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in which employees arrive at the same location during the peak 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
travel period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Average passenger occupancy survey (APO survey) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the survey of employees' commute patterns 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
required to be conducted at a work location by employers in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with paragraph (h) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Average vehicle occupancy 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
AVO 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the average occupancy 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of all commuting vehicles arriving at all work locations within 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Sacramento ECO Program Area during the peak travel period.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
  
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Carpool 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a group of two to eight employees commuting to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and from work by means of a vehicle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Clean Air Act 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the Federal Clean Air Act, as amended 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(42 U.S.C. 7401 et seq.) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Commute alternative 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the mode of travel between a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
person's place of residence and place of employment, which is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other than in a motor vehicle occupied by one person. Commute 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
alternatives include, but are not limited to, public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transportation, carpools, vanpools, buspools, ferries, bicycling, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and walking, which may be used independent of or in conjunction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with compressed work week schedules, telecommuting and like 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
measures. For purposes of this section, telecommuting is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered a commuting alternative. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compliance plan 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the specific plan an employer is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
required to submit before March 1, 1997 and subsequently 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
implement demonstrating that the employer will reach the APO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
target before March 1, 1999. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compressed work week 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a schedule in which employees 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
work 35 or more hours in fewer than five work days or more than 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
70 hours in fewer than ten work days. Compressed work week 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
refers to schedules that include but are not limited to: ``4 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
day-40 hour'', ``3 day-36 hour'', 9 day-80 hour'', ``9 day-72 hour'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
schedules, and other work schedules that reduce the number or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
frequency of required commute trips. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Employee 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a partner or limited partner in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
partnership, or any person employed by an employer, in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or contract 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
position, excluding volunteers, who either reports to work or is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
assigned primarily to a work location 80 or more hours per 28-day 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
period for at least two months in any four consecutive months. A 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contract position is one in which the employee reports to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
work location for a period of at least two months and whose work 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hours and assignments are defined by the employer at any time 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
after the effective date of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00481 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Employee transportation coordinator (ETC) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an employee appointed by an employer to develop, implement, monitor, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
market a trip reduction program at a work location as required in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Employer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any person(s), trust, firm, business, joint 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stock company, corporation, partnership, association, non-profit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agency or corporation, educational institution, school district, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hospital or other health care facility, or federal, state, city 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or county government department, agency, or district, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subdivision or instrumentality thereof, or any other special 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purpose public agency or district that employs 100 or more 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employees reporting to a single work location. A city or county 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is a single employer for purposes of this section, not individual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
departments or agencies of the city or county. Individual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
departments or agencies of the State of California and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
federal government are separate employers for the purposes of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Highest ranking responsible officer 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the president, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
executive or managing director, other chief executive or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operating officer, or other highest ranking employee located at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
work location, who has primary responsibility for the operation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and management of that work location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Maintenance plan 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the plan an employer who achieves the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
APO target implements after that date to maintain the APO target 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at the work location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Peak travel period 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the time period between the hours 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of 6 a.m. and 10 a.m. inclusive, Monday through Friday. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plan 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any plan an employer is required to submit to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Administrator in accordance with paragraph (i) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. Specific plans an employer may submit under this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section include initial compliance plans, update plans, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maintenance plans. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Public transportation 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means rail passenger service, motorbus 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regular route service, paratransit service, and motorbus charter 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
service or other transportation services available to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
traveling public whose purpose is to carry passengers between two 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or more locations. Chauffeured limousines and taxi cabs are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered public transportation for purposes of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Sacramento ECO program area 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the Sacramento ozone 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nonattainment area as defined in 40 CFR 81.305. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Telecommuting 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a strategy in which an employee 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
substitutes the location at which work is performed for an entire 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
day. Work otherwise assigned to be done at the work location is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
instead done at the employee's residence. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transportation management association (TMA) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nonprofit organization that coordinates local commuter 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transportation services, including but not limited to public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transportation, vanpools, carpools, bicycling and pedestrian 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
modes, as well as strategies such as alternative work hours; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provides other similar services for corporations, employees, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
developers, individuals, and other groups. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Travel demand management (TDM) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a system of actions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whose purpose is to alleviate traffic-related problems through 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
improved management of vehicle trip demand. Primarily directed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at commuter travel, TDM actions are structured to reduce the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
dependence on and use of single occupant vehicles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Update plan 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the plan submitted by an employer who has 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
not achieved the APO target by March 1, 1999 showing what 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
additional actions the employer will implement to achieve the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
target APO within 1 year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vanpool 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a group of nine to fifteen employees, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
including the driver, commuting to and from their work location 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
using a vehicle that is used and maintained for the primary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purpose of ridesharing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vehicle 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a highway vehicle powered by a gasoline or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
diesel internal combustion engine used for commuting purposes 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the exception of public transportation, vanpools and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
vehicles used to convey disabled persons as described in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (g)(4)(viii) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Work location 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
or 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
location 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means an area, building, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
grouping of buildings in actual physical contact or separated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
only by a private or public roadway or other private or public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
right-of-way that does not represent an impassable barrier to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
bicycle or pedestrian travel located within the Sacramento ECO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Program Area under the ownership, operation, or control of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
same employer. Businesses operated separately and distinctly 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be considered separate work locations even if they are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owned by the same employer and are physically located in the same 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or adjacent buildings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(d) Employer requirements and exemptions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Overview of employer requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This section requires the following seven actions of all subject employers. An employer failing to undertake any
or all of these actions shall be considered in violation of this section and shall be subject to penalties in accordance
with paragraph (l) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Register with the Administrator as an employer subject 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the provisions of this section (paragraph (f) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (ii) Designate an Employee Transportation Coordinator (ETC) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at each work location (paragraph (i) of this section). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Conduct an annual APO survey of employees at each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
work location to determine employees' commute patterns and report 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the results of the survey to the Administrator (paragraph (h) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (iv) Develop and submit to the Administrator by March 1, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1997 and in subsequent years as required by this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance, update, or maintenance plans that describe activities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to be implemented at the location under an employee commute 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
option (ECO) program (paragraph (i) of this section). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Implement the program outlined in the compliance, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
update, or maintenance plan (paragraph (i) of this section). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) No later than March 1, 1999, increase the average 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
passenger occupancy (APO) at each location by not less than 25 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
percent over the average vehicle occupancy (AVO) for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento ECO program area (paragraph (g) of this section). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) Maintain the target APO after achieving it. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00482 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An employer that meets any of the criteria 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
described in paragraph (d)(2) (i) or (ii) of this section may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
apply to the Administrator for an exemption from the requirements 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section. Requests for exemptions shall be made in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
writing and shall be signed by the highest ranking responsible 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
officer at the work location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (i) Any employer that employs 100 or more employees at a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
single work location, but has fewer than 33 employees reporting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to work during the peak travel period may apply to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator for an exemption from the requirements of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (ii) Any employer whose employee population at a work 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location decreases to fewer than 100 employees for a 12 month 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
period, calculated as a monthly average, may apply to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator for an exemption from the requirements of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. The employer must submit documentation demonstrating an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employee population of less than 100. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Employer notification. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 The Administrator will notify employers individually and by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
published notice of the requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (1) Individual notification of employers. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
By May 1, 1995 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or 90 days after final promulgation of this section whichever is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
later, the Administrator shall notify employers known to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject to this section by certified mail of their obligations 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under this section. The notification letter shall outline the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedure for employer registration and be accompanied by a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard registration form described in paragraph (f) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. In each year after the initial notices are mailed, The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator shall send notices to any employer known to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
added to the employer list since the previous notification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
mailing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
General notification of employers. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Not later than May 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1, 1995 or 90 days after final publication of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whichever is later and annually thereafter, the Administrator 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall publish notice and information concerning Sacramento 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employers' obligations under this section. The notice shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provide information on how employers can obtain required forms 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from EPA and shall establish a date by which employers must 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
return a completed form to the Administrator. The Administrator 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall publish the notice beginning on the date of the first 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
individual notification mailings and shall run the notice for at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
least three days over a two week period in Sacramento regional 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
newspapers. Also, the Administrator shall publish the notice in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the first 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 released after the date of the first 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notification mailings. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (3) Failure to receive an individual notification as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provided for in paragraph (e)(1) of this section shall not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
relieve any employer of the obligation to meet all applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Employer registration. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (1) Registration deadlines. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (i) By the due date specified in the notification mailing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and as published in the public notice (see paragraph (e) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section), each employer who received by certified mail the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard registration form shall submit a completed standard 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registration form to the Administrator. Notwithstanding that an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employer may not have been mailed or received notice from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator, an employer is required to complete the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registration form and submit the completed form to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator by the deadline specified in the published notice. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Copies of the registration form may be obtained upon request from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (ii) Any employer that receives a notification packet must 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
respond even if the employer believes it is not subject to this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. An employer that does not meet the definition of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employer under this section is not required to submit the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard registration form, but instead must submit an ECO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
program return card included in the notification packet 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
indicating the reason for non-applicability. The Administrator 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
may request the employer to submit additional documentation to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
verify an employer's non-applicable status. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (iii) An employer who is not subject to this section at the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
time the first notices are mailed, but subsequently becomes an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employer subject to this section, shall submit a registration 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
form to the Administrator within 60 days of becoming subject to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (iv) An employer that moves its work location within the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento ECO program area after registering with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator must submit a new registration form within 60 days 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
after the date of the relocation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (2) Completion and submittal of registration form. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
