<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00483 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 
<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
(i) Each employer who is subject to this section or who 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
receives by certified mail a standard registration form shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
complete a standard registration form for each work location in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Sacramento ECO Program Area. The form must be signed by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
highest ranking responsible officer at the location who shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
attest to the accuracy of the information reported. An employer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall provide the following information on the form: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (A) The name of the employer and address of the work 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (B) The name and telephone of the highest ranking 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
responsible officer at the location; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (C) Designation of the location as a single site, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
headquarters, or branch; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (D) The total number of employees at the location and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
number assigned to report to the work location during the peak 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
travel period; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (E) The name, telephone number, and address (if different 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from that named in paragraphs (f)(2)(i) (A) and (B) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section) of the employee transportation coordinator (ETC) at the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location to receive APO survey and compliance plan forms and who 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will serve as the employer's contact with the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (ii) An employer with more than one location in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Sacramento ECO Program Area shall complete a separate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registration form for each work location, but individual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
registration forms may be submitted together. The employer shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
designate an ETC for EPA to contact at each location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Notwithstanding this provision, an employer may designate a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
single contact person to receive APO survey and compliance plan 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
forms for all work locations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (g) Average Passenger Occupancy (APO) target. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (1) Designation of target APO. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The CAA has established 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
average passenger occupancy (APO) at a work location as the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performance measure for determining an employer's compliance. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The APO performance target is 125 percent of the average vehicle 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
occupancy (AVO) for the Sacramento ECO Program Area. Given a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
baseline AVO of 1.11, the target APO for the Sacramento ECO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Program Area is 1.38. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Deadline for compliance with the target APO. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Not later 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than March 1, 1999, each employer is required to increase the APO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at the employer's work location during the peak travel period to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the target APO. An employer that has achieved the target APO is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
required to maintain the location APO at a level at least as high 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as the target APO, but is not required to increase its APO beyond 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the target APO. Each employer shall annually document 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
achievement of the target APO at each work location through the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
APO survey described in paragraph (h) of this section, and report 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the location's compliance with the target APO to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator in the maintenance plan, as required by paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (h) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Average Passenger Occupancy (APO) survey requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (1) Notice of requirement to survey. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Within 180 days of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
receiving completed registration forms from employers, but not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
later than March 1, 1996, the Administrator shall notify each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employer of the requirement to conduct an APO survey and to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
develop and implement a compliance plan in accordance with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements of paragraph (h)(1)(i) of this section. The notice 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall include copies of the required APO survey and compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
plan forms. Failure of an employer to receive such notification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall not relieve any employer of the obligation to comply with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
all applicable obligations of this section. Employers not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
receiving such forms may request them from EPA by contacting the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Region IX office. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirement to survey. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
For the purpose of documenting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the work location APO, each employer shall conduct annual APO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surveys of the commute patterns of the employees who arrive at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
its work location during the peak travel period. An employer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with more than one location in the Sacramento ECO Program Area 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall conduct a survey at each location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Survey procedure. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An employer shall conduct an APO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
survey of all employees assigned to report to the work location 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
during the peak travel period using the following procedure, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
except as provided in paragraph (h)(3)(iii) of this section: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (i) Except as provided below, an employer shall use the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard APO survey form provided by the EPA. The APO survey 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
form is designed to collect information on the commute patterns 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of employees and to allow the employer to calculate the work 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location APO as described in this paragraph. The standard form 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be used without alteration. If the employer's individual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
survey form has been submitted to and approved by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator prior to administration of the survey, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator may permit the employer to use this pre-approved 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
form as a substitute for the standard APO survey form. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator shall not approve any survey form that could be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
expected, in the Administrator's judgement, to produce different 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
survey results than if the standard form had been used. An 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
employer is permitted to attach additional survey forms to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard form if desired, without prior approval of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (ii) Employers shall choose a typical week in which to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conduct the APO survey. A week shall not be considered typical 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
if it: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (A) Includes a holiday observed by the employer; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (B) Immediately follows a week in which a holiday was 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
observed on Friday or precedes a week in which a holiday will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
observed on Monday; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (C) Is a week during which the employer holds a rideshare 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fair or other intensive information promotion related to the ECO 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
program; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
