<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(ii) Calculation of location APO shall count employees arriving at the location during the peak travel periods, Monday
through Friday of the survey week as follows: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Each employee that arrives at the location during the peak travel period shall be counted as one employee arriving
for each of the days Monday through Friday of the survey week that the employee reports to the location, regardless
of the length of time the employee remains at the location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Each employee that telecommutes all day from the employee's home shall be counted as one employee arriving for
each day the employee telecommutes. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Each employee that works a compressed work week shall be counted as one employee arriving for each day the employee
works and for each compressed work week day off. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) For calculation of APO, the count of vehicles arriving shall include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Passenger cars and trucks, with fewer than nine employees; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Motorcycles and mopeds. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The following shall be counted as zero vehicles arriving: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Vanpools with nine or more employees; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Public or private buses, trains, or other mass transportation vehicles and; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) Bicycles and other non-motorized vehicles. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) An employee that works a compressed work week or telecommutes the entire day at home shall be counted as arriving
at the work location in a zero vehicle on the day he or she does not report to the work location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) An employee that is dropped off at the work location by another employee or employees commuting to their work location
or locations shall be counted as arriving in a share of a vehicle proportional to the number of occupants in the vehicle.
An employee that is dropped off at the work location by a person not traveling to his or her work location shall be counted
as arriving in a single occupant vehicle. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) An employee that commutes in a commute alternative for 50 percent or more of the total length of his or her work
trip or in a commute alternative for 10 or more one-way miles, whichever is less, shall be counted as arriving in that
commute alternative in the APO calculation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) An employer shall not count employees who have disabilities which require the use of a single-occupant vehicle
(or a chauffeured vehicle) for commuting or their vehicles in the APO calculation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ix) An employee that does not respond to the APO survey as described in paragraph (h)(3)(iv) of this section shall
be considered for purposes of the APO calculation to have arrived at the work location in a single-occupant vehicle
and be counted as one employee arriving in one vehicle, unless the response rate of the survey is 90 percent or above.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reporting of APO survey results
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. An employer shall tabulate the APO survey results and report the results to the Administrator on a standard form provided
by the EPA. An employer shall submit the APO survey results as a component of the compliance plan in accordance with
paragraph (i) of this section. In years in which the employer is required to document and provide its work location
APO to the Administrator but is not required to submit a plan, survey results shall be submitted as an APO survey report.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Required components of APO survey reports
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. A complete APO survey report submittal will consist of the following elements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Completed APO survey report, prepared on standard forms provided by the EPA; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) A letter signed by the highest ranking responsible officer at the work location or report preparer, if different
from the employer, who attests to the accuracy of the information included in the report. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Compliance, update, and maintenance plans. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Requirements
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Each employer shall prepare and implement compliance, update, or maintenance plans in accordance with the procedures
and schedules established in this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plan submittal schedule
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Each employer shall submit compliance, update, or maintenance plans, as described in paragraph (i)(3) and (4) of
this section respectively, to the Administrator in accordance with the following schedule. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Not later than March 1, 1997, each employer shall prepare and submit to the Administrator a compliance plan for
each work location. An employer that becomes subject to this section after March 1, 1997 shall be given a minimum of
180 days from the date it registers with the Administrator, as required by paragraph (f) of this section, to prepare
and submit a compliance plan. This employer further shall not be required to demonstrate achievement of the target
APO until two years following submittal of the compliance plan. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Not later than March 1, 1999, each employer who has not achieved the target APO shall prepare and submit to the Administrator
an update plan for each work location as described in paragraph (i)(4) of this section. An employer that fails to meet
the target APO by March 1, 1999 shall be subject to the penalty for failure to reach the target APO as of March 1, 1999.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Not later than March 1, 1999, each employer who has achieved the target APO shall prepare and submit to the Administrator
a maintenance plan. If an employer determines that no additional measures are needed to maintain the APO target, the
original compliance plan may be referenced to meet this requirement. Additional update plans demonstrating achievement
and maintenance of the target APO may be required later if an employer is not in compliance with the target APO. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) An employer that moves its work location within the Sacramento ECO Program Area, desires to modify the elements
of its compliance plan, or experiences a change in its work location operations that could reasonably be expected
to affect the appropriateness or effectiveness of an approved compliance, update, or maintenance plan, shall submit
a revised plan within 90 days of the change. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00486 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Components of a plan. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) An employer shall prepare a plan using a standard plan form developed by the EPA. The plan will include all information
required by the standard plan form, including the following information: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The name of the employer, address of the work location, and name, title, and signature of the Employee Transportation
Coordinator (ETC) at the work location appointed by the employer; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) The results of the most recent APO survey and a description of the procedure used to conduct the APO survey; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) A description of the physical and transportation service characteristics of the work location, and demographic,
work, and travel-related characteristics of the employee population; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) A description of ECO strategies currently implemented that provide commute alternative incentives to employees
at the work location and additional ECO strategies the employer will implement at the work location; an employer desiring
advice and suggestions on ECO strategies should refer to resource materials provided by the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) Activities planned by the employer to implement the ECO program and a time schedule for implementation of the program;

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) A description of the process by which the employer will periodically monitor and review progress toward the APO
target. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Each employer shall provide information included in paragraphs (i)(3)(i) (A) through (F) of this section in
the compliance plan to establish a baseline against which future years can be compared. Beginning with the 1999&hyph;2000
update plan and for any subsequent update plan, an employer that has not achieved the target APO shall update any changes
to the information under paragraphs (i)(3)(i) (A) through (F) of this section and provide the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) A discussion of the employer's ``good faith efforts'', described in paragraph (k)(4) of this section, to achieve
the target APO; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) An explanation of why the ECO strategies included in the last plan did not produce the target APO; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) A discussion of how the employer plans to achieve the APO target within one year. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Required additional elements of plan submittals.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A complete compliance plan submittal to the Administrator shall include of the following additional elements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) An executive summary plan that shall consist of a cover sheet that includes information described in paragraphs
(i)(3)(i) (A) and (B) of this section, and a summary of information described in paragraphs (i)(3)(i) (C) through
(F) of this section, and paragraph (i)(3)(ii) of this section as appropriate; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) A letter signed by the highest ranking responsible officer at the work location who shall attest that the employer
will implement the plan as described, retain all ECO documents on file, as required by paragraph (i)(7) of this section,
and make such documents available for review by the Administrator or an agent designated by the Administrator; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) A letter signed by the highest ranking responsible officer at the work location or plan preparer, if different
from the employer, who shall attest to the correctness of the information included in the plan. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Alternative plan preparers.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 An employer may contract with a transportation planning consultant, TMA or outside entity to prepare or assist in
preparation of a compliance plan or report. The use of an outside entity for this purpose shall not, however, remove
or reduce the responsibility of the employer with regard to any of the requirements of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirement for an ETC.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 An employer shall designate an employee transportation coordinator (ETC) at each work location with 100 or more employees
to administer the ECO program at that work location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Document recordkeeping.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 An employer shall maintain copies of all documents prepared or used in the document preparation by the employer or
by other entities acting on behalf of the employer in accordance with this section in the office of the ETC for a period
not less than four years from the date the documents were first generated. These documents shall include, but not be
limited to documents related to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Conduct of the APO survey; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Calculation of work location APO; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Preparation of compliance, update, and maintenance plans and APO survey reports; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Program implementation, including all organizational policies and procedures; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00487 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(v) Program monitoring and evaluation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(j) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plan certification.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Prior to submittal to the Administrator, plans shall be certified as to completeness. Notwithstanding this provision,
an employer that submits a revised or maintenance plan in accordance with paragraph (i)(2)(iv) or paragraph (k)(1)
of this section shall not be required to have the plan certified prior to its submittal to the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plan Certifiers.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The Administrator shall designate an organization or organizations as plan certifiers for the Sacramento ECO program
area. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The Administrator will provide the Air Districts in the Sacramento ECO area with the first opportunity to become
designated certifiers for employer plans for employers in the geographic areas for their jurisdiction. In addition
to certifying plans for completeness, the Air Districts may provide, if they so choose, a recommendation regarding
the approvability of plans. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Should any or all of the Air Districts in the Sacramento area decline the opportunity to become designated certifiers,
the Administrator will designate another organization or organizations to certify plans. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plan certification criteria.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 In assessing whether a plan can be certified, the certifier shall consider the following criteria: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The completeness of the plan based on the presence of all required components of plan submittals as described in
paragraphs (i)(3) and (4) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The accuracy of the work location APO computation; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Consistency with this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Certification procedures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (i) A certifier shall review the plan utilizing EPA approved training and the criteria described in paragraph (j)(2)
of this section. The certifier may contact the employer to clarify questions related to the plan or to request reasonable
additional documentation from the employer. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) If the certifier deems the plan to meet the certification criteria, the certifier shall certify the plan and return
it to the employer for submittal to the Administrator. Plans not meeting the certification criteria shall be returned
to the employer with an explanation of the reasons the plan was returned, indication of the sections of the plan that
are unacceptable, and an indication of where corrections are necessary in order to make the plan meet certification
requirements. The employer shall revise its plan as appropriate and re-submit the revised plan to the certifying
agency. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) It is the responsibility of an employer to allow adequate time for certification. Failure of the certifier to
certify the employer's plan in time to allow submittal of the plan to the Administrator prior to the deadline shall
not excuse the employer from this obligation. Notwithstanding this provision, however, an employer that submits
a certifiable plan to a certifier at least 90 days prior to the plan submittal deadline shall not be considered in violation
of the plan submittal deadline until 60 days after the scheduled submittal date to the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(k) Plan review and approval. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Plan review and approval schedule. The Administrator will strive to approve or disapprove plans within 90 days
of receipt of a plan. An employer whose plan is returned shall have 60 days from the date of return to revise and resubmit
the plan to the Administrator. The employer shall not be required to have the plan recertified prior to re-submittal
to the Administrator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Plan review guidelines. The Administrator shall review and approve plans based on the following criteria: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The presence of all required plan sections and minimum plan requirements, as described in paragraph (i) of this
section; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The accuracy of the APO calculation, in accordance with the formula provided in paragraph (h) of this section;
and, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) A demonstration of plan certification, in accordance with the procedures defined in paragraph (j) of this section.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The appropriateness of the commute alternatives proposed in the plan to the location and employee population;

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The appropriateness of the ECO program services and incentives selected by the employer to the commute alternatives;

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) The likely effectiveness of the ECO strategies in producing the target APO by the scheduled deadline; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) The ability of the proposed implementation schedule to ensure ECO strategies included in the plan are implemented
in a timely and thorough manner; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) The ability of the proposed monitoring process to allow a timely and effective review of the employer's progress
toward the target APO. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(l) Enforcement and penalties. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Noncompliance.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 An employer shall be subject to civil or criminal penalties according to 42 U.S.C. 7413 (section 113 of the Clean Air
Act) for violations of any provisions of this section. Upon determining that a violation has occurred, the Administrator
shall issue the employer a notice of violation. Penalties for continued noncompliance may accrue from the date of
the notice of violation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Penalties.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The Administrator may assess civil penalties of up to $25,000 per day of violation. Penalties under this section will
be assessed according to criteria in 42 U.S.C. 7413(e). These criteria include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (i) The size of the business; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The economic impact of the penalty on the business; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The violator's compliance history and good faith efforts to comply; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The duration of the violation; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Prior payment of penalties for similar violations; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) The economic benefit of noncompliance; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) The seriousness of the violation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Work location audits.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 To verify implementation of work location programs, the Administrator shall have the authority to conduct or cause
to be conducted audits of an employer's location. The employer shall provide the Administrator access to all records
pertaining to the development, implementation, and administration of the ECO program described in the employer's
plan, and access to employees at the location. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Good faith effort.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 A good faith effort will be taken into account when penalties are determined. The Administrator may consider any or
all of the following criteria in assessing an employer's good faith effort: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Did management at the location demonstrate significant commitment to implementation of the program and institute
written employee policies that encouraged the use of commute alternatives?; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Did the employer assess the transportation needs and interests of employees through employee surveys or other
techniques?; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Did the employer periodically review its progress toward the target APO, at a minimum through conduct of an APO
survey of its employees in the second program year (1996&hyph;1997), and through other actions designed to assess
the continuing appropriateness of the employer's ECO program services and incentives?; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) If the employer's 1997&hyph;1998 APO survey showed the APO increase was less than 50 percent of that needed to
achieve the target APO, did the employer increase and or modify its program to include appropriate contingency strategies?;

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Did the employer seek advice from the EPA, a TMA, a transportation consultant, or other entity with TDM experience,
prior to September 1, 1998, regarding desirable future actions to increase APO?; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00488 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(vi) Did the employer have strategies like those known to be implemented by others like it?; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) Did the APO at the work location increase a reasonable amount compared to other employers with similar work location
characteristics and employee populations? 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(m) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Extensions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Deadline extensions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 An employer that, for reasons beyond its control, is unable to meet a deadline established in this section may petition
the Administrator for an extension of the deadline. All requests shall be submitted in writing and signed by the highest
ranking responsible officer at the site. The Administrator will strive to rule on extensions of scheduled deadlines
within 30 days from receipt of the request. Extensions may be considered for hardship circumstances or other unusual
circumstances that may make it impossible to meet the deadlines established in this section. Requests for deadline
extensions must be filed in the following manner. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) A request for an extension of the deadline to register as an employer shall be submitted not less than 45 days in advance
of the deadline for registration. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) A request for extension of the deadline to submit a plan or APO survey report shall be submitted not less than 90
days in advance of the deadline. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;52.3000 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
General permit requirements (Sacramento). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Purpose.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 This section provides an orderly procedure for the review of new sources of air pollution and the orderly review of
the modification of existing sources through the issuance of permits. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Definitions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 When used in this section, &sect;52.3001, New Source Review, and &sect;52.3002, Emissions Reduction Credit Authorization,
the following terms have the meanings given below. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Actual emissions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means measured, or estimated if measurement is not possible, emissions which most accurately represent the emissions
from an emissions unit. Fugitive emissions associated with the emissions unit shall be included in the actual emissions
of the emissions unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Actual emissions reductions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means reductions of emissions from an emissions unit. Actual emission reductions shall be calculated pursuant to
paragraphs (d)(12) and (13) of &sect;52.3001, New Source Review, and authorized pursuant to section &sect;52.3002,
Emissions Reduction Credit Authorization, and shall meet all of the following criteria: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The emissions reductions shall be real, enforceable, quantifiable, and permanent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) The emissions reductions shall be surplus emissions reductions in excess of any emissions reduction which is:

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Required or encumbered by any laws, rules, regulations, agreements, or orders; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Attributed to a control measure noticed for workshop in the district, or proposed or contained in a State Implementation
Plan or Federal Implementation Plan; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Proposed or contained in the district air quality attainment plan for attaining the annual reductions required
by the Clean Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Emission reductions attributed to a proposed control measure contained in the District Air Quality Attainment
Plan (AQAP) may be re-eligible as an offset emission reduction only if such measure has been removed from the AQAP during
the next AQAP update. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Source shutdowns and curtailments may not be given emission reduction credit in the case of non-attainment pollutants,
including precursors, if the shutdown or curtailment occurred prior to the date of application unless: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The crediting of shutdown emissions complies with the most recent emission trading policy of the EPA, and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The proposed new source or modification is a replacement, and the shutdown or curtailment occurred after August
7, 1977, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The shutdown or curtailment was claimed by the affected facility as a credit within 180 days of the last date of
operation, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The district has met statutory planning mandates and air quality improvement milestones. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Actual interruptions of electrical power
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means when electrical service is interrupted by an unforeseeable event. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Actual operating days
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any day of operation which results in the emission of an affected pollutant from the emissions unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Administrative permit amendment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an amendment to an Authority to Construct which: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Corrects a typographical error; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00489 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(2) Identifies a minor administrative change at the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stationary source; for example, a change in the name, address, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
phone number of any person identified in the permit; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Requires more frequent monitoring or reporting by a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
responsible official of the stationary source; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Transfers ownership or operational control of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stationary source, provided that, prior to the transfer, the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
receives a written agreement which specifies a date for the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transfer of permit responsibility, coverage, and liability from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the current to the prospective permittee. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Ambient air quality standards
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means state and federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ambient air quality standards for the purpose of submittal to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA for inclusion in the California State Implementation Plan. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
All references in this section, &sect;52.3001, and &sect;52.3002 to ambient 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air quality standards shall be interpreted as National Ambient 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Air Quality Standards. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicable requirements
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means air quality requirements with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which a facility must comply pursuant to the State Implementation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Plan, the Federal Clean Air Act as amended in 1990 and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
implementing regulations, other provisions of the United States 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Code, and the Code of Federal Regulations. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Authority to construct
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a preconstruction permit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authorizing construction prior to the start of construction and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conforming to the requirements of &sect;52.3001, New Source Review. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Authorized
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means emission reduction credits (ERCs) which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
have been evaluated by the EPA to verify that they are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
quantifiable, enforceable, permanent and surplus at the time of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
use. Authorization of the ERCs must occur both prior to approval 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of, and concurrent with, the application for use of the ERCs as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
offsets pursuant to &sect;52.3001, New Source Review. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Banking 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the system of quantifying, adjusting, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certifying, recording, and storing ERCs for future use and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transfer. Procedures for banking ERCs are described in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable district banking rules. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Begin actual construction
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means initiation of physical, on-site construction activities on an emissions unit which are of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanent nature. Such activities include, but are not limited 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to, installation of building supports and foundations, laying of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
underground pipework, and construction of permanent storage 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
structures. With respect to a change in the method of operation, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this term refers to those on-site activities other than 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
preparatory activities which mark the initiation of the change. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Best available control technology (BACT)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) For any emissions unit, an emission limit based on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
most stringent of the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The most effective emission control device, emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limit, or technique, singly or in combination, which has been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
required or used for the type of equipment comprising such an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit unless the applicant demonstrates to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
satisfaction of the EPA that such limitations required on other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sources have not been demonstrated to be achievable. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any alternative basic equipment, fuel, process, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission control device or technique, singly or in combination, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determined to be technologically feasible and cost-effective by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00490 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(iii) For replacement equipment only, the emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitation that is based on the maximum degree of reduction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
achievable, taking into account environmental, energy, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
economic impacts by each class or category of source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) In making a BACT determination for a nonattainment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollutant, the EPA may consider the overall effect on other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nonattainment pollutants. In some cases the lowest emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rates may be required for one or more nonattainment pollutants at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the cost of not achieving the lowest emission rate for other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
nonattainment pollutants. The EPA shall discuss these 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considerations in the Preliminary Decision prepared pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the provisions of &sect;52.3001(d)(3). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Under no circumstances shall BACT be determined to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
less stringent than the emission control required by an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable provision of district, state or federal laws or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regulations unless the applicant demonstrates to the satisfaction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the EPA that such limitations are not achievable. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Best available retrofit control technology (BARCT)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission limitation that is based upon the maximum degree of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction achievable, taking into account environmental, energy, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and economic impacts by each class or category of source. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
criteria for BARCT are specified in ``California Clean Air Act 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Guidance for the Determination of Reasonably Available Control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Technology and Best Available Retrofit Control Technology,'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California Air Resources Board, April 1990. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
California Environmental Quality Act (CEQA)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California Environmental Quality Act, Public Resources Code, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Section 21000, et seq. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cargo carriers
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means trains dedicated to a specific source 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and marine vessels while docked at a specific source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Certified
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means emission reduction credits which have been 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
evaluated under the requirements of a district banking rule. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Commence 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means that the owner or operator has all of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
necessary permits or approvals required under state and federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air quality control laws, district rules and regulations, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
those air quality control laws and regulations which are part of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the California State Implementation Plan or any applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Federal Implementation Plan, and has: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Begun, or caused to begin, a continuous program of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on-site construction of the source, to be completed in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable time; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Entered into binding agreements or contractual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
obligations which cannot be cancelled or modified without 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
substantial loss to the owner or operator, to undertake a program 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of actual construction of the source to be completed within a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable time. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Complete application
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an application for an Authority 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to Construct a new or modified emission unit that, on the basis 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the criteria of 40 CFR part 70.5(c) of the Federal Operating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Permit Program and the applicable requirements of this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contains adequate information for the EPA to evaluate the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application for compliance with the applicable requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section. Such determination shall be made after receipt of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
payment of an application filing fee, as determined by the EPA, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that reflects the costs to the EPA to review the application and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
issue permits. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Construction
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any physical change or change in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
method of operation (including fabrication, erection, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
installation, demolition, or modification of an emissions unit) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which would result in a change in actual emissions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Contiguous property
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means two or more parcels of land with a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
common boundary or separated solely by a public roadway or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
public right-of-way. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cost-effective
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a cost per unit of emissions reduction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which is lower than or equivalent to the maximum unit costs, for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the regulated pollutant or source category, of the same emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction through the use of Best Available Control Technology, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calculated in current year dollars in accordance with methodology 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and criteria specified in the EPA OAQPS Control Cost Manual (EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
450/3&hyph;90&hyph;006). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
District
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the local air pollution permitting agency 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with jurisdiction within the area in which this section applies. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
``District'' may also refer to the geographic area in which the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
local permitting agency has jurisdiction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission decrease
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any modification which would result 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in a decrease of actual emissions. The emission decrease shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be calculated by subtracting the proposed emissions from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
historic actual emissions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emission reduction credits (ERC)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means reductions of actual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions from an emission unit that are registered with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
district in accordance with the requirements of a district 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
banking rule. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emissions limitation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means one or a combination of permit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions specific to an emissions unit which restricts its 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maximum emissions, at or below the emissions associated with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maximum design capacity. An emissions limitation shall be: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Contained in the latest Authority to Construct and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contained in or enforceable by the latest district or federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permit to operate for the emission unit; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Enforceable on a daily basis or quarterly basis 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to provisions of &sect;52.3001(d)(7)(ii). Emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitations should be stated in a manner consistent with testing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedures. Emission limitations may be expressed as enforceable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
design, operational, or equipment standard pursuant to provisions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of &sect;52.3001(d)(7)(iii); and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) No less stringent that the applicable emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standards given at 40 CFR part 60, Standards of Performance for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
New Stationary Sources, and 40 CFR part 61, National Emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Standards for Hazardous Air Pollutants. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emissions unit
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an identifiable operation or piece of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
process equipment such as an article, machine, or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contrivance which controls, emits, may emit, or results in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions of any regulated air pollutant or hazardous air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollutant (HAP), directly or as fugitive emissions. An emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unit shall not include the open burning of agricultural biomass. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Enforceable
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means verifiable and legally binding. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Enforceable, for the purposes of federal requirements, means all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
federally enforceable limitations and conditions enforceable by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA, including NSPS; NESHAP; requirements within any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable State Implementation Plan; any permit requirement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
established pursuant to 40 CFR 52.21, 40 CFR 51.160 through 166, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or 40 CFR 70. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
EPA
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an official of the U.S. Environmental Protection 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Agency, or his or her authorized representative. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00491 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
ERC certificate 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a document identifying the quantity 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and type of ERCs issued by the district pursuant to a banking 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rule to the source identified on the Certificate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fugitive emissions 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means those emissions which could not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonably pass through a stack, chimney, vent, or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
functionally equivalent opening. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Halogenated hydrocarbons 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the following: 1,1,1-trichloroethane, methylene chloride, 2,2-dichloro-1,1,1-trifluoroethane (HCFC-123),
2-chloro-1,1,1,2-tetrafluoroethane (HCFC-124), trichlorofluoromethane (CFC-11), dichlorodifluoromethane
(CFC-12), 1,1,1-trichloro-2,2,2-trifluoroethane (CFC-113), 1-chloro-1,1-difluoro-2-chloro-2,2-difluoroethane
(CFC-114), chloropentafluoroethane (CFC-115), pentafluoroethane (HFC-125), 1,1,2,2-tetrafluoroethane (HFC-134),
tetrafluoroethane (HFC-134a), 1,1-dichloro-1-fluoroethane (HCFC-141b), 1-chloro-1,1-difluoroethane (HCFC-142b),
1,1,1-trifluoroethane (HFC-143a), chlorodifluoromethane (HCFC-22), trifluoromethane (HFC-23), 1,1-difluoroethane
(HFC-152a), and the following four classes of perfluorocarbon compounds: Cyclic, branched, or linear, completely
fluorinated alkanes; cyclic, branched, or linear, completely fluorinated ethers, with no unsaturations; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cyclic, branched, or linear, completely fluorinated tertiary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
amines with no unsaturations; and sulfur-containing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
perfluorocarbons with no unsaturations and with sulfur bonds only 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to carbon and fluorine. Perfluorocarbon compounds will be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
assumed to be absent from a product or process unless a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturer or facility operator identifies the specific 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
individual compounds (from the broad classes of perfluorocarbon 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compounds) and the amounts present in the product or process and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provides a validated test method which can be used to quantify 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the specific compounds.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG QTAG 02 -->
<!-- PJG /QTAG -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Hazardous air pollutant (HAP) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any air pollutant listed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to section 112(b) of the Clean Air Act as amended (42 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
U.S.C. 7401 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
et seq.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Historic actual emissions 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The actual emissions for the existing emissions unit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
averaged over the consecutive two-year period immediately 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
preceding the date of application for authorized emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction credits. If the last two years are unrepresentative of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
normal source operations as determined by the EPA, then any two 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
consecutive years of the last five years that represent normal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source operation may be used. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) If, at any time during the two-year period, actual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions exceeded the allowed or permitted emission levels, then 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
actual emissions shall be reduced to reflect emission levels that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
would have occurred if the unit were in compliance with all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable limitations and rules. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Where an emissions unit has been in operation for less 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than two years, a shorter averaging period of at least one year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
may be used, provided that the averaging period is representative 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the full operational history of the emissions unit. If an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit has been in operation for less than one year, then 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the historic actual emissions shall be zero. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Historic potential emissions 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means emissions based on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
potential to emit of the emissions unit prior to modification. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
In determining the potential to emit, daily emissions limitations 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be treated as part of an emissions unit's design only if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the limitations are representative of normal operations, of in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the facility has provided offsets form previous permitting 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
actions. If there are no enforceable limiting conditions, an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit's potential to emit shall be limited to the unit's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
historic actual emissions. For a new emissions unit, historic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
potential emissions are equal to zero. For the purposes of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
above determination, ``normal operations'' is defined as the usual 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or typical daily operating of an emissions unit resulting in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
actual emissions which are at least 80% of the specific limits 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contained in the emission unit's authority to construct or permit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to operate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Lake Tahoe air basin 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means that portion of Placer County 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
within the drainage area naturally tributary to Lake Tahoe 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
including said lake, plus that area in the vicinity of the head 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the Truckee River described as follows (as established 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to section 39606 of the Health and Safety Code of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
State of California and as described in Title 17, California Code 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of Regulations, section 60113 [b]): Commencing at the point 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
common to the aforementioned drainage area crestline and the line 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
common to Townships 15 North and 16 North, Mount Diablo Base and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Meridian (M.D.B. &amp; M.), and following that line in a westerly 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
direction to the northwest corner of section 3, Township 15 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
North, Range 16 East, (M.D.B. &amp; M.), thence south along the west 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
line of Sections 3 and 10, Township 15 North, Range 16 East, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
M.D.B. &amp; M., to the intersection with the drainage crestline, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
thence following the said drainage area boundary in a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
southwesterly, then northeasterly, direction to and along the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Lake Tahoe Dam, thence following the said drainage area crestline 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in a northeasterly, then northwesterly, direction to the point of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
beginning. This Lake Tahoe Air Basin is delineated on an official 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
map on file at the California Air Resources Board Headquarters 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Office. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major stationary source 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any stationary source which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emits or has the potential to emit 25 tons per year or more of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 or 25 tons per year or more of ROC. In addition, any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
physical change occurring at a stationary source not otherwise 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
qualifying as a major stationary source, which would constitute a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
major stationary source by itself makes the source a major 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stationary source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Major modification 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a modification to a major 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stationary source which, when aggregated with all other increases 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in potential to emit over the period of five consecutive years 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
before the application for modification, and including the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calendar year of the most recent application, results in an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
increase in the potential to emit greater than 25 tons per year 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 or 25 tons per year of ROC. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Modification 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any physical change, change in method of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation (including change in fuel characteristics), change in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hours of operation, or change in production rate, which: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) For an emissions unit: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Would necessitate a change in permit conditions; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00492 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(ii) Is not specifically limited by a permit condition; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Results in an increase, a decrease, or no change in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions which are not subject to an emissions limitation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) For a stationary source: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Is a modification of its emissions unit; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Is an addition of any new emissions unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The following shall not be considered a modification: a change 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in ownership; routine maintenance and repair; a reconstructed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stationary source or emissions unit which shall be treated as a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
new stationary source or emissions unit, not as a modification; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and the addition of a continuous emission monitoring system. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Mountain Counties air basin 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means (as established pursuant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to Section 39606 of the Health and Safety Code of the State of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California and as described in Title 17, California Code of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Regulations, section 60111 [i]), all of Placer County except that 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
portion included in the Lake Tahoe Air Basin, defined by 17 CCR 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
60113(b), and that portion included in the Sacramento Valley Air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Basin, defined by 17 CCR 60106(k). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-permitted emissions 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means those emissions of an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regulated pollutant which are not required to obtain a permit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to this section. Non-permitted emissions may include 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions from mobile sources, indirect sources, and exempt 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Nonattainment pollutant 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means any pollutant and its 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
precursors that have been designated ``nonattainment'' by the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in the 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Offset 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the use of an emission reduction credit to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compensate for an emission increase of an regulated pollutant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from a new or modified source subject to the requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.3001, New Source Review. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Permanent 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means only permanent reductions in emissions can 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be authorized as emission reduction credit. For stationary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sources, permanence shall be assured for sources subject to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
federal requirements through federally enforceable changes in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source permits. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
PM
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=4 -->
10
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means particulate matter with an aerodynamic diameter 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
smaller than or equal to a nominal 10 microns as measured by an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable reference test method or methods found acceptable by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Portable equipment 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means equipment which is periodically 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
relocated and is not operated more than a total of 180 days at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any one location in the district within any continuous 12-month 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
period. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Potential to emit 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the maximum daily physical and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operational design capacity to emit an air pollutant during each 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
calendar quarter. Any limitation on the physical or operational 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
design capacity, including emission control devices and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
restrictions on hours of operation, or on the type or amount of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
material combusted, stored, or processed, may be considered as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
part of the design only if the limitation, or the effect it would 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
have on emissions, is incorporated into the Authority to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Construct as an enforceable permit condition as daily emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitations. Fugitive emissions associated with the emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unit or stationary source shall be included in the potential to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emit of the emissions unit or stationary source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Precursor 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means a pollutant that, when emitted into the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
atmosphere, may undergo either a chemical or physical change 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which then produces another pollutant for which an ambient air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
quality standard has been adopted, or whose presence in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
atmosphere will contribute to the violation of one or more 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ambient air quality standards. The following precursor-secondary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air contaminant relationships shall be used for the purposes of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section, &sect;52.3001 and &sect;52.3002: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<TABLE>

<!-- PJG tableformat 2,L2,tp0,i1,s25,r25 -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=95 g=1 f=1 -->
&blank;
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 007 0150 intable -->
1Precursor 
<!-- PJG 007 0150 intable -->
1Secondary air contaminant
<!-- PJG 007 0152 intable -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=1 f=1 -->
Reactive organic compound 
<!-- PJG 007 0104 intable -->
(1) Photochemical oxidants 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (ozone).
<!-- PJG 007 0120 intable -->
(2) Organic fraction of PM
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=5 f=2 -->
10
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=1 f=1 -->
.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Nitrogen oxides 
<!-- PJG 007 0104 intable -->
(1) Nitrogen dioxide. 
<!-- PJG 007 0120 intable -->
(2) Nitrate fraction of PM
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=5 f=2 -->
10
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=01 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 007 0120 intable -->
(3) Photochemical oxidants (ozone).
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</TABLE>

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00493 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Proposed emissions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means emissions based on the potential to emit for the new or modified emissions unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quantifiable
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the ability to estimate emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions in terms of both their amount and characteristics. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The same method of estimating emissions shall be used to quantify 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the emission levels before and after the reduction. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quarterly
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means calendar quarters beginning in January, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
April, July, and October. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Quarterly emissions limitation
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means one or a combination of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permit conditions specific to an emissions unit which restricts 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
its maximum emissions, in pounds per quarter, at or below the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions associated with the maximum design capacity. A 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
quarterly emissions limitation must be: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Contained in the latest Authority to Construct and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contained in or enforceable by the latest Permit to Operate for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the emission unit; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Enforceable on a quarterly basis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reactive organic compound
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any compound containing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
carbon except methane, carbon monoxide, carbon dioxide, carbonic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
acid, metallic carbides or carbonates, ammonium carbonates, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
halogenated hydrocarbons. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Real
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means actually occurring, implemented, and not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
artificially devised. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reasonably available control technology (RACT)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lowest emission limitation that a particular source is capable of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
meeting by the application of emission control technology that is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonably available considering technical and economic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
feasibility. The criteria for RACT are specified in ``California 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Clean Air Act Guidance for the Determination of Reasonably 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Available Control Technology and Best Available Retrofit Control 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Technology,'' California Air Resources Board, April 1990 and in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the General Preamble to Title I, April 16, 1992.
<FOOTCITE>45</FOOTCITE>

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<FOOTNOTE>
<FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
45
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

</FOOTNAME>
<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
Proposed rule published in the 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=4 -->
Federal Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=28 g=1 f=1 -->
 of April 16, 1992 (57 FR 13498).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
</FOOTNOTE>

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Reconstructed source
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any stationary source or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit undergoing physical modification where the fixed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capital cost of the new components exceeds 50% of the fixed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
capital cost of a comparable, entirely new stationary source or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit. Fixed capital cost means the capital that is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
needed to provide all the depreciable components. A 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reconstructed source shall be treated as a new stationary source 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or emissions unit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Register
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means a document maintained pursuant to a district 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
banking rule which records all ERC deposits, withdrawals, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transfers, and transactions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Regulated air pollutant
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any pollutant that is emitted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
into or otherwise enters the ambient air, and for which the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
has adopted an emission limit, standard, or other requirement. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Regulated air pollutants include: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Oxides of nitrogen and volatile organic compounds; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Any pollutant for which a national ambient air quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard has been promulgated pursuant to section 109 of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Clean Air Act; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Any pollutant subject to a new source performance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
standard promulgated pursuant to section 111 of the Clean Air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Act; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Any ozone-depleting substance specified as a Class I 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(chlorofluorocarbons) or Class II (hydrofluorocarbons) substance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to Title VI of the Clean Air Act; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) Any pollutant subject to a standard or requirement 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
promulgated pursuant to section 112 of the Clean Air Act, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
including: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Any pollutant listed pursuant to section 112(r) of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Clean Air Act (Prevention of Accidental Releases), which shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered a ``regulated air pollutant'' upon promulgation of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
list. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any hazardous air pollutant subject to a standard or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other requirement promulgated by the EPA pursuant to section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
112(d) or adopted by the district pursuant to 112(g) and (j) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Clean Air Act which shall be considered a ``regulated air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollutant'' for all sources or categories of sources upon 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
promulgation of the standard or requirement or 18 months after 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the standard or requirement was scheduled to be promulgated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to section 112(e)(3) of the Clean Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Any HAP subject to a district case-by-case emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitation determination for a new or modified source, prior to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA promulgation or scheduled promulgation of an emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitation, which shall be considered a ``regulated air pollutant'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
when the determination is made pursuant to section 112(g)(2) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the Clean Air Act. In case-by-case emissions limitation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determinations, the HAP shall be considered a ``regulated air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollutant'' only for the individual source for which the emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitation determination was made. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Replacement equipment
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Routine replacement
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
: The replacement or modification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of emission units(s) where the replacement unit(s) serves the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
identical function as the unit(s) being replaced, and the maximum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rating and the potential to emit any pollutant will not be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
greater from the new or modified emissions unit(s) than the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replaced unit(s), when the emissions unit(s) is operated at the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
same permitted conditions. The EPA will determine, on a case-by-case basis, whether a project to replace an emissions
unit in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whole or part with functionally equivalent equipment is a routine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
repair, commonly made in the industry. Projects intended to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extend the expected useful life of the unit may not be considered 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
routine replacements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Identical replacement
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
: The total or partial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replacement of an emissions unit where the replacement is the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
same as the original unit in all respects except for serial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
number. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Responsible official
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means an individual with the authority 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to certify that a source complies with all applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements, including the conditions of permits issued to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sources. A ``responsible official'' means one of the following: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) For a corporation, a president, secretary, treasurer, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or vice-president of the corporation in charge of a principal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
business function, or any other person who performs similar 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
policy or decisionmaking functions for the corporation, or a duly 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authorized representative of such person if the representative is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
responsible for the overall operation of one or more 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
manufacturing, production, or operating facilities applying for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or subject to a permit and either: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The facilities employ more than 250 persons or have 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gross annual sales or expenditures exceeding $25 million (in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
second quarter 1980 dollars); or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The delegation of authority to such representative is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved in advance by the EPA; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) For a partnership or sole proprietorship, a general 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
partner or the proprietor, respectively; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) For a municipality, state, federal, or other public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agency, either a principal executive officer or a ranking elected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
official; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) For an acid rain unit subject to Title IV (Acid 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Deposition Control) of the Clean Air Act, the ``responsible 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
official'' is the designated representative of that unit for any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
purposes under Title IV. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Sacramento Valley air basin
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means that portion of Placer 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
County which lies west of Range 9 east, Mount Diablo Base and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Meridian (M.D.B. &amp; M.), as established pursuant to section 39606 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the Health &amp; Safety Code of the State of California and as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
described in title 17, California Code of Regulations, &sect;60106(k). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Shutdown
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the earlier of either the permanent cessation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of emissions from a source or an emission unit or the surrender 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of that unit's or source's operating permit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00494 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Startup
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means the setting in operation of a stationary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source or emission unit for any purpose. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Stationary source (source or facility)
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means any building, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
structure, facility, or emissions unit which emits or may emit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any regulated pollutant directly or as fugitive emissions. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The terms ``building,'' ``structure,'' ``facility,'' or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
``emissions unit'' include all pollutant-emitting activities which: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Belong to the same industrial grouping; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Are located on one property or on two or more 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contiguous properties; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Are under the same or common ownership, operation, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control or which are owned or operated by entities which are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under common control. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Pollutant-emitting activities shall be considered as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
part of the same industrial grouping if: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) They belong to the same two-digit standard industrial 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
classification code under the system described in the 1987 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Standard Industrial Classification Manual; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) They are part of a common production process. (Common 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
production process includes industrial processes, manufacturing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
processes and any connected processes involving a common 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
material.) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) The emissions within district boundaries of cargo 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
carriers associated with the stationary source shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
considered emissions from the stationary source to the extent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that emission reductions from cargo carriers are proposed as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
offsets. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Surplus
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means emission reductions that are in excess of any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions reduction which is: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Required or encumbered by any laws, rules, regulations, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agreements, or orders; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) Attributed to a control measure noticed for workshop in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the district, or proposed or contained in a State Implementation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Plan or Federal Implementation Plan; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) Proposed or contained in a district air quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
attainment plan for attaining reductions required by the Clean 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Air Act. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Temporary source
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means emission sources such as pilot 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
plants, and portable facilities that will be terminated or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
located outside the district after less than a cumulative total 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of 90 days of operation in any 12 continuous months, and the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions resulting from the construction phase of a new source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Title V permits
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 means permits issued, denied, renewed, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
amended, or reopened pursuant to the Clean Air Act as amended in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
1990 (42 U.S.C. 7401 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
et seq
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
.), and 40 CFR part 70, ``State Operating Permit Programs.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Total reduced sulfur compounds 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
means the sulfur compounds 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hydrogen sulfide, methyl mercaptan, dimethyl sulfide and dimethyl 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
disulfide. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Authority to construct
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Any person building, erecting, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
altering or replacing any article, machine, equipment or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contrivance, the use of which may cause, eliminate, reduce, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control the issuance ROC or NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, shall obtain authorization for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
such construction from the EPA as specified in paragraph (e)(3) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of this section, prior to beginning actual construction. An 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authority to Construct shall remain in effect until it expires or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the application is cancelled. An Authority to Construct shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
expire no later than two years following the date of permit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
issuance, unless the applicant has commenced construction prior 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to that date. If the applicant has commenced construction, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authority to Construct shall remain in effect for the life of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit(s), unless the EPA has taken action to modify or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
revoke it. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) An Authority to Construct shall be valid beyond two 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years if: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Commencement of construction has occurred; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Construction is completed in a reasonable period of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
time, as determined by the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) If a written request to extend the Authority to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Construct is received by the EPA prior to the expiration of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authority to Construct, an extension may be granted for up to two 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
years at the discretion of the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The EPA shall be notified of the anticipated date of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
initial startup or operation of any permitted article, machine, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment or other contrivance. Such notice shall be made no less 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
than 30 days prior to the startup date. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The EPA shall be notified of the actual date of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
initial startup within five days after such date. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards for granting applications
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The EPA shall deny an Authority to Construct except as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provided in &sect;52.3001, New Source Review, if the applicant does 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
not show that every article, machine, equipment or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contrivance, the use of which may cause, eliminate, reduce, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control the issuance of air contaminants, is so designed, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
controlled, equipped, and operated with such air pollution 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
control equipment that it may be shown to operate without 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emitting or without causing to be emitted air contaminants in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
violation of these rules and regulations or of such state or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
federal statutes as may be enforceable by the EPA on the date the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application is deemed complete. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The EPA shall require enforceable emission limitations 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as permit conditions in Authorities to Construct to assure 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with all analyses performed for the issuance of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permit, including the permanence of surplus actual emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions applied for use as internal reductions or authorized 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission reduction credits in accordance with &sect;52.3001, New 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Source Review, and &sect;52.3002, Emissions Reduction Credit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authorization. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Approval to construct shall not relieve any owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operator of the responsibility to comply fully with applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements, including applicable provisions of the California 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
State Implementation Plan or any applicable Federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Implementation Plan, district rules and regulations, or state or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
federal law. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Provision of sampling and testing facilities
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. In 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
addition to the monitoring and testing required to comply with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
state or federal laws or regulations, the EPA may, upon 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable written notice or before an Authority to Construct is 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
granted, require the applicant or the owner or operator of any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
article, machine, equipment, or other contrivance, the use of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which may cause the issuance of air contaminants, or the use of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which may eliminate, reduce, or control the issuance of air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contaminants to: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
