<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) Provide and maintain such facilities as are necessary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for sampling and testing purposes in order to secure information 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that will disclose the nature, extent, quantity or degree of air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contaminants discharged into the atmosphere from the equipment in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
question. In the event of such a requirement, the EPA shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
notify the applicant in writing of the required size, number and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location of sampling holes; the size and location of the sampling 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
platform; the access to the sampling platform; and the utilities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for operating the sampling, testing, and air monitoring 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
equipment. Such platform and access shall be constructed in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with the applicable General Industry Safety Orders of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the State of California. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Provide and maintain sampling and monitoring apparatus 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to measure emissions of air contaminants when the EPA has determined that such apparatus is available and should be
installed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Continuous emission monitoring systems at a minimum 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be installed when required, and to the performance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specifications required by &sect;52.3001. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) A violation of emission standards of these rules, as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shown by the stack-monitoring system, shall be reported by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owner or operator to the EPA within 96 hours, or such earlier 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
time as may be required by any permit issued pursuant to this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) In the event of a breakdown of monitoring equipment, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the owner or operator shall notify the EPA within 48 hours and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall initiate repairs. The owner or operator shall inform the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA of the intent to shutdown any monitoring equipment at least 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
24 hours prior to the event. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) If the EPA determines that technological or economic 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitations on the application of measurement methodology to a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
particular class of sources would make the imposition of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
numerical emission standard infeasible, the EPA may instead 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prescribe a design, operational, or equipment standard. In such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cases, the EPA may require the installation or modification of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
process monitoring devices such that the design characteristics 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or equipment will be properly maintained, or that the operational 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions will be properly performed, so as to continuously 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
achieve the assumed degree of control. To the extent applicable, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reporting requirements for process monitors shall be the same as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for continuous emission monitoring systems. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) A person operating or using a stack monitoring system 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall, upon written notice from the EPA, provide a summary of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the data obtained from such systems. This summary of the data 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be in the form and manner prescribed by the EPA. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
summary of data shall be available for public inspection at the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
office of the Air Pollution Control District. Records from the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
monitoring equipment shall be kept by the owner or operator for a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
period of five years, during which time they shall be available 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the EPA in such form as directed. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Transfer
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. An Authority to Construct shall not be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transferable, whether by operation of law or otherwise, either 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from one location to another, from one piece of equipment to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
another, or from one person to another. In the event any person 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contemplates or desires to make any such transfer as herein above 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
described, said person shall make an application for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authorization in accordance with paragraph (e)(3) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Performance testing
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. Within 60 days after achieving 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the maximum production rate or the maximum rate of emissions to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which the source is limited by enforceable conditions, but not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
later than 180 days after initial startup of such source, or as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
otherwise required by the EPA to determine continuous compliance 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with emission limitations or to confirm emission reductions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
claimed, the owner or operator of such source shall conduct 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performance test(s) in accordance with methods and under 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operating conditions as are approved by the EPA and furnish the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA a written report of the results of such performance test(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Such test(s) shall be at the expense of the owner or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operator. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Testing shall be conducted with the source(s) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions operating at maximum capacity or other rate conforming 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to the maximum rate of emissions to which the source(s) are 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limited by enforceable condition(s). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) The EPA may monitor such tests and may also conduct 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
performance tests. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The owner or operator of a source shall provide the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA 15 days prior notice of the performance test to afford the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA the opportunity to have an observer present. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The EPA may waive the requirement for performance tests 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
if the owner or operator of a source has demonstrated by other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
means to the EPA's satisfaction that the source is being operated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in compliance with all local, state and federal regulations which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
are part of the California State Implementation Plan or any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable Federal Implementation Plan. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
General
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The exemptions contained in this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall not apply to an otherwise exempt piece of equipment which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
is part of a process that requires a permit. An Authority to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Construct shall not be required for the equipment listed in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraphs (d)(2) to (11) of this section unless an emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
unit is: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Subject to New Source Performance Standards; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Subject to National Emission Standards for Hazardous 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Air Pollutants; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) An emissions unit or stationary source for which 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission reduction credits have been requested or granted in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accordance with &sect;52.3002, Emissions Reduction Credit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authorization; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Any emissions unit that, in combination with other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions units at the source, would cause the source to exceed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the offset trigger as specified in &sect;52.3001. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vehicles
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
