<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(i) Vehicles used to transport passengers or freight, but 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
not including any article, machine, equipment or other 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contrivance mounted on such a vehicle that would otherwise 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
require a permit under the provisions of this section and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;&sect;52.3001 and 52.3002. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Locomotives, airplanes and watercraft used to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
transport passengers or freight. This exemption shall not apply 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to equipment used for dredging of waterways or equipment used in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pile driving adjacent to or in waterways, nor to the emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
from watercraft while docked at a stationary source. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Combustion and heat transfer equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Internal combustion engines with a manufacturer's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
maximum continuous rating of 50 brake horsepower or less or gas 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
turbine engines with a maximum heat input rate of 3,000,000 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
British Thermal Units (Btu) per hour or less at ISO standard day 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
conditions (288 degrees Kelvin, 60% relative humidity, and 101.3 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
kilopascals pressure). The ratings of all engines or turbines 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
used in the same process will be accumulated to determine whether 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this exemption applies. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Any combustion equipment that has a maximum heat input 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of less than 1,000,000 Btu per hour (gross) and is equipped to be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
fired exclusively with purchased quality natural gas, liquefied 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
petroleum gas or any combination thereof. The ratings of all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
combustion equipment used in the same process will be accumulated 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to determine whether this exemption applies. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) Residential structures. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Equipment utilized exclusively 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in connection with any structure, when the structure is designed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for and used exclusively as a dwelling for not more than four 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
families. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Plastics and ceramics processing. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Ovens, kilns, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
furnaces fired by electricity used exclusively for the heating, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
curing, softening, or annealing of plastics or ceramics, and not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emitting more than 5 pounds of volatile organic compound (VOC) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions in any one day. These exemptions shall not apply to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ovens used for heating or curing of fiberglass reinforced 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
plastics. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Storage and transfer. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Tanks, reservoirs, vessels or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other containers and their associated dispensing, pumping and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compression systems used exclusively for the storage of: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Liquefied or compressed gases. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Unheated organic materials with an initial boiling 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
point of 150
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C (302
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;F) or greater, as determined by the testing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedure specified in paragraph (f)(1)(ii) of this section, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with an organic vapor pressure of 5 mm Hg (0.1 psia) or less at 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
20
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C, as determined by the testing procedure specified in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (f)(1)(iii) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Organic liquids with a vapor pressure of 77.5 mm Hg 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1.5 psia) or less at 20
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C, as determined by the testing 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
procedure specified in paragraph (f)(1)(iii) of this section, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
having a capacity of 23,000 liters (6,076 gallons or less). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Equipment used exclusively for the transfer of organic liquids 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with a vapor pressure of 77.5 mm Hg (1.5 psia) at 20
<!-- PJG 0017 degreeslatlong -->
&cir;C to or from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
storage. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Unheated solvent dispensing containers of 380 liters 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(100 gallons) capacity or less. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Surface coating and preparation. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Water solution for surface preparation, cleaning, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stripping, etching (other than chemical milling) or the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
electrolytic plating with electrolytic polishing of, or the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
electrolytic stripping of brass, bronze, cadmium, copper, iron, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lead, nickel, tin, zinc, and precious metals. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Surface coating operations using a combined total of 1 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gallon per day or less of coating material and solvent. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Unheated non-conveyorized solvent-rinsing containers 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or unheated non-conveyorized coating dip tanks of 380 liters (100 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
gallons) capacity or less. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(8) Food processing. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The following processing equipment 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for food or other human consumables and exhaust systems or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
collectors serving exclusively such equipment used in: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Eating establishments for the purpose of preparing food 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for human consumption. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Smokehouses in which the maximum horizontal inside 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cross-sectional area does not exceed 2 square meters (21.5 square 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
feet). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Mixers and blenders used in bakeries. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Confection cookers. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Grinding, blending or packaging tea, cocoa, spices, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
roasted coffee. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(9) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Laboratory equipment. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Laboratory equipment used 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
exclusively for chemical or physical analysis and bench-scale 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
tests, including associated vacuum-producing equipment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
