<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00497 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(10) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Repairs and maintenance. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Routine repairs or maintenance not involving changes to any equipment for which a permit has been granted under paragraph
(c)(1) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(11) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Other equipment. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Other equipment authorized for exemption by the EPA and which would emit less than 2 pounds in any 24-hour period of
any pollutants without the benefit of air pollution control devices.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Administrative requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Posting. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A person who has been granted a permit to operate any article, machine, equipment, or other contrivance described
in paragraph (c)(1) of this section shall maintain a legible copy of said permit on the premises of the subject equipment.
Other information, analysis, plans or specifications which disclose the nature, extent, quantity, or degree of
air contaminants which are or may be discharged from such source shall be readily available for inspection by the EPA.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Altering of permit. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
A person shall not willfully deface, alter, forge, counterfeit, or falsify an Authority to Construct any article,
machine, equipment, or other contrivance described in paragraph (c)(1) of this section. A permit amendment or revision
requested by the owner or operator, other than an administrative permit amendment or an amendment pursuant to paragraph
(c)(1) of this section, shall require the filing of an application. For an administrative permit amendment, a responsible
official may implement the change addressed in the written request immediately upon submittal of the request. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) After designating the permit revisions as an administrative permit amendment, the EPA may revise the permit without
providing notice to the public or any affected state. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The EPA shall provide a copy of the revised permit to the responsible official. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) While the EPA need not make a completeness determination on a written request, the EPA shall notify the responsible
official if it determines that the permit can not be revised as an administrative permit amendment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applications. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An application for an Authority to Construct, Permit to Operate, change of ownership, or an application for a permit
amendment, permit reopening, or revision shall be filed in the manner and form prescribed by the EPA, and shall give
all the information necessary to enable the EPA to make the determinations required by paragraph (c)(2) of this section
and &sect;52.3001, New Source Review. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) A responsible official representing the owner or operator shall certify the truth, accuracy and completeness
of application forms. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) When the information submitted with the application is insufficient for the EPA to make the determination required
by paragraph (c)(2) of this section, &sect;52.3001, and any other applicable rule, regulation, or order, a responsible
official shall supplement any complete application with additional information upon the written request of the
EPA within the time frame specified by the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) A responsible official shall promptly provide additional information in writing to the EPA upon discovery
of submittal of any inaccurate information as part of the application or as a supplement thereto, or of any additional
relevant facts previously omitted which are needed for accurate analysis of the application. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Intentional or negligent submittal of inaccurate information shall be reason for denial of an application.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) An application for an Authority to Construct, permit amendment or revision shall be accompanied by payment of
the application filing fee as determined by the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) An application for an Authority to Construct shall be accompanied by evidence of a sufficient number of authorized
emission reduction credits, to meet any offset obligation in accordance with &sect;52.3001, New Source Review.

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Action on applications. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The EPA shall notify the applicant in writing of its approval, conditional approval, suspension, or denial of the
application for an Authority to Construct. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) In the event said notification or notification of application completeness pursuant to &sect;52.3001, New Source
Review, is not received by the applicant within 30 days of the filing of the application, or within 30 days of providing
further information as required by paragraph (e)(3) of this section, the applicant may, at his or her option, deem
the application to construct denied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Service of said notification may be made in person or by mail, and such service may be proved by the written acknowledgement
of the person(s) served or affidavit of the person making the service. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00498 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Conditional approval. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The EPA may issue an Authority 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to Construct subject to conditions which will bring the operation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of any article, machine, equipment or other contrivance, the use 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of which may cause the issuance of air contaminants or the use of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which may eliminate or reduce or control the issuance of air 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
contaminants, within the standards of paragraph (c)(2) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. The conditions shall be specified in writing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Commencing work under such an Authority to Construct shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
deemed acceptance of all the conditions so specified. The EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall issue an Authority to Construct with revised conditions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
upon receipt of a new application, if the applicant demonstrates 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that the article, machine, equipment or other contrivance, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
use of which may cause the issuance of air contaminants, can 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operate under the revised conditions within the standards of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (c)(2) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Denial of application. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
In the event of a denial of an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authority to Construct, the EPA shall notify the applicant in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
writing of the reasons therefore. Service of this notification 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
may be made in person or by mail, and such service may be proved 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
by the written acknowledgement of the person(s) served or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
affidavit of the person making the service. The EPA shall not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
accept a further application unless the applicant has complied 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with the objections specified by the EPA as his or her reasons 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for denial of the Authority to Construct. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Disclosure. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The EPA, at any time, may require from an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicant, or holder of any permit provided for in these rules 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and regulations, such information, analyses, plans, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specifications which will disclose the nature, extent, quality, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or degree of air contaminants which are, or may be, discharged by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the source for which the permit was issued or applied. A 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
responsible official representing the owner or operator shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
certify the truth, accuracy and completeness of disclosures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Studies necessary to provide such information shall be completed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
at the expense of the owner or operator of the source for which a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permit was issued or applied. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(8) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Suspension. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The EPA may suspend a permit if a holder 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of such permit willfully fails and refuses to furnish 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information, analyses, plans, and specifications, within a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable time, as requested by the EPA pursuant to any law, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rule, regulation, agreement, or order enforceable by the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
The EPA shall serve notice, in writing, of such suspension and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the reasons therefore. Service of said notification may be made 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in person or by mail, and such service may be proved by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
written acknowledgement of the persons served or affidavit of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
person making the service. The permit shall be reinstated when 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA is furnished with all requested information, analyses, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
plans, and specifications. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(9) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Cancellation of application. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An Authority to Construct 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application may be cancelled by the EPA: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) At the request of the applicant; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) If additional information has been requested of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicant in accordance with paragraph (e)(3) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
without the subsequent submittal of information within a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reasonable time. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Monitoring and records. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Testing procedures. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) General requirements. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Except as otherwise specified in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the district rules and regulations, the State Implementation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Plan, any applicable Federal Implementation Plan, any Authority 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to Construct issued pursuant to this section, testing methods for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determining compliance with emission limits shall be: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The appropriate methods of 40 CFR part 50, appendix M, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Recommended Test Methods for State Implementation Plans; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Any appropriate method of 40 CFR part 60, appendix A, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Test Methods; or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) An alternative method following review and approval of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that method by the California Air Resources Board and EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Initial boiling point. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D&hyph;1078&hyph;86, ``Test Method 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for Distillation Range of Volatile Organic Liquids.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Vapor pressure. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
ASTM D&hyph;2879&hyph;86, ``Vapor 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Pressure-Temperature Relation and Initial Decomposition 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Temperature of Liquids by Isoteniscope.'' 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Monitoring. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
As applicable, each emission source 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
subject to the requirements of paragraph (c)(1) of this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall comply with the following monitoring requirements: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The requirements of 40 CFR part 51, appendix P, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Minimum Emission Monitoring Requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The applicable federal requirements for monitoring of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Title V of the Clean Air Act as amended (42 U.S.C. 7401 et seq
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
.) 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
 (3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Recordkeeping.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
