 In no case shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions from the new or modified stationary source prevent or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
interfere with the attainment or maintenance of any applicable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ambient air quality standard. The EPA may require the use of an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
air quality model to estimate the effects of a new or modified 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stationary source. The analysis shall estimate the effects of a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
new or modified stationary source, and verify that the new or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
modified stationary source will not prevent or interfere with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
attainment or maintenance of any ambient air quality standard. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
In making this determination, the EPA shall take into account the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
mitigation of emissions through offsets pursuant to this section 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and the impacts of transported pollutants on downwind pollutant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
concentrations. The EPA may impose, based on an air quality 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
analysis, offset ratios greater than the requirements of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (c)(3) of this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
