<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any Authority to Construct if the EPA finds that the subject of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the application would not comply with the standards set forth in 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
federal rules or regulations. Stationary sources and emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
units are required to curtail operations corresponding to the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
extent that required offsets are not obtained, or are not 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
permanently maintainable. The owner or operator of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stationary source or emissions unit requiring offsets has the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
ultimate responsibility for ensuring that offsets are real, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surplus, permanent, and quantifiable. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Alternative siting analysis.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 By means of an analysis 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of alternative sites, sizes, production processes, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
environmental control techniques for a new or modified stationary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source, the owner or operator of the proposed stationary source 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
or modification shall demonstrate to the satisfaction of the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that the benefits of the proposed source significantly outweigh 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the environmental and social costs incurred as a result of its 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
location, construction, or modification. Whenever any proposed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source or modification is subject to action by a state or federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
agency that might necessitate the preparation of an environmental 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
impact statement, which includes an alternative siting analysis, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA may accept the alternative sitings analysis prepared 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to that action to meet this requirement to the extent 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
appropriate. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Administrative requirements.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
administrative requirements shall apply to any activities 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
regulated by this section. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Complete application.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The EPA shall determine whether 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the application is complete no later than 30 days after receipt 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of the application, or after such longer time period that the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicant and the EPA have agreed to in writing. If the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determines that the application is not complete, the applicant 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be notified in writing of the decision specifying the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information required. Upon receipt of any re-submittal of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application, a new 30-day period to determine completeness shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
begin. Completeness of an application or a re-submitted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application shall be evaluated on the basis of the information 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements set forth in 40 CFR 70.5(c), Federal Operating 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Permit Program and the information required by this section. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA may, at any time during the processing of the application, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
request an applicant to clarify, amplify, correct, or otherwise 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
supplement the information submitted in the application. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Air quality models.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All air quality models used for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the purposes of this section shall be consistent with the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements provided in the most recent edition of the EPA's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
``Guidelines on Air Quality Models, OAQPS 1.2&hyph;080,'' unless the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
finds that such model is inappropriate for use. After making 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
such a finding, the EPA may designate an alternate model only 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
after allowing for public comment. Credit shall not be given for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
stacks higher than dictated by good engineering practice. All 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
modeling costs associated with the siting of a stationary source 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall be borne by the applicant. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Preliminary decision.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Except as provided in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b)(2) of this section, following acceptance of an application as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
complete, the EPA shall perform the evaluations required to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
determine compliance with all applicable requirements of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section and make a preliminary written decision as to whether an 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authority to Construct should be approved, conditionally 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
approved, or denied. The decision shall be supported by a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
succinct written analysis. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Publication, public comment, and requests for public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hearings.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Except as provided in paragraph (b)(2) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, within 10 calendar days following a preliminary decision 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pursuant to paragraph (c) of this section, the EPA shall publish, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
in at least one newspaper of general circulation in the district, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
a notice stating the preliminary decision of the EPA noting how 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the pertinent information can be obtained, and inviting written 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
public comment for a 30-day period following the date of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
publication. The notice shall also provide that any interested 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
person may submit a written request for a public hearing, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
that such request must include a statement of the issues proposed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to be raised in the hearing. If a written request for a public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hearing is received during the public comment period, the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall use the procedures given at 40 CFR 124.12, Public Hearings, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable to PSD permits, to grant or deny the request and to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
hold a public hearing. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00504 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Public inspection.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Except as provided in paragraph 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b)(2) of this section, the EPA shall make available for public 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
inspection, at the district's office and the Regional Office of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA, the information submitted by the applicant and the EPA's 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
analysis no later than the date the notice of the preliminary 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
decision is published pursuant to paragraph (d)(4) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section. Information submitted that contains trade secrets shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be handled in accordance with the requirements of 40 CFR part 2. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Authority to Construct, final action.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Except as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provided in paragraph (b)(2) of this section, the EPA shall 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
provide written notice of the final action to the applicant, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall make the notice and all supporting documents available for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
public inspection at the district's office and Regional Office of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the EPA. Within 30 days after the final decision has been made 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
on the authority to construct, the applicant or any person who 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
filed comments of the preliminary determination, may petition the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
EPA to review any condition of the permit. Any person who failed 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to file comments on the preliminary decision, may petition for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
administrative review only on the changes from the preliminary to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the final determination. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Requirements, authority to construct. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) General conditions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 As a condition for the issuance of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
an Authority to Construct, the EPA shall require that the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit and stationary source, and any emissions units 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
which provide offsets, be operated in the manner stated in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application in making the analysis required to determine 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
compliance with this section, and as conditioned in the Authority 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to Construct. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emissions limitations.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 All of the following emissions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitations shall be included in the Authority to Construct, if 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
applicable: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) The Authority to Construct shall include emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
limitations which reflect Best Available Control Technology. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Such condition(s) shall be expressed in a manner consistent with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
testing procedures, such as ppmv NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
, g/liter VOC, or lbs/hr. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) A quarterly emissions limitation for each affected 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollutant for which offsets are being provided pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (c)(2) of this section shall be contained in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Authority to Construct. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00505 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(C) A daily emission limitation shall be contained in the Authority to Construct when offsets are not being provided
pursuant to paragraph (c)(2) of this section, or when required to be consistent with ambient air quality standards.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Design, operational, or equipment standards. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
If the EPA determines that technological or economic limitations on the application of measurement methodology
to a particular class of sources would make the imposition of a numerical emission standard infeasible, the EPA may
instead prescribe a design, operational, or equipment standard. In such cases, the EPA shall make a best estimate
as to the emission rate that will be achieved. Any permits issued without an enforceable numerical emission standard
must contain enforceable conditions that assure that the design characteristics or equipment will be properly maintained,
or that the operational conditions will be properly performed, so as to continuously achieve the assumed degree of
control.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Offsets.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(A) Except as provided in paragraph (b) of this section, the operation of any emissions unit or stationary source which
provides offsets shall be subject to enforceable permit conditions, containing specific emissions and operational
limitations, to ensure that the emission reductions shall be provided in accordance with the provisions of this section
and shall continue for the reasonably expected life of the proposed emissions unit or stationary source.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(B) Where the source of offsets is not required to obtain an Authority to Construct pursuant to &sect;52.3000, General
Permit Requirements, and &sect;52.3002(c)(2), a legally binding contract shall be required between the applicant
and the owner or operator of such source. Such contract, by its terms, shall be enforceable by the EPA. For such non-permitted
sources, a source-specific SIP revision is required.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(C) An internal emission offset will be considered federally enforceable if it is made a SIP requirement by inclusion
as a condition of the authority to construct.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(D) External offsets must be made enforceable either by revision of an offsetting source's Authority to Construct
or by a SIP revision prior to the operation of the emissions unit.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(E) A violation of the emission limitation provisions of any contract pursuant to the above stipulations shall be
a violation of this section by the applicant.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(F) The operation of any emissions unit or stationary source which uses offsets provided by another emissions unit
or stationary source shall be subject to enforceable permit conditions, containing specific emissions and operational
limits, to ensure that the emission reductions are used in accordance with the provisions of all applicable rules
and shall continue for the reasonably expected life of the proposed emissions unit or stationary source.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(G) The permanence of emissions reductions may be demonstrated by federally enforceable changes in source permits
to reflect a reduced level of allowable emissions.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(8) Issuance, replacement unit. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Where a new or modified stationary source is, in whole or in part, a replacement for an existing stationary source on
the same property, the EPA may allow a maximum of 90 days as a startup period for simultaneous operation of the existing
stationary source and the new source or replacement.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(9) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Regulations in force. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
An Authority to Construct shall be granted or denied based on Best Available Control Technology requirements and
offset requirements of paragraphs (c)(1) and (c)(2) of this section in force on the date the application is deemed
complete as defined in &sect;52.3000(b). In addition, the EPA shall deny an Authority to Construct for any new stationary
source or modification, or any portion thereof, unless:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The new source or modification, or applicable portion thereof, complies with the provisions of this section and
all other applicable district rules and regulations; and
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The owner or operator of the proposed new or modified source has certified that all existing major stationary
sources owned or operated by such person (or by any entity controlling, controlled by, or under common control with
such person) in California which are subject to emission limitations are in compliance, or on an expeditious schedule
for compliance, with all applicable emission limitations and standards.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(10) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Calculation of emissions_BACT. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The emissions change for a new or modified emissions unit shall be calculated by subtracting historic actual emissions
from proposed emissions. Calculations shall be performed separately for each emissions unit for each calendar quarter.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00506 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(11) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Calculation of emissions_offsets trigger for ROC and NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The potential to emit for each calendar quarter for a stationary source shall be the sum of the potential to emit, including
fugitive emissions, for all emissions units based on current Authority to Construct permits, information contained
in current Permits to Operate, the pending application, and banked authorized emission reduction credits.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(12) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Calculation of emissions_offsets general. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The emissions change for a new or modified emissions unit shall be calculated by subtracting historic potential emissions
from proposed emissions. Calculations shall be performed separately for each pollutant and each emissions unit
for each calendar quarter. Negative emissions changes shall be processed under the procedures specified in &sect;52.3002,
Emissions Reduction Credit Authorization.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(13) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Calculation of emissions_offsets required for ROC and NO
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=5 f=2 -->
X
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
. The cumulative net emissions increase pursuant to paragraph (d)(12) of this section for a stationary source shall
be the sum of emissions from each of the following for each calendar quarter expressed in terms of pounds per quarter.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) The potential to emit including associated fugitive emissions not previously offset, for all emissions units
installed after September 21, 1993, based on current Authority to Construct permits, information contained in current
Permits to Operate, and the pending application.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) All emission increases, including associated fugitive emissions not previously offset, from the modification
to emissions units installed before September 21, 1993, as determined by procedures specified in paragraph (d)(12)
of this section. Any emissions increase represented by an Authority to Construct, which has been canceled by the EPA
or has expired, shall not be included in the cumulative emissions increase calculation.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Fees.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) The EPA will collect permit fees calculated in accordance with the fee requirements imposed in the district, not
to exceed the costs to EPA to issue permits and administer the permit program.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) If this section is delegated, the delegated agency will collect fees calculated in accordance with the fee requirements
imposed in the district. Upon delegation of any portion of this section, the EPA will cease to collect fees imposed
in conjunction with that portion.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(f) Monitoring and records. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
The following records shall be maintained for five years and shall be provided to the EPA upon request.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Emergency electrical generating equipment. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Records of operation for maintenance purposes, for actual interruptions of power.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Portable and temporary equipment. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Records of operating location and corresponding dates of operation.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=80 g=1 f=1 -->
&sect;52.3002 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=89 g=1 f=1 -->
Emissions reduction credit authorization (Sacramento).
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(a) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Purpose. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
To provide an administrative mechanism for authorizing surplus emission reductions for transfer to other sources
as offsets pursuant to &sect;52.3001, New Source Review. Actual emission reductions certified in a district bank
shall be reevaluated and authorized under the requirements and procedures specified in this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(b) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Applicability. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
This section shall apply to all emissions reduction credits which are to be used for offsets pursuant to &sect;52.3001,
New Source Review.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(c) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Standards.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Authorization. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
Only actual emission reductions shall become authorized ERCs. Such actual emission reductions shall meet the following
requirements to be authorized as ERCs:
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Be certified in accordance with a district banking rule except as provided in paragraph (c)(3) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Receive written approval of the EPA, as described in paragraph (e)(4) of this section.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) If the emission reduction is created from an emission unit where the demand for the services or product could
shift to other similar sources in the district, submittal of data to document that such reductions will result in district-wide
emission reductions may be required by the EPA. Such documentation must be approved by the EPA.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Emissions reductions shall be prescribed by enforceable emission limitations contained in Authority to Construct
permits.
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00507 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(2) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Non-permitted sources.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 If state or federal law 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prohibits the permitting authority from requiring an Authority to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Construct or a Permit to Operate pursuant to &sect;52.3000, General 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Permit Requirements, the applicant for authorized emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction credits shall execute a legally binding contract with 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
one or more owner(s) or operator(s) of the non-permittable 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emissions unit that ensures the sum of all emission reductions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
will be provided in accordance with the requirements of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, and will continue for the life of the stationary source 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
using the credits or life of the credits as provided in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
application. Such a contract shall be filed with the EPA and, by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
its terms, be enforceable by the EPA. In the absence of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
federally enforceable conditions, the execution of a source- 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
specific SIP revision is required. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Certification of ERCs in the absence of a district 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
banking rule.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 If the applicable district does not have a banking 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rule, the EPA will certify the ERC in accordance with EPA's most 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
recent emission trading policy. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(d) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Exemptions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Concurrent stationary source modification: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Concurrent reductions need not be authorized prior to use as 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
offsets, if those reductions satisfy all criteria established by 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
this section; &sect;52.3000, General Permit Requirements; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
&sect;52.3001, New Source Review. For the purposes of this exemption, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
``concurrent stationary source modification'' means the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
simultaneous modification of emission units and/or the addition 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of new emissions units to a stationary source with all emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions occurring after the issuance of the Authority to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Construct authorizing such reductions, but before the start of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
operation of the new or modified emissions unit(s) with emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
increases. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(e) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Administrative requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(1) Procedures for authorization of ERCs. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Any person or entity, or an authorized agent, applying 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
to use an ERC in accordance with &sect;52.3001, New Source Review, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
must submit a complete application for authorization of ERCs 60 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
days prior to submitting an Authority to Construct Application 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
under &sect;52.3001. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) The person or entity requesting ERC authorization 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall submit an application on forms approved by the EPA. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Except as provided in paragraph (c)(3) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, the application must include an engineering evaluation 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and verification of district certification of the ERC and any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
other information necessary to calculate the emission reductions 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
as described in paragraph (e)(2) of this section. Documents 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
submitted and received according to a district banking rule may 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
be sufficient for the application for authorization. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Applicants may claim confidentiality for submitted 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information to the extent allowed and provided for by Federal 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Regulation at 40 CFR part 2. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) To verify emission reductions claimed in conjunction 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
with an application for ERC authorization, the EPA may require 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
source tests by approved methods, continuous monitoring, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
production records, fuel use records, or any other appropriate 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
means. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(2) General calculation of emission reductions.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following procedures apply to the calculation of ERCs for all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
sources: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Actual emission reductions from modifications to, or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shutdowns of, existing emissions units shall be calculated for 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
each calendar quarter by subtracting the proposed emissions from 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
historical actual emissions. Any positive value shall qualify 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
for conversion to an emission reduction credit. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Credits shall be quantified in terms of pounds of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
pollutants per quarter for each calendar quarter. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) In addition to the criteria explained in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
definition of Actual Emission Reductions above, actual emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions shall be adjusted to at least reflect those emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
rates achievable with reasonably available control technology 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(RACT), or best available retrofit control technology (BARCT), or 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
any requirement of federal or state implementation plan rules, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
whichever results in the greatest adjustment. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) The EPA may adjust the credits to maintain any 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
discounting by the district prior to district certification of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the ERCs. Such discounting includes adjustments made by the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
district for deposit into a district priority reserve bank and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions claimed by the district to meet any federal planning 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
requirements. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The original ERC Certificate should be surrendered 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
prior to authorization of an ERC. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



<DOC>
<DOCNO> FR940505-1-00508 </DOCNO>
<PARENT> FR940505-1-00012 </PARENT>
<TEXT>
 
<!-- PJG STAG 4702 -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
(3) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Notification.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 Following the authorization of emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reduction credits, the EPA shall issue a Authorization 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Certificate to the owner(s) by certified mail or in person. The 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authorization certificate shall contain the following 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
information: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) Authorization Certificate number; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Date of authorization which expires pursuant to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
paragraph (e)(6) of this section; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Street address and Application Number of the site 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
creating the surplus emissions reductions for which the ERC 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Certificate is issued; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Signature of the responsible EPA official; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) The name of the owner, typed on the certificate, and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the owner's signature. If the owner is a public or private 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
business entity, a person authorized to sign on behalf of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
owner shall sign the certificate; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) The life of the credit specifying the date and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
duration (and time of year, for seasonal emissions reductions) of 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the expected reduction; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vii) Conditions of operation or use, including 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
restrictions on the use of the reductions (e.g., on site only, 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
replacement equipment only, seasonal equipment only, etc.), and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
current rules which affect the value of the ERCs; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(viii) The mechanism by which the credit was created (e.g., 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shutdown, installation of Flue Gas Recirculation system, 1D/3D 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
cyclone, etc.). 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(4) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Registration.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 When an Authority to Construct permit 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
using authorized emission reduction credits has been issued, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
following information shall be entered in the register: 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(i) All information required in paragraph (e)(3) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section except the information in paragraph (e)(3)(v) of this 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
section, which can not be entered into the register; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(ii) Date that the Authorized ERC Certificate was 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
surrendered to the EPA; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iii) Permit numbers to which ERCs are being applied; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(iv) Name and address of ERC user; 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(v) Name (if any), address, and application number of site 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
where ERCs are being used as offsets; and 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(vi) Number of ERCs being used for offsets. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(5) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Public inspection.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 The information entered in the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
register pursuant to paragraph (e)(4) of this section shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
available for public inspection at the EPA Region IX office after 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
the date of use of authorized ERCs as offsets. In addition, all 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
such information shall be transmitted to the district, the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
California Air Resources Board, and (for trades proposed within 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
100 km of a Class I area, or for trades more than 100 km from a 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Class I area that might reasonably be anticipated to impact such 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
area) the appropriate Federal Land Manager. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(6) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Expiration of authorization. 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
If an Authority to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
Construct permit is not granted within one year of the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
authorization of an ERC, the ERC will lose its authorized status 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
and must reapply for authorization when a source again applies to 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
use the ERC. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
(7) 
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=3 -->
Moratorium.
<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG ITAG l=11 g=1 f=1 -->
 If the EPA determines that additional 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
emission reductions are necessary, a moratorium on authorizations 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
of ERCs may be imposed. Prior to imposing a moratorium, the EPA 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
shall provide notice to holders of ERCs and other interested 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
parties and a 30-day opportunity for public comment on the 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
proposed issuance of a moratorium. The moratorium shall be 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
lifted upon determination by the EPA that additional emission 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->
reductions are not necessary. 
<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG 0012 frnewline -->

<!-- PJG /ITAG -->

<!-- PJG /STAG -->
</TEXT>
</DOC>



